Druid Starter Quest (Night Harbor).content:
{{NeedsInfo}}
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = phicon.png
| width             = 100px
| caption           = Placeholder Image
|Start Zone         = [[Night Harbor]]
|Quest Giver        = [[Rolan Talmula]]
|Minimum Level      = 1
|Classes            = [[Druid]]
|Related NPCs       = [[Calaada]]; [[Aaliyah]]; [[Milham the Mad]]; [[Almina Weepingwind]];
|Related Items      = [[Bat Wing]]; [[Fire Beetle Eye]]; [[Shiny Pyrite Coin]];
|Quest Rewards      = (exp); [[Worn Circle Tunic]]; [[Blessed Fire Beetle Eye]]; [[Halfling-Made Boots]]; [[Dousing Rod of Scarce Rains]]
}}

== Walkthrough ==

=== Part 1 - Reagent Run - Req. Lvl 1 ===
{{QuestNote|Read [[Earth-Stained Note]]. As a new [[Druid]] character in [[Night Harbor]], you will start with one in your inventory.}}
<pre>
Greetings wanderer,

The Circle of Scarce Rains invites those in tune 
with nature to gather at our headquarters in 
Saltbreeze Park, located in the center of Night 
Harbor, below Highpoint Terrace and its Great 
guild Hall.

Kindly deliver this note to Rolan Talmula if you 
wish to learn more about our order.

To find your way, remember that our sun, Eth, 
shines its life-giving rays from the east to the west, 
while the ruthless waves of the Twilight Sea crash 
upon the desert sand to the south.

May the merciful Krivea watch over you. 
</pre>
{{QuestNote|Head to Saltbreeze Park in [[Night Harbor]]. The druid guild is the southern building inside of Saltbreeze Park.}}
{{QuestNote|Inside of the druid guild, seek out [[Rolan Talmula]]. Rolan tends to wander around between the entrance balcony and the first floor.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Earth-Stained Note]] to Rolan Talmula.}}
{{exp}}
{{Emote|Rolan Talmula squints at the note, then looks up to you with a warm smile.}} 
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|Ah, you must be the new initiate. Thank you for bringing this note to me. We shall begin your training at once.}}
{{Emote|Rolan Talmula sizes you up for a moment before handing you a tunic.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Worn Circle Tunic]] from Rolan Talmula.}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|As you may already know, one of our duties here at the Circle of Scarce Rains is to maintain the delicate balance we have created here at the gardens.}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|Nature is not static, it moves like a river. Our goal is not to dam the river, so to speak, but to make sure that we have a place next to it.}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|Your first task is to collect reagents for the senior members of the guild and learn about the balance of nature while you are at it. Take this sack, fill it with eight bat wings, then collect a fire beetle eye, and bring them back to me.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sack for Bat Wings]] from Rolan Talmula.}}
{{QuestNote|Head to either West Gate or North Gate and begin hunting [[A desert bat]] and [[a fire beetle]].}}
{{QuestInfo|You can also find [[a desert bat]] outside The Concourse of Souls and the Druid Guild in Saltbreeze Park.}}
{{QuestNote|You will need 8 x [[Bat Wing]] and 1 x [[Fire Beetle Eye]]. Killing bats should give you sufficient levels to solo a fire beetle for the eye.}}
{{QuestNote|Alternatively, you may find [[Bat Wing]] and rarely [[Fire Beetle Eye]] for sale on various cooking merchants across [[Night Harbor]], sold by other players.}}
{{QuestNote|Place 8 x [[Bat Wing]] in your [[Sack for Bat Wings]] and click Combine to create [[Sack of Bat Wings]]. The bat wings can be stacked for the combine.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Rolan Talmula]] and give him your [[Sack of Bat Wings]] along with a [[Fire Beetle Eye]].}}
{{QuestInfo|If you only hand in one item, you get some additional flavor text.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you only hand in the eye...}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|It looks like you have found the fire beetle eye, and a fine one at that! However, where is the bag of bat wings? You were tasked with gathering those as well, initiate.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from Rolan Talmula.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you only hand in the sack of bat wings...}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|Oh, you have the bat wings. Wonderful. Do you have the eye as well, or perhaps it is in your bag, and you forgot to give it to me?}}
{{Emote|Rolan Talmula smiles knowingly.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from Rolan Talmula.}}
{{QuestInfo|Hand Rolan both the fire beetle eye and sack of bat wings...}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Circle of Scarce Rains|+}}
{{Emote|Rolan Talmula clutches the bag in his gnarled fingers, counting out the bat wings.}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|...four pairs and the eye. Very good, you have done well.}}
{{Emote|Rolan Talmula nods approvingly.}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|We druids have a duty not just to life, but to death as well. You would do well not to be squeamish about bloodshed, it is part of the natural order.}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|Krivea teaches us that gratitude for all life is important. We should thank any creature that gives its life, from the tiny insect to the giant beast, whether plant or animal.}}
{{Emote|Rolan Talmula mutters an incantation over the fire beetle eye.}}
{{Emote|Rolan Talmula hands you the eye, along with a wooden token.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Blessed Fire Beetle Eye]] from Rolan Talmula.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Wooden Circle Token]] from Rolan Talmula.}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|I have blessed the eye. You, too, will learn this skill in time. Now, go and present the wooden token to Calaada.}}
{{Chat|say|Where is Calaada?}}
{{Chat|Rolan Talmula|Yes, of course. Calaada is on the top floor of the guild, overlooking Saltbreeze Park with her companion, Oakheart.}}

=== Part 2 - Offerings - Req. Lvl 5===

{{QuestNote|Head inside the Druid Guild. Inside, turn right, and at the balcony, turn left and walk up the three ramps. Turn left after climbing to the top of the ramp BEFORE the balcony and enter the room, taking a left, then another left with another ramp up. Exit this room to the balcony to find [[Calaada Acaciathorn]] at the end of the balcony.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you are not level 5 or higher when turning in the token...}}
{{Emote|Calaada Acaciathorn looks at the token, then back to you.}}
{{Chat|Calaada Acaciathorn|It would seem that you've been training, initiate, but this task requires someone a little more seasoned. Return to me when you're a little more experienced.}}
{{Emote|Calaada Acaciathorn returns the token with a warm smile.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you are level 5 or higher when turning in the token...}}
{{Emote|Calaada Acaciathorn turns over the token in her palm, inspecting it.}}
{{Chat|Calaada Acaciathorn|Well, it would seem that you've been training. Rolan told me about your work with the bats.}}
{{Chat|Calaada Acaciathorn|I'd like to formally welcome you to the Circle of Scarce Rains. Our order hasn't been welcoming new members for some time, but our council decided that hiding away in our guild hall wasn't the best way to enact Krivea's will.}}
{{Chat|Calaada Acaciathorn|The Circle has mostly kept to itself, but I don't believe we should stand idly by while people suffer. Nature encompasses all, and it would behoove us to serve our citizens, just as we cultivate nature.}}
{{Emote|Calaada Acaciathorn nods as she scratches a notch into the back of the token.}}
{{Chat|Calaada Acaciathorn|Take this to Aaliyah, she should have another task for you.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Notched Circle Token]] from Calaada Acaciathorn.}}
{{Chat|say|Tell me about the Circle of Scarce Rains.}}
{{Chat|Calaada Acaciathorn|The Circle of Scarce Rains has been an integral part of Night Harbor since its founding. It's our duty to bless the fields, so that even in this harsh place, life can flourish.}}
{{Chat|say|Tell me about Krivea.}}
{{Chat|Calaada Acaciathorn|The merciful Krivea is the patron goddess of the Circle of Scarce Rains. Please feel free to make an offering at the shrine in the lower level of the guild.}}
{{QuestNote|Head down one level and locate [[Aaliyah]].}}
{{QuestNote|Give Aaliyah the [[Notched Circle Token]].}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah excuses herself from the class as she takes the token.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Calaada must have sent you. Welcome to the Circle!}}
{{exp}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah claps her hands enthusiastically.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|We're beholden to this land and its people for many of our duties. Considering that you're not as seasoned as some of the druids here, a task befitting an initiate seems appropriate.}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah fumbles through her waist pouch.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Here. Head west, outside the city gates. You'll see a collection of wayshrines along the road toward the Shaded Dunes. Travelers often place candles in the shrines, along with offerings to the guardian spirits that reside within them. Collect the latter in the offering bag and bring them back to me.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Silken Offering Bag]] from Aaliyah.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Good luck initiate!}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah returns her attention to the class.}}
{{Chat|say|What are wayshrines?}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Wayshrines can be found all across Aethoril. Travelers often place candles in them, supposedly to appease the spirits who live inside.}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah chuckles to herself.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Those of us who tend the roads often collect the offerings from these shrines, not for any material benefit, mind you. There's a certain magic imbued in them that we offer to our goddess, Krivea.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Life on the road has a mysterious magic to it. I'm sure the Sojourners can attest to this.}}
{{Chat|say|Who are the Sojourners?}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|The Sojourners? They're nomads with strong ties to ancient tradition. They protect nature and the spirits of the land, similar to us druids.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Each Sojourner clan belongs to a frus, or Beast Lord, who presides over them as their patron spirit.}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah clasps her hands in front of her.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|I hope this information was helpful to you.}}
{{QuestNote|Head towards West Gate. Along the roadway leading out from West Gate, you will spot three shrines. They are rocks with a nook carved out and a candle lit within. You need to be standing in front of the shrine facing the candle when you /look}}
{{QuestNote|You will need to use "/look shrine" command on each of the 3 shrines followed by "/take offering" or "/take note". Afterwards, you will have 2 offerings and 1 note.}}
{{QuestInfo|While you are outside West Gate, be sure to kill [[A large rat]] for 1 x [[Raw Rat Meat]] for later in the quest. You can often find some for sale on [[a shifty gnome]] nearby as well.}}
{{QuestNote|Using MUD commands, begin investigating shrines.}}
{{QuestInfo|Shrine #1:}}
{{Chat|mud|/look shrine}}
{{Emote|A crude wayshrine sits along the path, meant to guide travelers at night and provide a place for wayward spirits to rest. Some offerings have been left in front of it.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take offerings}}
{{Emote|You gather up the various offerings.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Humble Offering]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Shrine #2:}}
{{Chat|mud|/look shrine}}
{{Emote|A crude wayshrine sits along the path, meant to guide travelers at night and provide a place for wayward spirits to rest. Some offerings have been left in front of it.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take offerings}}
{{Emote|You gather up the various offerings.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Meager Offering]].}}
{{QuestNote|Proceeding to the third shrine, you will note something abnormal...}}
{{QuestInfo|Shrine #3:}}
{{Chat|mud|/look shrine}}
{{Emote|A crude wayshrine sits along the path, meant to guide travelers at night and provide a place for wayward spirits to rest. Usually, offerings are left in front of it, but this time, there is only a small note.}}
{{QuestInfo|Be sure to use /take note for this shrine...}}
{{Chat|mud|/take note}}
{{Emote|You gingerly take the note from the shrine.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Crudely Written Note]].}}
{{QuestNote|Reading the note drops some clues as to its writer. Bearing a signature of "milham" and the mention of someone named Willy, enter West Gate and turn left.}}
{{QuestNote|Run past the West Bank and enter the Sojourner's Camp area of Night Harbor. Turn left and walk towards Wayfarers Hospice (Cleric / Paladin guild hall).}}
{{QuestNote|Before entering Wayfarers Hospice, turn right and follow the building until you find [[Milham the Mad]] and [[Willy]] located to the right of the guild hall.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Crudely Written Note]] to [[Milham the Mad]].}}
{{Chat|Milham the Mad|What's this...?}}
{{Emote|Milham the Mad looks over the paper before a gap-toothed smile spreads across his face.}}
{{Chat|Milham the Mad|So, one with a warm heart will help Milham? I have borrowed, yes, for Willy. Please, help! He's been bitten!}}
{{Chat|Milham the Mad|He won't eat his help! Maybe if you put it in his favorite meat... rat... like they do with the kings...?}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Willy's Medicine]] from Milham the Mad.}}
{{Chat|say|What is his favorite meat?}}
{{Chat|Milham the Mad|Meat... meat from the jackals won't do... must be rat, yes, his favorite is rat.}}
{{QuestNote|Place 1 x [[Raw Rat Meat]] inside [[Willy's Medicine]] and combine to create [[Willy's "Treat"]].}}
{{QuestInfo|If you forgot to obtain 1 x [[Raw Rat Meat]] before, you can hunt rats outside of West Gate, or buy one from [[a greedy halfling]] or [[a cook]] nearby.}}
'''WARNING! Be prepared for combat with buffs and full health before turning in [[Willy's "Treat"]]. You will need to run to a nearby zone line to avoid killing [[Willy]], as doing so will result in negative faction hits within the city.'''
{{QuestNote|When ready, give [[Willy's "Treat"]] to [[Willy]].}}
{{Emote|Willy sniffs your hand for a moment, its tail wagging lazily as it languorously reaches for the food, snatching it up in its mouth.}}
{{Emote|Willy suddenly starts convulsing, its mouth beginning to foam as it bares its teeth and attacks you!}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sample of Willy's Spittle]] from Willy.}}
{{QuestNote|Make a run for a zone line to drop agro from Willy.}}
{{QuestNote|Afterwards, return to [[Milham the Mad]] and give him [[Sample of Willy's Spittle]].}}
{{Chat|Milham the Mad|Willy! No! My sweet boy!}}
{{Emote|Milham the Mad buries his face in his sleeve, sobbing loudly.}}
{{Emote|Milham the Mad hiccups, his cheeks and nose red, before reaching a trembling hand into his robes and handing you the offerings.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Returned Offering]] from Milham the Mad.}}
{{Chat|Milham the Mad|Thank... thank you. I need an eternity alone now.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sample of Willy's Spittle]] from Milham the Mad.}}
{{QuestNote|Place the [[Humble Offering]], [[Meager Offering]], and [[Returned Offering]] inside the [[Silken Offering Bag]] and click Combine to create [[Bag of Circle Offerings]].}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Aaliyah]] at the druid guild in Saltbreeze Park.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand [[Aaliyah]] the [[Bag of Circle Offerings]] along with [[Sample of Willy's Spittle]].}}
{{QuestInfo|If you only hand in [[Bag of Circle Offerings]]...}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Ah, the offerings!}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah looks at you inquisitively.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Is something wrong? Did you find something else?}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from Aaliyah.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you only hand in [[Sample of Willy's Spittle]]...}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah looks at the vial with a puzzled expression.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Do you have the offerings as well?}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from Aaliyah.}}
{{QuestInfo|Handing in both [[Bag of Circle Offerings]] and [[Sample of Willy's Spittle]]...}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah takes the offerings with a nod, then squints at the vial.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Where did this come from?}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah swirls the vial in her hands.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|From a sick hound, here in the city? That's not good... the disease has already made its way here...}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Quickly, bring the vial to Almina. She's stationed in Sungreet Strand, at the druid rings. She'll know what to do.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sample of Willy's Spittle]] from Aaliyah.}}
{{Emote|Aaliyah pauses a moment before seemingly remembering something, then hurriedly thrusts a package into your hands.}}
{{Chat|Aaliyah|Tanna made you a new pair of boots for collecting the offerings. You can wear them on your journey to Sungreet Strand... Be careful out there.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Halfling-Made Boots]] from Aaliyah.}}
{{Faction|Circle of Scarce Rains|+}}
{{exp}}

=== Part 3 - Req. Lvl 15 ===
{{QuestInfo|This section needs further improvement, formatting, and any additional notes such as exp or faction hits and item links.}}

1) Travel to the druid rings in the south end of Sungreet Strands, same place as your level 16 teleport spell. (A bit after the quarry on your left, head right towards the coast to a copse of trees near a large boulder.)

'''Hand the Sample of Willy's Spittle to Almina''' (you are given Imbued Circle Coin)
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Almina Weepingwind looks over the bottle.</span>
: Almina Weepingwind says, "Another sick animal... and Aaliyah told you to come to me with this urgently? Hm, this is worrying indeed."
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Almina Weepingwind lets out a deep sigh.</span>
: Almina Weepingwind says, "This disease isn't natural, I'm afraid."
: Almina Weepingwind says, "We need to track the source of these horrific acts, or it could affect us all... and even reach the city!"
: Almina Weepingwind says, "Search for clues throughout the mountain ranges and near water sources."
: Almina Weepingwind says, "While you look, hold this coin in your palm.  It's imbued with a spell that makes it heat up when you're near a strong , tainted source."
: Almina Weepingwind says, "If you find anything, come back to me immediately."

2) Travel to the northwest in SGS to the cliff / ramp up. Follow it past the three towers and bridge towards the garrison / fort where the Pyrmos mercenaries are. Through the fort access the aqueducts (looks like tiny bridge for carrying water) and travel it to the end where two mercenaries stand guard.

: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">As you approach the Gateway to the aqueducts, the metal coin in your possession begins to heat up considerably! This must be what Almina wanted you to find.</span>
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#D6A100;">You receive Searing Circle Coin.</span>

* You may wish to Souldbind here as you will be back.

3) Head back to Almina and turn in the coin.

: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Almina Weepingwind takes the coin in hand and flinches slightly, conjuring a sphere of water to help cool down the imbued coin.</span>
: Almina Weepingwind says, "It appears that you have successfully tracked down the source of the disease, though I cannot begin to fathom how the aqueducts could have become tainted when they are so heavily guarded."
: Almina says, "Someone, or something, must be capable of slipping past the Pyrmos mercenaries unnoticed."
: Almina says, "We will also be barred access, as the governor has hired the Pyrmos to keep any of the local factions away from such an important piece of Night Harbor's power struggle."
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Almina Weepingwind chews her lower lip and then withdraws a sheaf of parchment, scribbling out a note and offering it back to you.</span>
: Almina says, "We will simply have to appeal to the morals of one of the mercenaries posted there. Did you encounter a guard posted at the aqueduct gates themselves?"
* /say Yes, I did.
: Almina says, "Good, then you already know who you can deliver my message to. You must stress to them just how urgent the situation is."
: Almina says, "With any luck, they may be able to point us in the direction of where we act next. Move swiftly with the speed of the wild!"

4) Head back to the same place, and at the end of the aqueducts two mercenaries stand guard, one named. The named is Foldja. Hand her the note and she will hand you back a note.

: Mercenary Foldja says, "Uh? What's this, then?"
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Mercenary Foldja unfolds the message and scans it quickly, frowning. She rolls up the parchment and returns it to you.</span>
: Mercenary Foldja says, "Sounds like your Almina friend already knows that I can't let you inside, but you're also lucky that you brought this to me instead of someone else."
: Mercenary Foldja says, "The Pyrmos would take offense to any notion that we're failing in our duties, but being stationed at the gateway means I've heard the things that crawl around in the night."

* /say things?

: Mercenary Foldja says, "There are eerie chants and cackles from the crags here at night. Very goblin-like cackles, if you get me."
: Mercenary Foldja says, "I can assure you that nothing gets through this gateway, but I wouldn't be surprised if those Muggrah scamps found a hidden passage on the other side of the mountain."
: Mercenary Foldja says, "The Bloodynose clan nearby are too scrawny and occupied with their war against the ashira clans, while the Muggrah camp just beyond our keep is always under our watchful eye, so I wouldn't be worried about that one."
: Mercenary Foldja says, "No, if I were a betting woman, I'd say that the goblins on the other side of the mountain in the Glass Flats were the ones scaling the cliffs and being a nuisance."
: Mercenary Foldja says, "You can go tell your Almina friend that I said as much."

5) Head back to Almina. Target here and /say goblins, earn your satchel, and prepare for Glass Flats goblins.

* /say goblins

: Almina Weepingwind says, "Goblins? What motivation would they have to infect the city's water supply? The goblin clans are typically drawn toward acts of greed, not sheer malice."
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Almina Weepingwind pauses to ponder for a moment before shaking her head and taking back the letter, handing you a leather satchel in its place.</span>
: Almina Weepingwind says, "That will have to be an investigation for another day, I suppose. If the goblin shamans truly are scaling the mountains and infecting the city's water with their magics, we'll need to create a remedy to counteract it."
: Almina Weepingwind says, "The Muggrah shamans and spiritualists derive their power from covetous forces that they link to their personal possessions. You will have to relieve the shamans of a number of these possessions, so that I can develop a counteragent to deliver back to Night Harbor."
: Almina Weepingwind says, "Take this satchel and do what you must to fill it with the shaman's trinkets. I am not sure what they currently use, be it beads, fetishes, or some other token, but you must fill the satchel all the same."
: Almina Weepingwind says, "Return the filled satchel to me as soon as you can!"

6) Head to Glass Flats and kill goblin shamans and spiritualists.

* You will want to be level 16 or so and in a full group.
* From SGS, enter GF, turn immediately left, and look for goblin camps.
* You need to farm 6 [[Shiny Pyrite Coin]]
* Fill satchel with 6 coins and combine.
* Hand in to Almina.

: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Almina Weepingwind takes a look inside the satchel and raises her eyebrows.</span>
: Almina Weepingwind says, "Coins? I suppose I should not be surprised, given the goblins' beliefs."
: Almina Weepingwind says, "You did well, <player>. Allow me a moment to confer with the spirits on how to best counter this form of magical disease."
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Almina Weepingwind closes her eyes as a rush of wind and sand sweeps through the circle of standing stones. Your own connection to natural forces allows you to perceived the faint whispers of Szuur conversing with the skilled druidess, who then suffuses her power into a conjured sphere of floating water and douses the satchel of coins.</span>
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Almina Weepingwind continues to concentrate as the cloying sickness that once permeated the satchel begins to abate. Almina nodes and deposits what remains of her conjured sphere into an open flask, then offers it to you.</span>
: Almina Weepingwind says, "Bring this back to Aaliyah so she can treat the waters flowing in from the aqueducts. This is only a temporary solution, but it should at least be sufficient in preventing any further spread of the disease into Night Harbor."
: Almina Weepingwind says, "Thank you, <player>, and may Krivea guide your journey."

* You will receive Almina's Remedy. Take this back to Aaliyah.

: Aaliyah says, "You're back! What did I tell you? I knew Almina would know what to do!"
: Aaliyah says, "I'll see that this remedy gets delivered straight to the aqueduct's tenders. How bizarre that the goblin clans were involved in all of this."
: Aaliyah says, "We may have to look further into that another day, but for now, you're due for a reward for all your efforts."
: Aaliyah says, "Take this token to Calaada just above. I believe she wants to have a word with you."

* Head on up to Calaada and hand in the token.

: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Calaada Acaciathorn accepts the token with a warm smile.</span>
: Calaada Acaciathorn says, "I'm told you went to great lengths to seek out what was plaguing our water supplies, <player>."
: Calaada Acaciathorn says, "I'm both thankful and honored to have you as a member of the Circle of Scarce Rains. Please, accept this dousing rod so you may continue to bring fresh waters to all those who require it."
: Calaada Acaciathorn says, "In the future we may call upon your services once more, but until then, you're free to set out on whichever journey Krivea has laid out for you."
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Calaada Acaciathorn presents you a magical dousing rod.</span>



