Bones of the Ancestor.content:
{{NeedsInfo}}
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = Bones_of_the_ancestor.png
| width             = 300px
| caption           = 
|Start Zone         = [[Sungreet Strand]]
|Quest Giver        = [[Bree Weatherstoll]]
|Minimum Level      = 1
|Classes            = All
|Related NPCs       = 
|Quest Rewards      =
}}

== Walkthrough ==

{{QuestNote|[[Bree Weatherstoll]] is located in the halfling camp west of the quarry in [[Sungreet Strand]].}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Bree Weatherstoll.}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|Hi there youngling. You seem to have wandered away from home.}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|Stay with us a while if you like, eat some potato stew with blessings from the Warrenmother. Fayma provides for all of her children.}}
{{Emote|Bree Weatherstoll smiles at you warmly.}}
{{Chat|say|Who is the Warrenmother?}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|Fayma Warrenmother? She's an old soul. For many generations Fayma has watched over and provided for her younglings.}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|She's even watching over us now.}}
{{Chat|say|What is a youngling?}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|Please take no offense by it. Fayma sees all the races of the world as her younglings.}}
{{QuestInfo|There is some missing dialogue here...}}
{{QuestNote|In the middle of the camp a pot with cooking stew can be found.}}
{{QuestNote|Using MUD commands, you can learn a bit more detail about the camp...}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|Here, a small gathering of halflings scurries about the camp with excited energy.}}
{{Emote|The outer edge is lined with colorful tents, and crates and boxes are scattered haphazardly between them.}}
{{Emote|From the center of the camp, the savory aroma of stew wafts up from two cast iron pots over the fire.}}
{{Emote|Toward the eastern wall, a partially dug alcove catches your eye. Within the shadowed recesses, something ivory gleams faintly.}}
{{QuestNote|You can also take some Stew as suggested by [[Bree Weatherstoll]] earlier in your conversation with her.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take stew}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Halin Hearty Stew]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Any further emotes here?}}
{{QuestNote|The halfling bones discovered by the passing farmer that Bree mentions are in an alcove nearby.}}
{{QuestNote|You can again /look at the bones to learn more about them.}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|In the partially dug alcove, the faint glow of torchligh reveals the skeletal remains of an ancient halfling, their fragile bones cradled by the desert sand.}}
{{Emote|The skull, smaller, rounder and pronounced brow ridge, bear the markings of an ancient halfling, its jaw slightly agape as if in silent protest against time.}}
{{Emote|It seems to gaze longingly towards the pot of stew bubbling in the camp, as though the desire for one last meal lingers even in the afterlife.}}
{{Emote|The ribcage, partially buried, jugs out like the curved petals of a withered flower.}}
{{QuestNote|You can pour the [[Halin Hearty Stew]] on the skeleton with MUD commands.}}
{{QuestNote|Pick up the [[Halin Hearty Stew]] so it is on your cursor, and then type:}}
{{Chat|mud|/pour stew}}
{{Emote|You pour the hearty stew onto the drooping jawbone of the halfling skeleton. It runs through the bones and drips onto the ground.}}
{{Emote|The stew is wasted, but you feel mildly satisfied with yourself.}}
{{QuestInfo|Unclear if there is any further dialogue here...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect skeleton }}
{{Emote|You inspect the remains closely. The skill appears smaller and rounder, with a more pronounced brow ridge than that of a modern halfling.}}
{{Emote|Its jaw hangs slightly agape, as if on silent protest against time, while the ribcage, partially buried, juts out like the curved petals of a withered flower.}}
{{Emote|A faint aura of mystery and reverence hangs in the air, as though the desert itself refuses to release its memory.}}
{{QuestNote|At some point during the night, [[Bree Weatherstoll]] wanders over to the halfling remains and mentions something about ruins.}}
{{QuestInfo|Missing dialogue.}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|Look here. See the pronounced brow? I wonder how long our ancestor's hair was. Did it grow over their eyes too? Hmm...}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|The research we do here will fill may gaps in our history. Soon, we'll go into the ruins. The answers we seek will be there. They have to be.}}
{{Chat|say|Research?}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|We halflings have long sought out the ancient home of our people. It's our greatest hope that the desert of Szuur may have some answers.}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|Recently, a passing farmer took shelter from a storm here and came across these ancient halfling bones.}}
{{QuestInfo|Unclear if there is further dialogue here.}}
{{Chat|say|What ruins?}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|To the north, there is a quarry.}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|West of the quarry is a winding path that leads up the ruins of [[Tel Ekir]].}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|It's been long suspected to have once been home to Halin people.  We intend to go there soon.}}
{{Emote|Bree Weatherstoll looks at you sternly, her eyes unmoving.}}
{{Chat|Bree Weatherstoll|If you go there and happen to find any artifacts of halfling make, please bring it to me.}}

{{QuestInfo|More information is required...}}

{{QuestInfo|It is possible there are undiscovered /mud command responses inside of [[Tel Ekir]] which further the progress of this storyline.}}

{{QuestInfo|Additionally, there are known factions that can be gained within [[Tel Ekir]] which unlock further dialogue with various NPCs within the zone and may be key to continuing this storyline.}}

