}}

* Faction gained with [[Penitent Knights of the Hospice]]

{{QuestInfo|This quest is repeatable.}}

== Walkthrough ==

{{QuestNote|Squire Ryland is located inside of the Wayfarers Hospice in [[Night Harbor]] near the Paladin class trainers. Enter Wayfarers Hospice and take the first door on the right, then turn right.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Squire Ryland.}}
{{Chat|Squire Ryland|Hello there. Have you come seeking salvation?}}
{{Chat|say|I have come seeking salvation.}}
{{Chat|Squire Ryland|Very well, stranger. If you're looking to prove yourself, I have a simple task for you. That is, unless you're too experienced.}}
{{Chat|say|What is your task?}}
{{Chat|Squire Ryland|Excellent. We can always use some help cleaning up the weaker undead that roam the gates. They lack aggression during the day, but at night, they attack unsuspecting travelers.}}
{{Chat|Squire Ryland|We can't risk them being used in a more sinister plot. Bring me any of their bone chips so that we may destroy their haunted remains.}}
{{QuestNote|Kill skeleton mobs which drop [[Bone Chips]]. You will need sets of 5 x [[Bone Chips]] for each turn-in.}}
{{QuestNote|Give 5 [[Bone Chips]] to [[Squire Ryland]].}}
{{Chat|Squire Ryland|Thank you for purging the land of another undead menace. I'll dispose of these remains.}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Penitent Knights of the Hospice|+}}
{{QuestNote|If you hand less than 5 Bone Chips...}}
{{Chat|Squire Ryland|While noble of you, I've requested that you turn over at least five bone chips so that I can see to their proper disposal.}}
{{QuestInfo|Note: There may be a follow-up quest with [[Sir Leon Kardek]] or [[Sir Allan Fortir]] - more information is required.}}
{{Chat|say|I am too experienced.}}
{{Chat|Squire Ryland|Too experienced, eh? Then you should speak with Sir Allan or Sir Leon. These brave paladins not only saved my life, but they are great and holy men.}}
{{QuestInfo|Perhaps a certain faction standing with the Penitent Knights of the Hospice is required?}}

