{{Chat|Captain Keyaryn Thornshade|I wish I could tell you more. [[Scout Amberward]] has eyes on the ruins and made the report.}}
{{Chat|Captain Keyaryn Thornshade|On your way there, you could stop by and ask him about the robed figure. If they're the ones responsible for raising the undead, then you have my full permission to pursue and eliminate them.}}
{{Chat|Captain Keyaryn Thornshade|Bring back ten piles of ash and I'll be happy. Bring me the ash along with evidence of this robed figure's involvement and I might just kiss you.}}
{{Chat|Captain Keyaryn Thornshade|Again... figuratively speaking. No offense. Just get out there, scout, and make me proud.}}
{{QuestNote|You can take a quick detour and chat with [[Scout Amberward]] for some further details about [[a dark-robed figure]].}}
{{Chat|say|What can you tell me about the robed figure?}}
{{Chat|Scout Amberward|Good to see you again, <player>. You're investigating the robed figure I mentioned in my report? I'm glad they sent someone competent to look into things.}}
{{Chat|Scout Amberward|I'll tell you all that I know so far. I'm not certain if this figure is involved in the raising of the undead, but they only seem to arrive under the cover of nightfall.}}
{{Chat|Scout Amberward|They don't have the build of an orc, so I'm not convinced that it's one of their kind.}}
{{Chat|Scout Amberward|I've never spotted the figure entering or leaving the area, so they can either employ invisibility magic or have some other means of blending in with the undead in the area.}}
{{Chat|Scout Amberward|Unfortunately, that's all I have to offer you. If you do find any evidence of this figure's involvement, be sure to bring it to the captain.}}
{{Chat|Scout Amberward|Good hunting, scout.}}
{{QuestNote|The Calafreyan ruins are located south of [[Scout Amberward]]. Follow the two bridges to the south. On the last bridge before you enter the ruins, you will be able to use your [[Blessing of the Forest Spirits]].}}
{{QuestNote|[[Blessing of the Forest Spirits]], when clicked near the Calafreyan ruins, will give your player a buff which gives auto attacks a chance to proc holy damage which only works inside the ruins of old Calafrey.}}
{{QuestNote|The captain will ask you to venture to the ruins and collect 10 [[Necrotic Ash]] as well as proof of a mysterious robed figure's involvement.}}
{{QuestNote|[[Necrotic Ash]] is dropped by Calafreyan humanoids in the ruins, such as [[a Calafreyan archer]], if your character has the buff provided by the [[Blessing of the Forest Spirits]] applied when the mob is killed.}}
{{QuestNote|Once you collect the ash you need to head into the ruins in the evening to find the robed figure. (see video link at bottom of page).}}
{{QuestNote|In the back of the ruins, your character will spot something via an emote text in chat.}}
{{Emote|Your keen gaze spots a mysterious sigil etched onto a stone in a small clearing of leaves and pine needles.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect sigil}}
{{Emote|The sigil looks strangely familiar to you, and as you move closer to examine it, a robed figure appears from out of the shadows!}}
{{Chat|[[a dark-robed figure]]|Keep your filthy hands away from my work!}}
{{Chat|a dark-robed figure|You will interfere with my plans no longer}}
{{QuestNote|This step is virtually impossible solo at 8 so make sure you take a group with you. Estimates put these quest mobs around 13-18 with the robed figured not determined.}}
{{QuestInfo|Decent video walkthrough:}}
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RugZB-PbB7k
{{QuestNote|Upon death of [[a dark-robed figure]]..}}
{{Chat|a dark-robed figure|[[House Varros]] will be your undoing ... foolish kin...}}
{{QuestNote|Loot [[Letter of Correspondence]] and [[Dark Hood]] from [[a dark-robed figure]].}}
{{QuestNote|Hand [[Blessing of the Forest Spirits]], 10 x [[Necrotic Ash]] (can be in a single stack of 10) and 1 x [[Letter of Correspondence]] to [[Captain Keyaryn Thornshade]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Faction|Wyrdguard|+}}
{{Emote|Captain Keyaryn Thornshade takes a moment to go over the letter, his eyes narrowing.}}
{{Chat|Captain Keyaryn Thornshade|Impressive work, <player>. You've not only brought down the threat of the undead, but uncovered a plot to keep them raised, as well.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Scout's Longbow of the Wyrdguard]] from Captain Keyaryn Thornshade.}}

