[[Obsidian Shackle]]
}}

{{QuestInfo|This quest is the prelude for access to the city via the various [[Ail'Vorith Class Quests]].}}

__TOC__

== Walkthrough ==
=== Comprehension Test ===
{{QuestNote|Read the [[Imbued Parchment]] you start with as a new character in [[Ail'Vorith]]:}}

<pre>
You have been spared.

You only exist by the mercy of:

THE ETERNAL QUEEN AND HIGH LISTENER,
QUEEN NALIADRA
The Queen of Corruption, She Who Spoke With
the Shadow, the Immortal Consort of the
Darkness, and the Avatar of Barbhaal

Make no reference to your former house from this point forward, as *it never existed*.
Therefore, you have no privileged beyond the breath you breathe and your ability to *serve
our Queen*.

You have been cast out of Ail'vorith, welcome
only in its Foreign Quarter, as befitting one of 
the shadowless. Any attempt to enter further 
districts will result in your immediate 
extermination. You have been warned.

To prove yourself useful to our Queen and the 
Houses of Ail'vorith, seek the head toilmaster 
outside the city. Find him and present to him 
this writ if you wish to be tested for any worth 
left in you.

*You are now a shadowless nothing*. It is 
your decision as to whether you remain such.
</pre>

{{QuestNote|You are looking for [[Toilmaster Verith]] or [[Toilmistress Rallvessa]], who are mere feet away from where you spawn as a new character in Ail'Vorith.}}

{{QuestNote|Hand [[Toilmaster Verith]] or [[Toilmistress Rallvessa]] your [[Imbued Parchment]].}}

<tabber>
|-|Toilmaster Verith=
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|What's this, then?}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith looks over the writ and then turns to regard you with newfound disdain.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Yet another shadowless exile comes barking at my quarry for a morsel? Very well.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|I care not for your status so long as you're able to toil for me like any good meat should.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|First you'll have to prove to me that you're not completely blind, deaf or dumb.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|There are crates with pickaxes next to us, open those so-called eyes of yours and look for a pickaxe that isn't broken or damaged.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|You do at least know how to look, don't you?}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Once you find one that isn't damaged, take it. Then bring it here and show it to me.}}
|-|Toilmistress Rallvessa=
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|What do you want?}}
{{Emote|Toilmistress Rallvessa reads over the writ and then turns to regard you with newfound disdain.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|Yet another shadowless exile comes barking at my quarry for a morsel? Very well.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|I care not for your status so long as you're able to toil for me like any good meat should.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|First you'll have to prove to me that you're not completely blind, deaf or dumb.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|There are crates with pickaxes next to Toilmaster Verith, look for a pickaxe that isn't broken or damaged.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|You know how to give them a good look, don't you?}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|Once you find one that isn't damaged, bring it here and show it to me.}}
</tabber>

{{exp}}<br>

{{QuestNote|Using [[MUD Commands]], you will search the nearby crates for a [[Slave Pickaxe]].}}

<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" data-expandtext="If you choose to take a broken pickaxe...">
{{Chat|mud|/look crate}}
{{Emote|A haphazard heap of pickaxes reside within this crate, all of which appear to be broken or worn from use. The crate itself appear to be labeled with a placard that clearly states, "BROKEN".}}
{{Chat|mud|/take pickaxe}}
{{Emote|You take one of the worn pickaxes from the crate labeled "BROKEN". It does not look as though it could survive another strike against the stone.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Broken Slave Pickaxe]].}}
{{QuestNote|If you hand the [[Broken Slave Pickaxe]] to [[Toilmaster Verith]]...}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith scowls at you as he tosses the already broken pickaxe to the ground, shattering it completely.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Are you blind, or just incredibly stupid?! You need a pickaxe that is NOT broken or damaged if you're to do any toil for me!}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith proceeds to strike you with the back of his heavy gauntlet.}}

: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff0000;">Toilmaster Verith's Slam hits YOU for 2 points of damage!</span>
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Use your eyes, you useless thing! Take a pickaxe from the clearly labeled crate, if you only knew how to look!}}
</div>

{{Chat|mud|/look crate}}
{{Emote|This crate appears to be filled with recently repaired pickaxes, all of which are crude but serviceable. The crate itself is clearly labeled, "REPAIRED".}}
{{Chat|mud|/take pickaxe}}
{{Emote|You take one of the repaired pickaxes. It feels hefty in your grip, but should serve well for the tasks ahead.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Slave Pickaxe]].}} 
{{QuestNote|Hand the [[Slave Pickaxe]] to [[Toilmaster Verith]] or [[Toilmistress Rallvessa]]}}
<tabber>
|-|Toilmaster Verith=
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|So you're not actually that blind or stupid? How surprising.}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith tosses the pickaxe back to you.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|If you do have a brain, then I am sure you can guess what is required next of you, yes?}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|You will use that pickaxe to toil for me until you've hewed at least one full stack of stone from the old quarry. That is at least twenty rocks worth.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Return to me with what you gather alongside your pickaxe.}}
|-|Toilmistress Rallvessa=
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|So you're at least half capable.}}
{{Emote|Toilmistress Rallvessa tosses the pickaxe back to you.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|If you do have a brain, then I am sure you can guess what is required next of you, yes?}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|You will use that pickaxe and bring me a full stack of stone from the old quarry. At least twenty rocks worth.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|Return to me with the stones and your pickaxe.}}
</tabber>

=== Mining ===

{{QuestNote|Head south from the Toilmaster (the direction he's facing; away from the city) into the water and then right. Follow the wall until you find a small cave with several mining nodes. The nodes will respawn quickly (5-10 seconds) once mined. Place the [[Slave Pickaxe]] in your Main Hand slot and right-click the rocks to mine the [[Stone Ore]] veins until you have 20 [[Fragile Quarry Rock]].}}
{{QuestNote|Hand in a stack of 20 [[Fragile Quarry Rock]] and your [[Slave Pickaxe]].}}

<tabber>
|-|Toilmaster Verith=
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith proceeds to toss your pickaxe into the nearby crate labeled "BROKEN". He then deposits the rock you harvested into a neatly filled pack before heaving it to you without warning. You nearly lose your footing at the heft of the bag as it slams into your arms, weighing you down considerably.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Congratulations! You earned a trip to the foreign quarter.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Proceed towards the footbridge that leads into Ail'vorith.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|You're to deliver this pack of rock to Supplier Jul inside the supply shop. It's the building directly to your left as you enter the foreign quarter.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|He should have a delivery of sharpening stones that you will bring back here, to me.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Keep in mind that you are still worthless. You are not permitted to enter any other district of the city, or you'll be disposed of on sight.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|I don't rightly care what happens to you, but I do care about what happens if you lose my shipment, so just do as you're told.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Now go!}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Pack of Stone]] from Toilmaster Verith.}}
|-|Toilmistress Rallvessa=
{{Emote|Toilmistress Rallvessa deposits the rock you harvested into a neatly filled pack before heaving it to you without warning. You nearly lose your footing at the heft of the bag as it slams into your arms, weighing you down considerably.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|Congratulations! You earned a trip to the foreign quarter.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|Proceed towards the footbridge that leads into Ail'vorith.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|You're to deliver this pack of rock to [[Supplier Jul]] inside the supply shop. It's the building directly to your left as you enter the foreign quarter.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|He should have a delivery of sharpening stones that you will bring back to Toilmaster Verith across from me.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|Keep in mind that you are still worthless. You are not permitted to enter any other district of the city, or you'll be disposed of on sight.}}
{{Chat|Toilmistress Rallvessa|I don't rightly care what happens to you, but I do care about what happens if you lose my shipment, so just do as you're told.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Pack of Stone]] from Toilmistress Rallvessa.}}
</tabber>

<span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff0000;">You are encumbered.</span>

{{exp}}<br>

=== The Supplier ===

{{MessageBox
| class = warning
| img = Itemicon0001AA.png
| header = Change Language to Deep Common
| message = From this point forward in the quest, be sure you have set your language to Deep Common (right-click Main Chat window > Languages > Deep Common), or quest NPCs may not respond to your prompts.
}}

{{QuestNote|Carry the heavy pack of stone up the hill behind [[Toilmaster Verith]] and follow the verbal instructions given to you to find [[Supplier Jul]].}}
{{QuestNote|Hand [[Supplier Jul]] your [[Pack of Stone]]}}

<span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff0000;">You are no longer encumbered.</span>
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|Another supply from Vorith? Good. Set it down there, I'll get to it later.}}
{{Emote|Supplier Jul eyes you up and down a moment. He smiles broadly.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|As for his sharpening stones, I'm afraid he'll have to wait.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|The smith has been requisitioned by House Vael'xirith and hasn't felt the need to waste his time with petty stone work, you see.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|Unless you feel you're up to the task? You exiles are searching for a means to get back into standing with the Houses, are you not?}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|I'll throw in a good word for you to your master.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|The sharpening stones that Vorith needs are simple enough for a novice to make, and I'll provide you materials and directions to finish the work order.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|What do you say, will you do it?}}
{{Chat|say|I will do it.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|Wonderful! I don't want to have to deal with Vorith's complaints and you want to get on his good side, so this is a win-win situation for us both.}}
{{Emote|Supplier Jul produces a satchel and offers it to you, alongside a slip of parchment.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|Here's a satchel and the recipe to fashion sharpening stones. Take as much rock as you need from the pile next to me. You're going to want enough to craft five stones worth.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|Once you have the rock you need, take a left out of the shop and head through the gate to the foreign trader's market.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|At the end of the market you'll find a grinding stone next to the forge that you can use to turn these into proper sharpening stones. You'll need five of them to complete the work order.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|Place five sharpening stones in that satchel and then seal the container before returning it to me.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sharpening Stone Satchel]] from Supplier Jul.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Recipe: Fragile Sharpening Stone]] from Supplier Jul.}}
{{QuestNote|Right click the recipe to learn how to craft [[Fragile Sharpening Stone]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You have learned a new recipe!}}
{{QuestNote|Use your [[MUD Commands]] again to search the crate next to [[Supplier Jul]] and acquire some [[Fragile Quarry Rock]].}}
{{Chat|mud|/look crate}}
{{Emote|You notice a crate filled with rocks.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take rock}}
{{Emote|You take a handful of the fragile quarry rocks.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Fragile Quarry Rock]].}}
{{QuestNote|Repeat this until you have 5-8 [[Fragile Quarry Rock]], as you may fail a couple combines. There is a slight delay between MUD commands, so you may have to wait a few seconds between collecting each rock.}}

'''Since you skill up in [[Stone Cutting]] as you make the [[Fragile Sharpening Stone|Fragile Sharpening Stones]], feel free to collect extra rocks (trivial at 5).'''

=== Grinding the Stones ===

{{QuestNote|Once you have your rocks, take a left out of the shop and head through the gate. Proceed through the marketplace, turn right, and proceed through the tunnel. At the fork in the tunnel, take the right path. After exiting the tunnel, enter the first building on your right and turn right to find [[Blacksmith Zorvek]] and a small grinding wheel next to the forge.}}
{{QuestNote|Click on the grinding wheel and create 5 [[Fragile Sharpening Stone]]. Place the [[Fragile Sharpening Stone]] in your [[Sharpening Stone Satchel]] and click Combine to create a [[Full Sharpening Stone Satchel]].}}

<span style="font-weight:bold;color:#FF0000;">Sharpening Stone Satchel is consumed while crafting.</span>
{{ReceiveItem|You craft [[Full Sharpening Stone Satchel]].}}
{{QuestNote|Return the [[Full Sharpening Stone Satchel]] to [[Supplier Jul]].}}
{{Emote|Supplier Jul grins.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|That wasn't so bad, now was it? Granted you were working with quarry rock, and the most those can sharpen are the dull tools that Vorith has his slaves laboring with.}}
{{Emote|Supplier Jul writes out a receipt and includes it in the package before offering it back to you.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|There you are, one full delivery of sharpening stones for your master! I included a note inside about how you chipped in.}}
{{Chat|Supplier Jul|I'm sure Vorith will reward your efforts.}}
{{Emote|Supplier Jul smiles.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sharpening Stone Delivery Satchel]] from Supplier Jul.}}

{{exp}}<br>

=== Useless! ===

{{QuestNote|Return the [[Sharpening Stone Delivery Satchel]] to [[Toilmaster Verith]].}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith grunts dismissively as you return with the delivery.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|It's about time, exile. About the only thing the meat out here is good for is hewing rock, so a sharp pickaxe is essential.}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith opens the package and regards the note that was left by Supplier Jul. He scans the message quickly, his features soon hardening into a wicked scowl.}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith pulls out a stone that you recognize; a stone crafted by your own hand. He clenches it in his fist and the fragile stone crumbles immediately into dust.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|WHAT IS THIS?!}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|These stones are completely useless to me!}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|I had ordered hardened stones to be used on metal tools, not this worthless dreck!}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Jul's message says that YOU took it upon yourself to make these in his stead? Explain yourself, meat!}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Yes or no, did you make these stones?}}
{{Chat|say|Yes I made them|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Then you are either a fool or a subservient sap. Perhaps both.}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith narrows his eyes at you, his expression cooling.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Jul has undoubtedly kept my commission for himself so that he could profit from it and pass the blame on to a desperate exile like yourself.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|He was counting on me slaying you where you stand. Instead, I shall find out if there is yet a fire for vengeance burning in the embers of your lost soul, meat.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|This will also be a test of your ability. Are you prepared?}}
{{Chat|say|I am prepared!|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Good. You are to prove if you are proficient enough to survive the caverns of Ail'vorith.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Venture past the safety of these surroundings and murder the pathetic creatures you find there and fill this satchel with their remnants.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|I require two bone chips, two myconid caps and two deep beetle legs.}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith throws you a small leather satchel.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Small Leather Hunting Satchel]] from Toilmaster Verith.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Should you not survive, then good riddance. If you do manage it, return to me the filled satchel.}}

=== Finally, some killing! ===

{{QuestNote|Walk down the hill and begin hunting the newbie creatures for the required parts.}}

<ul>
<li>[[Bone Chips]] are dropped by [[a decayed skeleton]]</li>
<li>[[Deep Beetle Legs]] are dropped by [[a small beetle]] and [[a deep beetle]]</li>
<li>[[Damaged Fungus Cap]] are dropped by [[a cave sporeling]]</li>
</ul>

{{QuestNote|When you have all six items, place them in the [[Small Leather Hunting Satchel]] in single stacks and click Combine to create [[Filled Leather Hunting Satchel]].}}

<span style="font-weight:bold;color:#FF0000;">Small Leather Hunting Satchel is consumed while crafting.</span>
{{ReceiveItem|You create [[Filled Leather Hunting Satchel]].}}
{{QuestNote|Hand the [[Filled Leather Hunting Satchel]] to [[Toilmaster Verith]].}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith takes the satchel and inspects the contents, nodding with satisfaction.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|You yet live? Perhaps there is hope for you to serve after all. Most of the dregs who wash onto my shore are not even fit to cull a simple beetle.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|You also, for better or for worse, blindly follow instructions. Your subservience could be better suited to a House that would put it to use, but that is still to be determined.}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith produces a writ and adds it into the satchel before sealing it once more and offering it back to you.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Satchel of Questionable Spoils]] from [[Toilmaster Verith]].}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Bring your spoils to the cook, Vashuk, at the inn inside the foreign quarter.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|This time, do not ask or answer any questions. Simply make this delivery and then return to me when you are finished.}}

=== The Cook ===

{{QuestNote|[[Cook Vashuk]] is a questionable character, and as such is difficult to find.}}
{{QuestNote|Head inside the city by crossing the bridge behind [[Toilmaster Verith]]. Once inside the main gate, turn right and walk up the stairs into the first building on your left just past the courtyard fountain.}}
{{QuestNote|Once you climb up the stairs, enter the small doorway in the back-right of the inn and take the stairs DOWN.}}
{{QuestNote|In the far back of the cellar, you will find [[Cook Vashuk]]. Hand [[Cook Vashuk]] your [[Satchel of Questionable Spoils]].}}
{{Emote|Cook Vashuk lets out a cackle as he snatches the satchel from your hands.}}
{{Chat|Cook Vashuk|The scent of spores and death lingers on the exile before me!}}
{{Emote|Cook Vashuk eagerly looks through the satchel, clawing at the note that was left by Vorith. He scans it with a crazed stare.}}
{{Chat|Cook Vashuk|Ah, I see, I see! Yes, yes, indeed. So it shall be.}}
{{Chat|Cook Vashuk|Go now, shoo! Off with you, disgraced one! Go tell your master that it shall be as he wishes.}}
{{Emote|Cook Vashuk cackles delightfully as he begins chopping the components you brought atop a grisly wooden board.}}

{{exp}}<br>

=== A recommendation! ===

{{QuestNote|Return to [[Toilmaster Verith]] and hail him.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Toilmaster Verith.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|You return, Good.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Vashuk is rather mad in the head, you see. He often pays others for near worthless monster parts, but in this case he'll be making a special meal for Jul in particular.}}
{{Emote|Toilmaster Verith smirks before his stern gaze returns.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|You have proven to be at least marginally competent. Do you still wish to attempt to rejoin the Houses of Ail'vorith?}}
{{Chat|say|Yes|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Very well. Here is a recommendation stating that you are not, entirely, without use.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Vorith's Recommendation]] from [[Toilmaster Verith]].}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Bring this to Provost Xan'shorn within the Obsidian Academy. The entrance is the first one that you'll see when you cross the footbridge to enter for foreign quarter.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|He will direct you further towards your...reintegration.}}
{{Chat|Toilmaster Verith|Be mindful of the shadows this time, meat. Else I find you back in my quarry barking for scraps.}}

{{exp}}

=== The Houses ===

{{QuestNote|Head back across the bridge and through the gate. In the courtyard, [[Provost Xan'shorn]] is to the left in the courtyard as you pass through the gate. He likes to walk in small circles around the left side of the courtyard.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand [[Provost Xan'shorn]] [[Vorith's Recommendation]].}}
{{Emote|Provost Xan'shorn frowns as he looks over the letter of recommendation, eyeing you suspiciously.}}
{{Chat|Provost Xan'shorn|Not often does vorith send me a worthy exile. Perhaps you will be more promising?}}
{{Emote|Provost Xan'shorn produces a shackle-like bracer that he clasps onto one of your wrists.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Obsidian Shackle]] from [[Provost Xan'shorn]].}}
{{Chat|Provost Xan'shorn|I welcome you, shadowless, to the Obsidian Academy. We are willing to instruct those of lesser station who wish to prove their worth to our Queen through blood, blade, and sacrifice.}}
{{Chat|Provost Xan'shorn|There are seven great Houses of Ail'vorith: Vael'xirith, Varros, Xal'tharn, Hal'kareth, Ith'vayen, Drezzorith, and Velgarrith.}}
{{Chat|Provost Xan'shorn|Each House has a representative that you can find here in the academy. Speak to them. Find one that resonates with the darkness in your own soul.}}
{{Chat|Provost Xan'shorn|Learn what you can do to pledge yourself to them to regain your own shadow. Yet know that the Houses are not in alignment. Pledging with one will earn the scorn of others, so make your choice wisely.}}
{{QuestNote|Quest Complete!}}
{{QuestNote|Follow up quest: [[Ail'Vorith Class Quests]]}}

== Additional Lore ==
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" data-expandtext="Click here to view additional lore dialogue...">
{{QuestNote|Seek out [[Vaslir Naiyth]] inside the Obsidian Academy after acquiring your [[Obsidian Shackle]].}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Vaslir Naiyth.|Deep Common}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Naiyth meets your eyes with a penetrating stare. An involuntary shiver runs through your body. There is a touch of something about her gaze that is not of this realm.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Karzzul, young aspirant. What brings you to this vaslir of House Varros?}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Does your ambition lead you towards the path of the vaslir?}}
{{Chat|say|I seek the path of the vaslir|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Vaslir is the title bestowed on those of us who have successfully bound a being from another plane. It is the signature art of our great house.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Members of our house start as junior apprentices and hope to become senior apprentices.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|From senior apprentices, if their ambition wins out, they advance to leth'vaslir.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Finally, those who survive long enough become full vaslir.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|The head of our house, Archbinder Zaelthir Varros, is the only one with the title neth'vaslir.}}
{{Chat|say|Who is Archbinder Zaelthir Varros?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|I see how you ended up an outcast. In Ail'vorith, survival depends on knowing your rivals.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Still, it is good that you're learning.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|House Varros, the Subjugator of the Ebon Realms, has played an important role in our civilization's survival and expansion. Our necromancers and elementalists control powerful minions that serve the Queen as well as any solider of House Vael'xirith.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|While House Hal'kareth boasts of its research into the Spirals, the demons we've bound give us our own insight into Ach'aron. We know the Sixth Spiral in ways that transcend the clumsy explorations of those wizards and their Hathalian magics.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Naiyth laughs.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Hil dur ana zehad, Or whatever nonsense it is that they say.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Some of us have actually advanced in our understanding of magic since those days.}}
{{Chat|say|What is Ach'aron?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|There are other planes beyond this realm. The spirals are among the most important of them. We have fought wars with them in the past, and the demons of Ach'aron, the Sixth Spiral, are now of great service to our empire.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Thanks to House Varros, of course.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Naiyth smiles smugly.}}
{{Chat|say|What is Hathalian magic?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|The First City. Across the sea. We were once part of that civilization long ago. Before Calafrey. Before the Shadow blessed us. But those lands are now lost. Our future is here.}}
{{Chat|say|What is Calafrey?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|After the fall of the First City, we came here, to the continent of Aethoril. The elves were one people then, spread across many cities.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|But then we heard the Shadow's wisdom and descended. Now our empire is greater than Calafrey ever was, and our pathetic cousins struggle to hold onto the merest scrap of what they once had.}}
{{Chat|say|What is the Shadow?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|What backwards cave was your house living in prior to its, apparently well deserved, annihilation?}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Naiyth sighs and then continues in a patient tone.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|The Shadow is the voice that led us here, saving us from the Burning Heavens. Our glorious queen, Naliadra, was the last to hear the Shadow's voice. Thus she is the High Listener. Varsa ai Neth'xanl}}
{{Chat|say|What is the Burning Heavens?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|The Burning Heavens was a momentous event. It ravaged the surface while we waited below, growing strong.}}
</div>

