Night Harbor Cemetery Key Quest.content:
{{NeedsInfo}}
{{HasQuickGuide}}
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = phicon.png
| width             = 100px
| caption           = Placeholder Image
|Start Zone         = [[Night Harbor]]
|Quest Giver        = [[Gatekeeper Nusder]]
|Minimum Level      = 1
|Classes            = All
|Related NPCs       = [[a diseased bat]], [[a catacombs rat]], [[Liyna Esueiruc]]
|Quest Rewards      = (exp); [[Key to the Night Harbor Cemetery]]
}}

== Walkthrough ==

=== Part 1 - Prove Your Worth ===
{{QuestNote|[[Gatekeeper Nusder]] is located at the Red Mantle Keep entrance to the cemetery in [[Night Harbor]].}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Gatekeeper Nusder.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Yes, what is it?}}
{{Chat|say|What is behind this gate?}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|I'm responsible for the gate to Night Harbor's cemetery and the crypts within.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Don't get any ideas about sneaking in... diseased beasts linger beyond the main path during the day, and it gets significantly worse at night. It's a very dangerous place, not for the faint of heart.}}
{{Chat|say|Why are there diseased beasts here?}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|The place is cursed. It wasn't like that years ago, but it's gotten much worse, especially after sunset.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|At night, the cemetery is full of undead creatures roaming the grounds, searching for poor souls to kill and haunt.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|They're the restless remains of our ancestors. The catacombs are filled with unnamed folk... buried alive, executed, or thrown in like bones to the dogs.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|The outdoor area beyond the bridge is the crypt. That's where the noble families are buried. All of them seem cursed to haunt the living forever, never able to find peace.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|We're powerless to stop it, and Haradrel knows we've tried. Many good men and women were lost, and we've got nothing to show for it. Such folly!}}
{{Chat|say|Maybe I can help stop it?}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Apologies, but I don't trust you to do anything but add to our troubles.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|My duty matters to me, and without proof of your worth, I won't risk another life on this venture.}}
{{QuestInfo|Gatekeeper Nusder may be referring to player level as 'proof of worth' here.}}
{{QuestInfo|Need to verify - minimum starting level for quest.}}
{{Chat|say|How can I prove my worth?}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder looks you over.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|You at least look like you can hold your own.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|There's one thing we've yet to try... analyzing the source of the curse. If we could figure it out, maybe we could strike at its source and get rid of it.}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder nods at you.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Fine! Go and grab the diseased flesh of the beasts during the day. Fill this sack with ten samples so there's plenty to analyze.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Empty Satchel]] from Gatekeeper Nusder.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|If you can return to me still alive, we might be able to get the samples looked at in Sageside.}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder looks at you sternly.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Let me make myself clear... do NOT linger in the cemetery after Eth has set. I don't want another death on my conscience!}}
{{QuestNote|The gates to the cemetery will close at sunset and re-open at sunrise. NPCs inside the cemetery become aggressive and higher level once the sun sets.}}
{{QuestNote|Enter the gate and kill [[a diseased bat]] or [[a catacombs rat]] and loot [[Chunk of Diseased Meat]] x10. The meat is NODROP and not guaranteed on every kill, so plan accordingly if grouping here.}}
{{QuestNote|After combining the meats in the [[Empty Satchel]], you receive [[Fetid Satchel]].}}
{{QuestNote|Give the [[Fetid Satchel]] to [[Gatekeeper Nusder]].}}
{{QuestInfo|No exp or faction hits for this step.}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder looks visibly relieved.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|You had me worried. I'm glad you're still breathing!}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|...And you've got the flesh we needed, well done.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Now, bring the satchel to my friend Liyna in Sageside. You'll find her in the Grand Library.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Ask her to take a closer look at the flesh and see if she can find anything.}}

=== Part 2 - The Source of Corruption ===
{{QuestNote|Find [[Liyna Esueiruc]] in the second floor (teleporter puts you on floor 3) of the [[Night Harbor]] library (which is due east from Gatekeeper Nusder, at the Spellbinders of the Spire).}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Liyna Esueiruc.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc continues reading her book, then lifts her eyes and furrows her brow.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|What's this you're carrying? I can sense something isn't right...}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Liyna Esueiruc]] the [[Fetid Satchel]].}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc drops the satchel out of shock.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc looks at you, stunned, then picks the satchel back up with the tip of her fingers, handing it back to you.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|The smell... and the cursed energy emanating from this! What is Nusder getting himself into? This can't be good.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|Are you certain this is something you want to be involved in?}}
{{Chat|say|Yes, I am certain.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc looks you in the eyes, finally giving you a nod.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|He must've seen something in you if he sent you to me.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc concentrates and casts a spell.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|There, hand me the bag once more, I should be able to handle it without risk now.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Liyna Esueiruc]] the [[Fetid Satchel]] again.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc looks at the contents with extreme focus and attention.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|An old scent... cursed magic from another generation. I'm not surprised it's coming from the graveyard.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc murmurs something unintelligible.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|The result of an ancient form of necromancy... I'm sure of it.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|We need to dig deeper.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc points in the direction of the cemetery.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|The diseased beasts are just a byproduct of what's really happening there. We need to find the source.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|Take this note to Nusder right away.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Lightly Scented Piece of Parchment]] from Liyna Esueiruc.}}
{{QuestInfo|No faction or exp}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Gatekeeper Nusder]] and hand him the [[Lightly Scented Piece of Parchment]].}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|A note? Give me a second to read through Liyna's words.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Hmm... I feared she would say that.}}
{{exp}}
{{QuestInfo|No faction}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder sighs deeply before handing you back the note.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Are you sure you want to keep going?}}

=== Part 3 - A Sign of Necromancy ===
{{Chat|say|Yes.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|It's been a while since I've seen someone so eager to throw themselves into the maw of death.}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder sighs with a slight grin on his face.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|You remind me of my younger self. I'd be remiss not to give you a chance.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|When you feel ready, head back into the cemetery during the day with a valiant group of adventurers and look for any signs of necromancy.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|It won't be easy to find, but if you do, come back to me immediately with the note and proof of it.}}
{{QuestNote|You are to head back into the cemetery and find a [[Bloodied Engraved Rune]].}}
{{QuestNote|Kill [[a pristine beetle]], [[a sanguine bat]], [[an old scarab]], [[an ornate beetle]], or other named that requires camping till it spawns at the top of the cemetery and loot [[Bloodied Engraved Rune]].}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Gatekeeper Nusder]] and give him [[Bloodied Engraved Rune]] along with [[Lightly Scented Piece of Parchment]].}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|What's this you've found?}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder looks over the bloodied rune.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|I'm not certain what it means... but then again, it's not something I've seen before. Let me quickly write to Liyna.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Here, take this note and the rune to Liyna right away!}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Simple Piece of Parchment]] from Gatekeeper Nusder.}}

=== Part 4 - Further Research ===
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Liyna Esueiruc]] and give her [[Bloodied Engraved Rune]] along with [[Simple Piece of Parchment]].}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc snatches the note out of your hands and reads it through hurriedly.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc looks at the bloodied rune, inspecting it from all angles.}}
{{exp}}
{{QuestInfo|Any faction hits?}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|An even stronger remnant of cursed magic... Now I'm sure of it. There's something, or someone, hiding in the cemetery, and they're doing more than just hiding.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|We need more clues, but the cemetery's beasts won't carry them.}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc looks at you intently.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|You know what this means, don't you?}}
{{Emote|Liyna Esueiruc scribbles something down and hands it to you.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|Please share this message with Nusder and see whether he's of a same mind.}}
{{Chat|Liyna Esueiruc|In the meanwhile I'll keep studying this rune and see if there's more we can figure out.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Scented Piece of Parchment]] from Liyna Esueiruc.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Gatekeeper Nusder]] and hand him the [[Scented Piece of Parchment]].}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|I see how it is... so be it. We have no other choice.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|I'm entrusting you with the task of finding more clues.}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder hands you a tarnished old key.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Key to the Night Harbor Cemetery]] from Gatekeeper Nusder.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|You've earned yourself a key to the cemetery, but use it with the utmost care. Stepping foot in there at night will test your mettle, and your life will be at great risk!}}
{{Emote|Gatekeeper Nusder stares worriedly at the cemetery gates.}}
{{Chat|Gatekeeper Nusder|Haradrel be with you, adventurer. We're onto something...}}
{{QuestInfo|To be continued, probably requires killing [[a noble skeleton]], [[a bejeweled skeleton]], [[a majestic skeleton]] or [[a crowned skeleton]].}}
{{QuestInfo|More details are required...}}

