== Walkthrough ==

=== Part 1 - Clothes Delivery ===
{{QuestNote|Find [[a wash maiden]] (during daytime hours only) in [[Night Harbor]] inside the Bath house which is west of Night Market near the West Gate.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, a wash maiden.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden stops folding laundry to consider you a moment with tired eyes.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Hail to you, lily. Forgive me if I don't stop. Laundry waits for no one, and it's piled high today.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|It's an endless job and few offer to help. I suppose I can't complain, though. Trust in Trem they say.}}
{{Chat|say|I can help.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Help? Oh... no, no. I manage. Always have. That's kind of you to offer, lily. Truly kind.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden pauses for a moment, glancing up at you.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|But... if you truly mean it...}}
{{Chat|say|I mean it.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden looks away from you shyly.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|I'm unaccustomed to asking strangers for favors. But lily, if you're offering...}}
{{Chat|say|I am offering.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden finally meets your eyes.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|I don't want to be a bother, but I could use the help. So let's make this deal...}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Could you get these deliveries to my customers? They tend to pay extra to get their clothing delivered to them, as they're quite busy with their own jobs. You can keep any extra coin they hand you.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|And bring me their laundry. They always have more laundry to do.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Do this for me, and though I have little in the way of coin, I can at least give you a clean shirt or robe. I'll even dye it in your favorite color.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Are we in agreement, lily?}}
{{Chat|say|I agree!}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Great! Take this basket and these clean clothes.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|There's three deliveries to be made...}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Steinn the stonemason is awaiting the arrival of his work shirt.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Layith the troubadour wants her favorite cloak to use in the play.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|And Iskandar, who's still on guard duty, will need his pantaloons.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden pauses, almost apologetically.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Just... take the clothes to where they belong. When you come back with their laundry, we'll settle our deal.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden smiles.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Byrthia remembers kindness. Always does.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Byrthia's Laundry Basket]] from [[a wash maiden]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Stonemason's Shirt]] from [[a wash maiden]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Damsel's Cloak]] from [[a wash maiden]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Patrol Pantaloons]] from [[a wash maiden]].}}
{{QuestNote|Your task is to deliver cleaned laundry to various citizens in Night Harbor, collect their dirty laundry, and combine the dirty laundry in the provided basket to return to the wash maiden.}}
{{QuestNote|Find [[Mason Steinn]] in [[Night Harbor]] in the temple against the cliff between Sojourner's Camp and the Tannery. Follow the road north until you reach the temple.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Mason Steinn.}}
{{Emote|Mason Steinn turns to you, a cloud of stone dust following him. He is bare-chested beneath a heavy leather apron, his arms crossed more out of habit than comfort.}}
{{Chat|Mason Steinn|What're you after? Block, lime, chisels? If it's stonework, say it plain.}}
{{Emote|Mason Steinn shifts slightly, clearly aware of the draft.}}
{{Chat|Mason Steinn|And make it quick, if you can. Temple wind's got no respect for old bones.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Mason Steinn]] the [[Stonemason's Shirt]]:}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Faction|Smallfolk Alliance|+}}
{{Emote|Mason Steinn blinks when he sees the shirt, then lets out a relieved huff as he takes it.}}
{{Chat|Mason Steinn|By the stone! That's sight for sore eyes.}}
{{Emote|Mason Steinn puts it on immediately, rolling his shoulders as if settling armor.}}
{{Chat|Mason Steinn|You've my thanks. Truly.}}
{{Emote|Mason Steinn reaches under the workbench, producing a bundled sack of grimy clothes and presses it into your hands along with a few coins.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Steinn's Dirty Laundry]] from [[Mason Steinn]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive 5 copper from [[Mason Steinn]].}}
{{Chat|Mason Steinn|Five copper there. Give her this and my thanks.}}
{{Emote|Mason Steinn lowers his voice just a touch.}}
{{Chat|Mason Steinn|And do me a kindness... tell Byrthia to go lighter on the wheat paste next wash. It keeps the seams stiff, but itches like a nest of ants once I start sweating.}}
{{Emote|Mason Steinn tugs at his beard.}}
{{Chat|Mason Steinn|She's a good washer, though. Best in the city. I'll not hear otherwise.}}
{{QuestNote|Next, find [[Layith Kharem]] in [[Night Harbor]] up a ladder in Glimmermoon Hall behind the performance stage in Night Market.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Layith Kharem.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|Oh! Hi there.}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem turns with practiced grace, already smiling as if she is on stage.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|Yes, yes, of course. One moment.}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem produces a small parchment and signs it with an elaborate flourish.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|There you are. Do spell my name correctly if you tell the story later.}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem studies you, chin lifted.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|Were you hoping to catch tonight's performance, or have you come to simply admire?}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Layith's Autograph]] from [[Layith Kharem]].}}
{{QuestInfo|The purpose of this autograph is currently unknown. This may just be a flavor item.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Layith Kharem]] the [[Damsel's Cloak]]:}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Faction|Azure Veils|+}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem gasps softly as she see the cloak, her hands dramatically pressed to her chest.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|Thank the stars!}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem takes it at once, inspecting the fabric with sharp, practiced eyes. A beat passes, then she smiles radiantly.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|Perfect. Absolutely perfect.}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem softens a little, looking at you anew.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|You're a dear. Truly.}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem presses a copper coin into your hand without hesitation.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive 1 copper from [[Layith Kharem]].}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|For your trouble... and your timing.}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem tilts her head in a conspiratorial manner and produces a small, neatly tied bundle.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|And if you'd be so kind... you may return these to the washer maiden.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Layith's Soiled Stockings]] from [[Layith Kharem]].}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|The one and only Layith's bespoke stockings! Handle them with care and use unscented oils only, understand?}}
{{Emote|Layith Kharem pauses briefly before donning a smile that suggests she has already forgotten the inconvenience.}}
{{Chat|Layith Kharem|Now, if you'll excuse me, my audience awaits!}}
{{QuestNote|Lastly, find [[Guard Iskandar]] in [[Night Harbor]] in front of the large palace gate at the east end of Saltbreeze Park.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Guard Iskandar.}}
{{Emote|Guard Iskandar inclines his head slightly, eyes never fully leaving the park grounds.}}
{{Chat|Guard Iskandar|State your business, if you please. Only government officials are permitted beyond this point.}}
{{Emote|Guard Iskandar remains vigilant. A bead of sweat runs down his temple, but his stance never wavers.}}
{{Chat|Guard Iskandar|No trouble today, I trust.}}
{{Emote|Guard Iskandar allows himself a small, polite smile.}}
{{Chat|Guard Iskandar|If you're lost, I can point you the right way.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Guard Iskandar]] the [[Patrol Pantaloons]]:}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Faction|City Watch of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|Guard Iskandar sees the pantaloons and takes them swiftly, folding them once and sliding them into his pack as if they were part of his kit all along.}}
{{Emote|Guard Iskandar quickly produces a wrapped piece of gear, along with two coins.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Iskandar's Padded Loin Guard]] from [[Guard Iskandar]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive 2 copper from [[Guard Iskandar]].}}
{{Chat|Guard Iskandar|You have my thanks.}}
{{Emote|Guard Iskandar leans in to you, his voice dropping just enough to speak words only for your ears.}}
{{Chat|Guard Iskandar|Please... my padded loin guard... needs washing.}}
{{Emote|Guard Iskandar pauses as a faint, sheepish breath can be heard through his nose.}}
{{Chat|Guard Iskandar|If you would... see it back to Byrthia.}}
{{Emote|Guard Iskandar straightens at once, his gaze forward again.}}
{{Chat|Guard Iskandar|Now... move along citizen, if you please.}}
{{QuestNote|In [[Byrthia's Laundry Basket]], Combine: [[Steinn's Dirty Laundry]], [[Layith's Soiled Stockings]], and [[Iskandar's Padded Loin Guard]] to create [[Byrthia's Full Laundry Basket]].}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[a wash maiden]] and give her [[Byrthia's Full Laundry Basket]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden sets the basked down with a heavy thump, then looks at you with tired eyes and a grateful smile.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|You've done more than carry cloth today. You helped an old ogre keep her promises.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden nods.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|That matters. Words matter. Keeping your word matters a lot in cities like this one. A few words from the right person can change lives.}}
{{Emote|A wash maiden rummages beneath the wash table and produces a small rolled parchment sakk, worn smooth from handling.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Speaking of words and promises...this here's a sakk. Good as tender with merchants in Night Harbor. This one is for tailoring services.}}
{{Emote|A wash maiden turns it over in her palm.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|I was going to choose something for myself. Thought I might need it.}}
{{Emote|A wash maiden presses it into your hands instead.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Crude Tailoring Sakk]] from [[a wash maiden]].}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|But I think it'll suit you better than it ever would me.}}
{{Emote|A wash maiden pauses.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Now there's a choice you have to make, lily.}}
{{Emote|A wash maiden crinkles her eyes with a knowing look.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Do you want a shirt or a robe?}}
{{QuestNote|At this stage in the quest, you need to choose either a shirt or robe as your reward, and the following quest steps will vary slightly.}}
<tabber>
Shirt=
=== Part 2 - Tailoring the Shirt ===
{{Chat|say|I would like a shirt}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden nods once, pleased.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|A shirt, then. Good choice.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden wipes her hands on her apron and gestures vaguely eastward.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|You'll want the Night Market. Look for signs. Follow the lamps and music.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Off the promenade, there's a small tailor's shop. Noura works there. Her shirts are the best.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden gives you a look of approval.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Show her the sakk and tell her it's from Byrthia. She'll see you fitted proper.}}
{{QuestNote|Go to the tailor's shop in the Night Market of [[Night Harbor]]. The tailor shop is located behind the weapon and cloth armor merchants.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Noura the Tailor]] the [[Crude Tailoring Sakk]].}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor sees the sakk and her face brightens.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Oh! Well now. I haven't seen one of these in a while.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor turns it over with practiced fingers and nods.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Aye, this is good. It's a tradesman sakk endorsed by the Bank of Night Harbor. It covers the labor for a shirt commission just fine.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor begins rummaging through shelves and drawers, the bolts of cloth shifting and rustling. After a few moments, she stops, frowns, and sighs softly.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Hmm,that's a shame.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor comes back empty-handed, not upset but thoughtful. She flips the sakk into the air in your direction, and you catch it easily.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Crude Tailoring Sakk]] from [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|The sakk pays for my hands and my time and I'll honor that gladly. But the materials... you might as well hang on to that sakk until I can get more stock in.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor gives a small, apologetic shrug.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|You see, I'll need six crude silk scraps. I don't know when I'll get more in the shop. Maybe come back later.}}
{{Chat|say|What are crude silk scraps?}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor smiles faintly.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Crude silk isn't the fine stuff that nobles flaunt. It's rough, clumpy silk for common folk. Though cheap and sturdy, it's easy enough to work with in a pinch.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|You can buy it cheaply from tailors, but few still keep it as there are more popular materials to work with.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor lets her gaze drift for a moment.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|I used to gather it from cobweavers when I was a girl. My uncle was a boatwright. He had a place down by the harbor with old beams, salt in the air... and tiny spiders everywhere.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor slowly drops her smile.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|He passed a few years back. I've not had the heart to go rooting through the place since.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor looks back at you with a hopeful glint in her eyes.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|If you're willing to check the old house for crude silk, let me know. Six crude silk scraps is all I need.}}
{{Chat|say|I will check the old house.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor gives you a reassuring nod while handing you a bronze key from behind the fabric rack.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Bronze Boatwright's Key]] from [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Head out of the market and go east until you get to the entrance of Saltbreeze Park, but don't enter the park. Instead, head south toward the harbor.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Once you get to the harbor, bear just a little right, and my uncle's house will be on the left at the small dry dock. There should be no one living there, but if a vagrant has moved in, grab a watchman.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Remember, I need six crude silk scrap. Bring them back with your sakk, and I'll have your shirt stiched soon thereafter. Oh, you will need this also.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor offers you a small loom.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Backstrap Loom]] from [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Use this to combine four crude silk webs to make the scraps. Return it to me when you have them made.}}
{{QuestNote|To find her uncle's house, leave Night Market and head towards Saltbreeze Park. When you get to the entrance of Saltbreeze Park, turn right and walk through the small gate.}}
{{QuestNote|Immediately after passing through the gate you will spot a house behind the navigation signpost with some barrels and boxes. Go to the right of that building. Just around the corner on the left is a door with anchors on either side. Hold the key on your cursor and click on the door to open.}}
{{QuestNote|Inside of Noura's uncle's house, you will find two rooms. The entryway has two [[a cobweaver hatchling]] spawn points, and the bedroom has three spawn points which can spawn [[a cobweaver hatchling]], [[a cobweaver spider]], or [[a cobweaver avicularia]] (rare spawn).}}
{{QuestNote|Some notable items that can drop from these spiders include [[Ring of the Pauper]], [[Salt-Crusted Hammer]] and [[The Ugly Doll]].}}
{{QuestNote|Each of these mobs have a decent chance of dropping [[Crude Spider Silk]] and a 3-4 minute respawn timer. You need to collect 24 x [[Crude Spider Silk]].}}
{{QuestNote|Equip the [[Backstrap Loom]] into a bag slot and use either the crafting menu or manually put 4 x [[Crude Spider Silk]] inside and combine to create 6 x [[Crude Silk Scraps]].}}
{{QuestNote|While you are farming silk, be sure to use [[MUD Commands]] to explore the interior of the home, as there are several additional items that you can collect to gain a small amount of faction and experience.}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|The inside of the boatwright's home feels claustrophobic and stale, as though the air has not stirred for quite some time. Cobwebs drape nearly every corner of the room with thick veils spanning from wall to wall. It feels undisturbed... but not entirely abandoned.}}
{{QuestInfo|While standing next to the workbench and anchor attached to the wall..}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|A large iron anchor hangs against the stonework over a craftsman's workbench. Its metal is dark with age and its flukes spread like hooked talons over the warm-toned brick. Next to the table, a lone half-barrel sits oddly flush against the wall.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect workbench}}
{{Emote|A sturdy workbench stands against the wall, its surface scarred with knife cuts and burn marks from long hours of labor. Dust and cobwebs soften its edges now, but scattered tools and curled wood shavings hint at a craftsman's once-busy hands.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect anchor}}
{{Emote|The iron anchor's surface has been pitted by salt and time. Near the crown, a script is carved into the metal that reads, "Nafas min Bahr."}}
{{QuestInfo|There is no known NPC in [[Night Harbor]] that reacts to the text "Nafas min Bahr", but perhaps you can find one?}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect barrel}}
{{Emote|You take a closer look at the half-barrel. The lid is loosely placed and seems like it could be easily pushed aside.}}
{{QuestInfo|You can /push lid to make a secret escape from the house, which is explained if you chose the Robe reward option.}}
{{Chat|mud|/push lid}}
{{Emote|You press your weight against the loose lid. It gives with a soft wooden groan, swinging outward on hidden hinges to reveal a small opening.}}
{{Emote|Beyond the opening, light pours in, and fresh, salty air flows steadily. You crouch down and crawl into the secret passage, exiting the boatwright's home.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you crawled outside and want to get back in...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect barrel}}
{{Emote|You take a closer look at the half-barrel. The lid is loosely placed and seems easily pushed aside.}}
{{Chat|mud|/push lid}}
{{Emote|You press your weight against the loose lid. It gives with a soft wooden groan, swinging inward on hidden hinges to reveal a small opening.}}
{{Emote|Beyond the opening lies a narrow crawlspace, swallowed by darkness and cobwebs. You crouch down and crawl into the secret passage, entering the building's shadowed belly.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you stand near the bench with the book...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect bench}}
{{Emote|The narrow wooden bench sags slightly at its center, its surface furred with dust and d raped in gray cobwebs. An old book rests upon it, its cover wrapped at the edges, forgotten long ago.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take book}}
{{Emote|You carefully lift the faded book from the bench. A thin puff of dust rises as its brittle spine creaks softly in your hands.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Child's Diary]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Hold onto this diary, as you can hand it in later for experience and faction.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you stand near the oven...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect oven}}
{{Emote|The brick oven's mouth-like opening gapes, craving flame like a man lost in the Shaded Dunes, driven mad by thirst. A pile of ash is all that remains within.}}
{{QuestInfo|Entering the bedroom...}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|The bedroom feels musty and damp. Cobwebs hang like curtains from the ceiling beams and stretch across the corners, softening the hard lines of the stone walls.}}
{{QuestInfo|Standing closer to the pots...}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|Broken clay jars lie leaped in the corner, their once-glazed surfaces now dulled and cracked.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect jars}}
{{Emote|One broken jar still cups a hollow of dust. Gently nestled within it rests a large sewing needle. It seems out of place, or perhaps just misplaced, or simply re-placed, lying where it last fell from a hand or slipped from a pocket.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take needle}}
{{Emote|You pick up the old sewing needle, its worn eye slightly bent.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Large Sewing Needle]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Hold onto this needle, as you can hand it in later for experience and faction.}}
{{QuestInfo|Standing near the bed...}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|Against the bedroom wall rests a simple wooden bed, broken and neglected. A glass vial lies shattered nearby, staining the floor beneath it with whatever fluid it once held. Above the bed, a narrow shelf sags slightly, and beneath it sits a plain crate pushed close.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect bed}}
{{Emote|The bed's wooden frame creaks softly at your touch. The mattress stuffing has long since rotted away, leaving only sagging canvas tangled in thick cobwebs.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect vial}}
{{Emote|Shards of thin glass lie scattered beside the bed. The faint, dark stain that marks the stone beneath carries the slight smell of dried milk and something else you cannot quite place. Was this a potion once? Perhaps...}}
{{QuestInfo|Walking over to the crate in the corner of the room...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect crate}}
{{Emote|A wooden crate sits tucked beneath the sagging shelf. A thin layer of dust coats its surface, undisturbed save for a set of faint footprints pressed into the grime. The impressions are small and unmistakably those of a child... or possibly a gnome.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect shelf}}
{{Emote|The narrow shelf sags beneath a heavy veil of dust and cobwebs. From where you stand, it is just high enough that you cannot properly see if anything rests upon it.}}
{{QuestInfo|Stand on the crate in the corner of the room and check the shelf again...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect shelf}}
{{Emote|Up on the shelf, a crude, ragged doll lies on its side, its stitched face faded and uneven. It wears a handmade dress fashioned to resemble a mermaid's tail, crafted from scraps of crude silk sewn together with earnest, careful hands.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take doll}}
{{Emote|You take the ragged mermaid doll with great care as its hand-stitched dress is brittle with age.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Mermaid Doll]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Hold onto this doll, as you can hand it in later for experience and faction.}}
{{QuestInfo|Finally, if you stand next to the chest...}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|An old sea chest stands against the wall, its wood darkened with age and bound tightly by iron bands.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect chest}}
{{Emote|Despite rust and age, the sea chest remains locked firmly. Whatever lies within was meant to stay there.}}
{{QuestInfo|Despite numerous items and MUD commands, the secret to opening this chest has yet to be discovered. Perhaps you know how to open this?}}
{{QuestNote|Once you have finished exploring the house and have crafted your 6 x [[Crude Silk Scraps]], return to [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{QuestNote|If you picked up [[Child's Diary]], you may wish to read it to explain the handful of items you collected during your visit to the house.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Noura the Tailor]] your [[Bronze Boatwright's Key]], [[Backstrap Loom]], [[Crude Tailoring Sakk]], and 6 x [[Crude Silk Scraps]] (these can be handed in while stacked).}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor takes in the bundle of material with wide eyes, already testing the crude silk's strength between her nimble fingers.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Well now! You truly went and found them. Excellent!}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor drops her gaze briefly to the old key. She hesitates, then clears her throat.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Thank you for returning this to me. My uncle was a kind man. I was very young when he passed away. My aunt passed not too long after that.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|I was brought to the Wayfarers Hospice and raised by Sojourners. The key was given to me later by the priests of Relle.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor sets the key aside carefully, before clapping her hands once with renewed brightness.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Right then! The sakk covers my labor and you've brought the materials. Stand back just a moment. Let me see what we can make of this.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor mounts the silk upon the backstrap loom, working the threads with surprising speed. The soft rasp of fiber sliding through fiber fills the shop. After a short while, she lifts a freshly sewn garment from her work table.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|There we are. One crude silk shirt. It's dirty and won't turn any heads in Highpoint Terrace, but it'll serve you well enough.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor folds it neatly and hands it to you.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|All you need to do now is wash it. Head down to the water in the harbor, near my uncle's house. There are some scullery maidens washing and drying the clothes. Tell them Noura sent you, and they'll show you what you need to do next.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Dirty Crude Silk Shirt]] from [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{QuestInfo|If you picked up various items from Noura's Uncle's house, hand them in to [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Child's Diary]] to [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor takes the small book from your hands, expecting perhaps an old ledger. The moment she sees the worn cover, her fingers become still.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Where did you find this?}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor opens it, her eyes scanning the first page.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Dear Diary...}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor pauses, the sounds of the shop seeming to fade around her.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|I'd forgotten this. I thought it was lost when... when we moved from there.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor brushes the edge of a page with her thumb.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|I was a foolish girl. We both were.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor closes the diary carefully, not meeting your eyes for a moment.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Thank you for bringing it back to me. It wasn't all bad back then.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor straightens herself, regaining her usual composure.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|You've done me a kindness, and I'll remember it. Thank you.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Large Sewing Needle]] to [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor barely glances up when you place the old needle in her palm, until she truly sees it.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor freezes in place.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|No... that cannot be...}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor turns it slowly in her hand.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Gran gave me this. I used it for everything... even mending things that didn't need mending.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor lets out a faint, embarrassed breath that is half laugh, half ache.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|I thought it was stolen. I was so certain that Mira had taken it... I let that foolishness grow into something larger than it ever should've been.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor closes her fingers gently around the needle, holding it like something fragile.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Thank you. I'll have to apologize to Mira the next time I see her at the Scarlet Oasis. It took me a long time to let it go.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Mermaid Doll]] to [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor shifts her expression the moment she sees the ragged mermaid doll, her composure faltering completely.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|You found Seelia! Where did you find her? She's so dirty! It's been so long since I've seen her.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|I originally made this for Mira. She loved the sea even then. She said she would one day live out in the Twilight Sea, far from the troubles of Night Harbor.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Those were just the wishful dreams of two young, silly girls.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor smiles and touches her lips.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|We fought over such small things back then, and I let pride be louder than friendship. After some time, we eventually became friends again.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor holds the doll to her chest for a moment before looking back at you.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Thank you. I don't think I would've ever found this. I just can't go back there again.}}
{{QuestInfo|One additional item, [[The Ugly Doll]], can drop from [[a cobweaver avicularia]] rarely. Despite flavour text suggesting it may belong to [[Mira Gables]], neither [[Noura the Tailor]] or [[Mira Gables]] will take the item.}}

=== Part 3 - Coloring Your Attire ===
{{QuestNote|[[Noura the Tailor]] will send you to [[Riham]] to clean your newly fashioned attire.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to the harbor and head for the uncle's house where you farmed spiders earlier. From here, walk around the house to the shoreline. Follow the shoreline to the east (left from the house) until you find [[Riham]] standing near some washing buckets.}}
{{QuestNote|[[Riham]] is only active during the daytime, and will spawn at 6 AM server time, and despawns at 6 PM server time.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Riham.}}
{{Emote|Riham keeps the stirring rod moving through the vat, steam rising around her as she gives you a measured look.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Hail. Mind the dye and speak your purpose.}}
{{Chat|say|Noura sent me to clean this shirt.}}
{{Emote|Riham lifts a brow at the name, slowing the stir of her rod just slightly.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Noura sent you? Good. Kind of her to remember us.}} 
{{Chat|Riham|I have known her since she was a child. She, since then, has grown into a fine seamstress.}}
{{Emote|Riham nods toward the steaming vats and nearby basins.}}
{{Chat|Riham|If she sent you, then you must have cloth that needs color. But dye will not take to dirt.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Wash the silk first. I have soap for sale, and you may use the basins there.}}
{{Chat|Riham|When it is clean, bring it back to me and I will show you how to set the dye proper.}}
{{QuestNote|Begin by inspecting the nearby basins. These will be the vats in the ground without a colored liquid in the middle. There are three north of Riham and two south of Riham. Use MUD commands to find one with soapy water. If neither have soapy water, you can purchase [[Tallow Soap]] from [[Riham]] for 2 silver (see below).}}
{{QuestInfo|A basin with soapy water...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect basin}}
{{Emote|The wash basin is rich with tallow soap suds, bearing traces of crushed oils and dried desert flowers.}}
{{QuestInfo|Generally in the morning (6 AM - 9 AM) the basins will already have soap. Later in the day, you may have to add soap yourself.}}
{{QuestInfo|A basin with dirty water...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect basin}}
{{Emote|The basin's water is dull and gray beneath fading traces of tallow and wilted flower oils.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you try to wash your shirt in the dirty basin...}}
{{Chat|mud|/rub shirt}}
{{Emote|You scrub the shirt in the murky basin, but the fouled water only spreads the grime in dull streaks across the crude silk.}}
{{Emote|When you lift it out, it is no cleaner than before... perhaps worse. This shirt will still need a proper washing in the morning.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you find a dirty basin, you can purchase [[Tallow Soap]] from [[Riham]] for 2 silver.}}
{{QuestInfo|Find your dirty basin and fill it with soap. Click [[Tallow Soap]] to put it on your cursor and then /place soap.}}
{{Chat|mud|/place soap}}
{{Emote|You lower the block of tallow soap into the basin, and it begins to soften at once, releasing a clean, fatty scent as pale suds bloom across the surface.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect basin}}
{{Emote|The wash basin is rich with tallow soap suds, bearing traces of crushed oils and dried desert flowers.}}
{{QuestInfo|You can now properly wash your attire.}}
{{Chat|mud|/rub shirt}}
{{Emote|You kneel before the basin and work the shirt against the soap-slick stone, beating and rinsing until the grime loosens and slips away in cloudy swirls.}}
{{Emote|When you lift it free, the crude silk hangs clean and damp in your hands, ready at last for dye.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Crude Silk Shirt]].}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Crude Silk Shirt]] to [[Riham]].}}
{{Emote|Riham studies the crude silk shirt between her fingers, giving a small, approving nod.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Yes... the weave is clean. It will take color well.}}
{{Emote|Riham gestures toward the dye vats along the shoreline, each steeped in its own hue.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Choose the basin of the color you favor. Lower the shirt in and rub the silk gently in the dye solution. Stir often, as patient hands make for rich color.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Bring the wet shirt back to me after the dye is set and I will show you how to dry it.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from [[Riham]].}}
[[File:Ldq dye.png|thumb]]
{{QuestNote|Scattered around [[Riham]] are several different colored vats which can be used to dye your robe to a desirable color (See reference visual).}}
{{QuestNote|You can choose from black, orange, yellow, blue, red, green, and white.}}
{{QuestNote|Stand INSIDE of the desired color vat and type /rub shirt.}}
{{Chat|mud|/rub shirt}}
{{Emote|You lower the shirt into the <color> dye and guide it with the stirring staff, sending ripples of <color> across the vat.}}
{{Emote|You lift it out for a moment, but when you notice that the dye is uneven, you gently place it back down and continue to stir...}}
{{Emote|and stir...}}
{{Emote|and stir some more...}}
{{Emote|and some more...}}
{{Emote|and even more...}}
{{Emote|When you finally draw it up again, the crude silk has taken on a <color> that is rich and even along the weave.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive Wet <color> Crude Silk Shirt.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand your wet colored shirt to [[Riham]].}}
{{Emote|Riham takes the damp shirt from your hands, studying the depth of its color with a quiet nod of approval.}}
{{Chat|Riham|You have done well. The dye has taken true.}}
{{Emote|Riham steps toward the open side of the dye house where the sea breeze rolls in. With practiced movements, she lifts the garment high, letting the coastal wind snap through the silk while the desert sun bears down upon it. Steam rises faintly as she turns it in her hands.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Honor the elements... Do you know Porbor's second lesson?}}
{{Emote|Riham holds the shirt high between her palms as it dries.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Honor the earth from which the silk is drawn, the water that cleansed it, the fire of the sun that strengthened it, and the air... the faithful winds that set the work. These elements are tools of the Tradesman.}}
{{Emote|Riham lowers the now-dry garment, its color rich and even across the weave. She folds it once and places it back in your hands.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Here, your shirt is ready to serve you. Wear it well.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive <color> Crude Silk Shirt from [[Riham]].}}

