=== Part 2 - Tailoring the Robe ===
{{Chat|say|I would like a robe.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden considers you for a moment, then nods.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|A robe, then.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden wipes her hands on her apron and gestures vaguely eastward.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|You'll want Mira Gables for that. The wizards of Sageside trust her wares. They've done so for years.}}
{{Emote|a wash maiden gestures upward, as if tracing a tall shape in the air.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Find her in the shadow of the wizard spire in the morning hours. That's when her shop is open.}}
{{Chat|a wash maiden|Tell her Byrthia sent you. She'll see to your needs.}}
{{QuestNote|Find [[Mira Gables]], who can be found in a tailoring building near the shops just inside of North Gate.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Mira Gables.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Yes? How may I help you?}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Crude Tailoring Sakk]] to [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables takes the sakk and weighs it in her palm, assessing it with sharp eyes. She nods once, satisfied.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|I will honor it.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables turns and glides her fingers over the hanging robes and folded bolts, considering the fabrics. After a moment, she stops.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|No.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables turns back to you.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|The sakk, of course, is for the work, not the weave.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Crude silk, not the fine kind scholars preen over, mind you. Common silk. Resourceful, durable, and resilient, much like those priests of Porbor.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables searches through her materials and produces a small stack of crude silk.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|I have six crude silk scraps here, but will need twelve to finish a robe.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables places the sakk in your hand.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Crude Tailoring Sakk]] from [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Keep the sakk for now. Since my crude silk stock is low, you will have to wait until I find more.}}
{{Chat|say|What are crude silk scraps?}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables lifts her brown slightly at the word.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Yes. Crude. Specifically, crude silk scraps.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Crude silk comes from cobweavers. You know, the tiny spiders no bigger than my thumb. Hardly a challenge for a slayer such as yourself.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables rolls her eyes, her gaze then drifting toward the distant harbor.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|There is an old house where you might find some. It is abandoned now. The owner passed long ago, and no one has been there in years. It is likely crawling with cobweavers, though, it was locked the last time I passed by.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|I knew the family once...well, I was a friend of the girl who lived there.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables pauses, then shakes her head slightly.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Never mind. That was long ago.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|If you wish to check out the house, let me know. Otherwise, just return later when I have more crude silk in stock.}}
{{Chat|say|I will check out the house.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables briefly hesitates at your words.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Oh...you want to check out the house?}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|When I was a girl, I stayed there often with my friend. We used to gather cobweaver silk from the attic. We made clothes for our dolls from it. Poor stitches, but we were proud of them.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables pauses a moment, as if debating whether she should go on.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|...But there is a curious barrel along the side of the building, under a torn awning. Always was.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables meets your eyes.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|The lid hides a small door we used to sneak through. I think they put it there as a way to cover the hole in the wall without pinching the purse.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|We would slip inside at night, then head down to the water to swim in the harbor. If her uncle caught us...well, he never did. He slept like a Scarwood bear in winter and we were quiet as mice.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables allows herself a faint, fleeting smile.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Good luck. I will see you when you get back. Oh, I almost forgot! You will need this.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables hands you a small loom.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Backstrap Loom]] from [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Use this to combine four crude silk webs to make the scraps, then return it to me when you have them made.}}
{{QuestNote|To find the correct house, head to the entrance of Saltbreeze Park as if coming from the Night Market. When you get to the entrance of Saltbreeze Park, turn right and walk through the small gate.}}
{{QuestNote|Immediately after passing through the gate you will spot a house behind the navigation signpost with some barrels and boxes. Go to the right of that building. Just around the corner on the left is a door with anchors on either side. Hold the key on your cursor and click on the door to open.}}
{{QuestNote|Inside of the house, you will find two rooms. The entryway has two [[a cobweaver hatchling]] spawn points, and the bedroom has three spawn points which can spawn [[a cobweaver hatchling]], [[a cobweaver spider]], or [[a cobweaver avicularia]] (rare spawn).}}
{{QuestNote|Some notable items that can drop from these spiders include [[Ring of the Pauper]], [[Salt-Crusted Hammer]] and [[The Ugly Doll]].}}
{{QuestNote|Each of these mobs have a decent chance of dropping [[Crude Spider Silk]] and a 3-4 minute respawn timer. You need to collect 24 x [[Crude Spider Silk]].}}
{{QuestNote|Equip the [[Backstrap Loom]] into a bag slot and use either the crafting menu or manually put 4 x [[Crude Spider Silk]] inside and combine to create 6 x [[Crude Silk Scraps]].}}
{{QuestNote|While you are farming silk, be sure to use [[MUD Commands]] to explore the interior of the home, as there are several additional items that you can collect to gain a small amount of faction and experience.}}
