{{Emote|Up on the shelf, a crude, ragged doll lies on its side, its stitched face faded and uneven. It wears a handmade dress fashioned to resemble a mermaid's tail, crafted from scraps of crude silk sewn together with earnest, careful hands.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take doll}}
{{Emote|You take the ragged mermaid doll with great care as its hand-stitched dress is brittle with age.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Mermaid Doll]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Hold onto this doll, as you can hand it in later for experience and faction.}}
{{QuestInfo|Finally, if you stand next to the chest...}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|An old sea chest stands against the wall, its wood darkened with age and bound tightly by iron bands.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect chest}}
{{Emote|Despite rust and age, the sea chest remains locked firmly. Whatever lies within was meant to stay there.}}
{{QuestInfo|Despite numerous items and MUD commands, the secret to opening this chest has yet to be discovered. Perhaps you know how to open this?}}
{{QuestNote|Once you have finished exploring the house and have crafted your 6 x [[Crude Silk Scraps]], return to [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{QuestNote|If you picked up [[Child's Diary]], you may wish to read it to explain the handful of items you collected during your visit to the house.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Mira Gables]] your [[Backstrap Loom]], [[Crude Tailoring Sakk]], and 6 x [[Crude Silk Scraps]] (these can be handed in while stacked).}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables accepts the sakk, the six crude silk scraps, and the backstrap loom without ceremony, her expression steady and unreadable.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Good. Everything is in order.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables wastes no time, mounting the crude silk upon the loom with swift, efficient movements.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|This will only take a minute or two.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables gets to work. The soft pull and snap of tightened threads fills the room. After some time, she cuts the finished garment free and gives it a brisk shake.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|There. A crude silk robe.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables folds it and hands it over to you.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|It is dirty and will not turn heads in Highpoint Terracce, but it will serve you well, I think.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables folds it neatly and presses it into your hands.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|All you need to do is wash it. Down by the water in the harbor, near the boatwright's house, there are some scullery maids working, washing and dying the clothes. Tell them Mira sent you. They will show you what you need to do next.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Dirty Crude Silk Robe]] from [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{QuestInfo|If you picked up various items from the house, hand them in to [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Child's Diary]] to [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables takes the diary as a faint crease forms between her brows, clearly expecting something trivial.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables opens it and goes very still.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|I had forgotten this little book.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables darts her eyes across the page, her jaw tightening slightly.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Noura always wrote when she was upset. Ink was safer than shouting, I guess.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables pauses, then closes the diary with deliberate care.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Children are quick to wound friends and foes alike with words, Noura was... thick-headed at times.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|I guess I was a foolish girl back then. We both were.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables sharpens her voice again, though not unkindly.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|It seems we were both guilty of that.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|You have done us both a kindness. I will get her property to her. Thank you.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Mermaid Doll]] to [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Night Harbor|+}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables eyes the ragged mermaid doll, and for a fleeting moment, her sharp composure falters.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|You found Seelia! She kept this from me... Took it back, actually.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables reaches out, but does not immediately take it, only brushing the edge of the tiny stitched dress with one finger.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|She made it for me. Noura said the sea was mysterious and would always have stories for us. Seelia was a mermaid in one of those tales.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables almost laughs, a breath escaping her lips.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|I was jealous of her hands even then... not her toys. Noura is a gifted seamstress.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables holds the doll to her chest for a moment before looking back at you.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Time makes fools of little children... and sometimes of grown women too. I will cherish this... always.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Large Sewing Needle]] to [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables looks down at the old sewing needle in your hand, her expression unreadable at first.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|So, it was there all along. I knew it would be.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables takes it between her fingers, turning it once in the light.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|I told her I did not take it. She, of course, did not believe me. She was upset. There was nothing I could say to change her mind.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Strange how a small thing can stitch a tear so wide.}}
{{Emote|Mira Gables hands it back to you after a moment.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|It seems the past has a way of surfacing when least expected. I cannot give this to her, you understand?}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|She thinks I took her Gran's needle long ago. We are long past that argument. Time mends all wounds.}}
{{Chat|Mira Gables|Take it to her. I am sure she will be happy it was found. Thank you for finding this.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from [[Mira Gables]].}}
{{QuestNote|You can find [[Noura the Tailor]] in the tailoring shop of the Night Market, just behind the used weapons and cloth armor merchants.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand the [[Large Sewing Needle]] to [[Noura the Tailor]].}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor barely glances up when you place the old needle in her palm, until she truly sees it.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor freezes in place.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|No... that cannot be...}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor turns it slowly in her hand.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Gran gave me this. I used it for everything... even mending things that didn't need mending.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor lets out a faint, embarrassed breath that is half laugh, half ache.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|I thought it was stolen. I was so certain that Mira had taken it... I let that foolishness grow into something larger than it ever should've been.}}
{{Emote|Noura the Tailor closes her fingers gently around the needle, holding it like something fragile.}}
{{Chat|Noura the Tailor|Thank you. I'll have to apologize to Mira the next time I see her at the Scarlet Oasis. It took me a long time to let it go.}}
{{QuestInfo|One additional item, [[The Ugly Doll]], can drop from [[a cobweaver avicularia]] rarely. Despite flavour text suggesting it may belong to [[Mira Gables]], neither [[Noura the Tailor]] or [[Mira Gables]] will take the item.}}

=== Part 3 - Coloring Your Attire ===
{{QuestNote|[[Mira Gables]] will send you to [[Riham]] to clean your newly fashioned attire.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to the harbor and head for the house where you farmed spiders earlier. From here, walk around the house to the shoreline. Follow the shoreline to the east (left from the house) until you find [[Riham]] standing near some washing buckets.}}
{{QuestNote|[[Riham]] is only active during the daytime, and will spawn at 6 AM server time, and despawns at 6 PM server time.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Riham.}}
{{Emote|Riham keeps the stirring rod moving through the vat, steam rising around her as she gives you a measured look.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Hail. Mind the dye and speak your purpose.}}
{{Chat|say|Mira sent me to clean this robe.}}
{{Emote|Riham lifts a brow at the name, slowing the stir of her rod just slightly.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Mira sent you? Good. She sends many mages from Sageside our way.}} 
{{Chat|Riham|I have known her a long time. She lived just a stones throw from here. One of the harbor children she was. Since then, she has grown into fine seamstress.}}
{{Emote|Riham nods toward the steaming vats and nearby basins.}}
{{Chat|Riham|If she sent you, then you must have cloth that needs color. But dye will not take to dirt.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Wash the silk first. I have soap for sale, and you may use the basins there.}}
{{Chat|Riham|When it is clean, bring it back to me and I will show you how to set the dye proper.}}
{{QuestNote|Begin by inspecting the nearby basins. These will be the vats in the ground without a colored liquid in the middle. There are three north of Riham and two south of Riham. Use MUD commands to find one with soapy water. If neither have soapy water, you can purchase [[Tallow Soap]] from [[Riham]] for 2 silver (see below).}}
{{QuestInfo|A basin with soapy water...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect basin}}
{{Emote|The wash basin is rich with tallow soap suds, bearing traces of crushed oils and dried desert flowers.}}
{{QuestInfo|Generally in the morning (6 AM - 9 AM) the basins will already have soap. Later in the day, you may have to add soap yourself.}}
{{QuestInfo|A basin with dirty water...}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect basin}}
{{Emote|The basin's water is dull and gray beneath fading traces of tallow and wilted flower oils.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you try to wash your robe in the dirty basin...}}
{{Chat|mud|/rub robe}}
{{Emote|You scrub the robe in the murky basin, but the fouled water only spreads the grime in dull streaks across the crude silk.}}
{{Emote|When you lift it out, it is no cleaner than before... perhaps worse. This robe will still need a proper washing in the morning.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you find a dirty basin, you can purchase [[Tallow Soap]] from [[Riham]] for 2 silver.}}
{{QuestInfo|Find your dirty basin and fill it with soap. Click [[Tallow Soap]] to put it on your cursor and then /place soap.}}
{{Chat|mud|/place soap}}
{{Emote|You lower the block of tallow soap into the basin, and it begins to soften at once, releasing a clean, fatty scent as pale suds bloom across the surface.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect basin}}
{{Emote|The wash basin is rich with tallow soap suds, bearing traces of crushed oils and dried desert flowers.}}
{{QuestInfo|You can now properly wash your attire.}}
{{Chat|mud|/rub robe}}
{{Emote|You kneel before the basin and work the robe against the soap-slick stone, beating and rinsing until the grime loosens and slips away in cloudy swirls.}}
{{Emote|When you lift it free, the crude silk hangs clean and damp in your hands, ready at last for dye.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Crude Silk Robe]].}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Crude Silk Robe]] to [[Riham]].}}
{{Emote|Riham studies the crude silk robe between her fingers, giving a small, approving nod.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Yes... the weave is clean. It will take color well.}}
{{Emote|Riham gestures toward the dye vats along the shoreline, each steeped in its own hue.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Choose the basin of the color you favor. Lower the robe in and rub the silk gently in the dye solution. Stir often, as patient hands make for rich color.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Bring the wet robe back to me after the dye is set and I will show you how to dry it.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from [[Riham]].}}
[[File:Ldq dye.png|thumb]]
{{QuestNote|Scattered around [[Riham]] are several different colored vats which can be used to dye your robe to a desirable color (See reference visual).}}
{{QuestNote|You can choose from black, orange, yellow, blue, red, green, and white.}}
{{QuestNote|Stand INSIDE of the desired color vat and type /rub robe.}}
{{Chat|mud|/rub robe}}
{{Emote|You lower the robe into the <color> dye and guide it with the stirring staff, sending ripples of <color> across the vat.}}
{{Emote|You lift it out for a moment, but when you notice that the dye is uneven, you gently place it back down and continue to stir...}}
{{Emote|and stir...}}
{{Emote|and stir some more...}}
{{Emote|and some more...}}
{{Emote|and even more...}}
{{Emote|When you finally draw it up again, the crude silk has taken on a <color> that is rich and even along the weave.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive Wet <color> Crude Silk Robe.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand your wet colored robe to [[Riham]].}}
{{Emote|Riham takes the damp robe from your hands, studying the depth of its color with a quiet nod of approval.}}
{{Chat|Riham|You have done well. The dye has taken true.}}
{{Emote|Riham steps toward the open side of the dye house where the sea breeze rolls in. With practiced movements, she lifts the garment high, letting the coastal wind snap through the silk while the desert sun bears down upon it. Steam rises faintly as she turns it in her hands.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Honor the elements... Do you know Porbor's second lesson?}}
{{Emote|Riham holds the robe high between her palms as it dries.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Honor the earth from which the silk is drawn, the water that cleansed it, the fire of the sun that strengthened it, and the air... the faithful winds that set the work. These elements are tools of the Tradesman.}}
{{Emote|Riham lowers the now-dry garment, its color rich and even across the weave. She folds it once and places it back in your hands.}}
{{Chat|Riham|Here, your robe is ready to serve you. Wear it well.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive <color> Crude Silk Robe from [[Riham]].}}

|-|
</tabber>

