== Walkthrough ==

{{QuestNote|[[Reeve Thurston Winter]] is located in a building in the center of Penshaw Village. His building is tan stone with a minaret and Red Mantle banners, similar to what you'd find in Night Harbor.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Reeve Thurston Winter.}}
{{Chat|Reeve Thurston Winter|Greetings. I am Reeve Thurston Winter, charged with keeping order in Penshaw.}}
{{Chat|Reeve Thurston Winter|These are hard times, and what peace we have left is easily broken. We have opened our doors to outsiders willing to help us face a growing threat.}}
{{Chat|say|What growing threat?}}
{{Chat|Reeve Thurston Winter|The Sangrel Fist has become a scourge on our roads and farms. They are ruthless thieves emboldened by their numbers, who prey on honest folk who can scarcely defend themselves.}}
{{Chat|Reeve Thurston Winter|We cannot allow this to continue. Seek them out and then their ranks. They wear red wraps upon their hands. Bring me four as proof.}}
{{QuestNote|Head off to kill [[A Sangrel striker]] and related mobs until you collect 4 x [[Sangrel Fist Wraps]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Where are these located relative to the quest giver?}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Reeve Thurston Winter]] and hand him 4 x [[Sangrel Fist Wraps]].}}
{{Chat|Reeve Thurston Winter|You certainly did your part. Well done. The Sangrel Fist has brought enough fear to this village. Perhaps they'll think twice before entering our gates.}}
{{Chat|Reeve Thurston Winter|Every bandit brought down is one less threat to our farms and homes.}}
{{Chat|Reeve Thurston Winter|Take this sigil. Carrying it authorizes you to privileged information, should be needed to defend Penshaw.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sigil of Inquiry]] from Reeve Thurston Winter.}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Red Mantles|+}}
{{Faction|Village of Penshaw|+}}
{{Faction|Ardent Keepers|+}}
{{Faction|Sangrel Fist|-}}

{{QuestNote|You can now speak with [[Detective Brunsworth]], located close to [[Reeve Thurston Winter]], to continue the storyline...}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Detective Brunsworth.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|Hail, Adventurer, and well met. I have heard good things about your services in Penshaw.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|I was sent here to investigate the growing threat of the Sangrel. Their numbers have sharply increased as of late. Perhaps you would be willing to dig a little further for us?}}
{{Chat|say|I will dig a little further.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|Very good. We know little of what binds these cult bandits together.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|This type of organization requires leadership. Go to their camps and search for clues. Whether found among their belongings or taken from those who carry them matters little.}}
{{QuestInfo|Is there more dialogue that can be exposed to explain the rites in the next step?}}
{{QuestNote|There are four rites that need to be collected and returned to [[Detective Brunsworth]].}}
{{QuestNote|[[Sangrel Rite I]] is found off Sangrels at the small sangrel camp next to the poachers.}}
{{QuestInfo|Camps in the southeast of Keepers Blight, near the treehouse.}}
{{QuestNote|[[Sangrel Rite II]] is found of shady farmers at the shady farm.}}
{{QuestInfo|Shady farmers south of Penshaw and the Temple (big white building near Penshaw)}}
{{QuestNote|[[Sangrel Rite III]] is found in a tent in the large sangrel camp, you will need to use mud commands.}}
{{QuestNote|Inside of the tent with the crate...}}
{{QuestInfo|When approaching the camps from the south, the tent is in the first camp, you will see a small box sitting on the ground.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect crate}}
{{Chat|mud|/take scroll}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sangrel Rite III]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Need MUD emotes and responses here.}}
{{QuestNote|[[Sangrel Rite IV]] is found off sangrels at the large sangrel camp.}}
{{QuestInfo| Any Sangrels in the north west corner of the map, on the coast side of the spider log.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Detective Brunsworth]].}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Sangrel Rite I]], [[Sangrel Rite II]], [[Sangrel Rite III]], and [[Sangrel Rite IV]] to [[Detective Brunsworth]].}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|How interesting... This text seems to be written in an old tongue.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|We will need an expert to translate its meaning. The abbey outside of Penshaw is home to scribes versed in forgotten tongues. Seek their aid, and when you return with their translation, present your sigil as well so you may be properly rewarded.}}
{{QuestInfo|Any exp or faction hits for this turn-in?}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sangrel Rites: Volume I - IV]] from a scribe of Detective Brunsworth.}}
{{QuestNote|Brunsworth will direct you to [[a scribe of Tilustra]] in the large church to the south of Penshaw.}}
{{Chat|a scribe of Tilustra|This... is not a devotional text of any tradition we preserve here. I dare not read such things aloud.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sangrel Rites: Volume I - IV (Translated)]] from a scribe of Tilustra.}}
{{Chat|a scribe of Tilustra|Tilustra teaches us that knowledge is meant to illuminate, not corrupt. This text ties selfish desire to divinity... a disturbing teaching, indeed. Take care with whom you share it. There are many easily drawn to such doctrine.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Detective Brunsworth]] and give him your [[Sigil of Inquiry]] and [[Sangrel Rites: Volume I - IV (Translated)]].}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|This appears to be doctrine... a structure set of rites meant to be memorized by initiates of this cult. It attracts the sort who would rather blame fate than earn an honest living.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|This is no reason to assume any truth in it. If Eyzin has followers, it is because he is persuasive, or because he understands how to manipulate desperate men.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|Their success is far more likely to be practical than divine. Spies within the town, watches along the roads, or a vantage point over our docks. That is where we find answers, not in fire and ash.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|I will gather further intelligence. This investigation is not concluded.}}
{{Chat|Detective Brunsworth|For now, you have proven capable. Take this. It is a sigil for one worthy of your skill, granted in recognition of your diligence.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sigil of Honor]] from Detective Brunsworth.}}
{{QuestInfo|Any exp hits? Faction hits? Follow-up breadcrumbs from nearby NPCs?}}

