{{QuestNote|This quest begins in [[Ail'Vorith]] in the Obsidian Academy courtyard by talking with [[Apprentice Esveth]]. Esveth is located directly across from the academy under a light post.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Apprentice Esveth.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Apprentice Esveth|Karzzul, I am Apprentice Esveth. My master, [[Vaslir Naiyth]], has tasked me with acquiring raw materials for House Varros.}}
{{Chat|Apprentice Esveth|I will pay you for ghoul skin, stacks of bone chips, and, of course, corpses.}}

=== Bone Chips ===

{{QuestNote|Upon handing 1x [[Bone Chips]] to [[Apprentice Esveth]]...}}
{{Emote|Apprentice Esveth inspects the bone chip.}}
{{Chat|Apprentice Esveth|It is of usable quality. However, I only pay for entire stacks. That means 20.}}
{{QuestNote|Upon handing 20x [[Bone Chips]] to [[Apprentice Esveth]]...}}
{{Emote|Apprentice Esveth inspects the bone chips.}}
{{Chat|Apprentice Esveth|Yes, we can make use of these. Here is your reward!}}

{{exp}}

{{Faction|House Varros|+}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive 25 copper from Apprentice Esveth.}}

=== Ghoul Skin ===

{{QuestInfo|1 ghoul skin at a time for 10 copper.}}

=== Corpses ===
{{QuestNote|The corpses Apprentice Esveth is referring to are the [[Sullen corpse]] and [[Mournful Corpse]] from the deep elf exiles.}}
{{QuestNote|Upon handing in either 1x [[Sullen corpse]] or 1x [[Mournful Corpse]] to [[Apprentice Esveth]]...}}
{{Emote|Apprentice Esveth inspects the corpse.}}
{{Chat|Apprentice Esveth|This is suitable for our work. Here is your pay}}

{{exp}}

{{Faction|House Varros|+}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive 10 copper from Apprentice Esveth.}}

{{QuestInfo|More information is required...faction amount?}}

House Xal'tharn (Quest).content:
{{NeedsInfo}}
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = klavel_sul.jpg
| width             = 200px
| caption           = 0.30.0.0
|Start Zone         = [[Ail'Vorith]]
|Quest Giver        = [[Klavel Sul]]
|Minimum Level      = 8
|Classes            = INQ MNK
|Related NPCs       = [[a separated skull]];[[a spectral remnant]]
}}

== Rewards ==
* Experience
* Inquisitor - [[Dull Iron Cuirass]]
* Monks -  [[Simple Chestwrap]]
* Access to the city

== Related Items ==
* [[Lost skull]]

== Walkthrough ==
{{QuestNote|This quest starts at the conclusion of the [[Ail'Vorith Starter Quest]] after you receive your [[Obsidian Shackle]].}}

=== Part 1 - Lvl 8+ ===
{{QuestNote|[[Klavel Sul]] is located in the Obsidian Academy with the melee class instructors. From the bridge and gate into the Foreign Quarter, enter the building on the left and head to the back of the room.}}
{{QuestInfo|Klavel's introduction text varies depending on your class, but the conversation is identical after the introduction line.}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Klavel Sul.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|Exiles sing of lost houses and pray to dead gods. Whom would you call master?}}
{{Chat|say|The Queen|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|The cenobites of House Xal'tharn serve the Dark Queen above all else. Her wrath and her pleasure are our only desires.}}
{{Chat|say|I would be a cenobite|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|The monks of House Xal’tharn carry out the Queen's will with iron staves and iron hearts.}}
{{Chat|say|Do you have a task for me?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|Fragments of the dead roam the western shore of the city. They are the accursed remnants of lesser houses who dared betray their Queen. Destroy them and fill this satchel with six of their skulls.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Remnant Satchel]] from [[Klavel Sul]].}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|Boats pass the west shore of Ail'vorith on their course to the sea.  Cross the bridge into the city at your peril, for the guards will not suffer an exile to pass the gates. You must take a different path.}}
{{QuestInfo|The mobs needed for the next step are levels 8-11}}
{{QuestNote|Swim around the west of the city where elementals and various skulls patrol the west island shores. Kill [[a separated skull]] and [[a spectral remnant]] to collect 6 [[Lost Skull]] to fill the bag.}}
{{QuestNote|Combine the container and return it to [[Klavel Sul]].}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|So it is done. Pity not the dead who chose the path of desolation. The Dark Queen's rule is absolute. Those who waver shall be cast into the pits of the Shol'tar, and those who challenge her sovereignty shall be cast into oblivion.}}
{{exp}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|Swear your allegiance to the Queen, and you may be permitted to enter the city as a servant of House Xal'tharn.}}
{{Chat|say|I swear allegiance to the Queen!|Deep Common}}<br>
{{exp}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|You have entered into the service of the Avatar of Barbhaal, Naliadra the Eternal. House Xal'tharn may call upon you to carry out her will, and you must answer under pain of death.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Simple Chestwrap]] from Klavel Sul.}}
{{QuestInfo|Do you receive experience twice during this dialogue? Or is it a typo?}}

=== Part 2 - level 13+ ===
{{QuestInfo|Faction hits? Any follow-up breadcrumbs?}}

<tabber>
|-|Inquisitor=
'''Until you are level 13, Klavel Sul will only respond to you in the following manner:'''<br>

{{Chat|say|Hail, Klavel Sul.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|You lack the skill to be of greater service to House Xal'tharn. Return to me when you are more seasoned.}}

'''Once you are level 13, he will give you the option to further serve the queen. <br>'''

{{Chat|say|Hail, Klavel Sul.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|The masters of House Xal'tharn summon you to the halls of the Shol'tar, {you}. Your oath compels you. Do you accept?.}}
{{Chat|say|I accept.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Klavel Sul|The Shol'tar lies beneath the Queen's arena. Take the road on the right as you go into the Dark City. You may pass through the dungeon gates, near the bank. Bring this summons to the Inquisitor, Lady Miniel.}}
'''Klavel will provide you with a summons that you can deliver to Lady Miniel.'''

From here you must find [[Miniel Ubast]] in the Inquisitor's Guildhall. If you find her without a summons, she will respond to you as follows:

{{Chat|say|Hail, Miniel Ubast.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Miniel Ubast|Hail, Inquisitor of Xal'tharn. You have not been summoned here today.}}

'''Once you give her the summons, she will provide you with a new duty.'''
{{Chat|Miniel Ubast|It is well that you have come when called, Inquisitor. It is time for you to carry out your duty to the Queen.}}
{{Chat|say|What duty shall my Queen have me complete?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Miniel Ubast|Exiles who refuse to serve are cast into the Shol'tar. Others flee and conspire to overthrow the great houses. The insolence of the lesser houses will not be tolerated.}}
{{Chat|say|Where can these traitorous exiles be found?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Miniel Ubast|Look for encampments of these outcasts to the south, by the river that flows into the Great Cavern Sea. Slay the exiles and collect the sigils of three lesser houses, and bring me the head of the traitor, Gullach Qtal'qar.}}
{{Chat|Miniel Ubast|Do this, and you shall have a weapon befitting your new life.}}

'''The exiles can be found past the waterfall where snakes gather, on the bottom "floor", past the invisible hired Thug. You have to kill them to get 3 sigils of a lesser house. They are [[Sigil of a Lesser House (Unknown)]], [[Sigil of a Lesser House (Silver)]], and [[Sigil of a Lesser House (Gold)]]. You can only have 1 of each, so you can loot them until you have all three. You can kill any exile to get a chance at a sigil drop, but Gullah Qtal'gar is a named that can only spawn in the place of the exiles on the bottom "floor" of that specific area behind the hired thug, so kill them all until he spawns and kill Gullah for [[Gullach's Head]]. Return the sigils and the head to Miniel Ubast.'''

Miniel Ubast will examine the sigils in turn before tossing them aside.
{{Chat|Miniel Ubast|Worthless Trinkets, all.}}
She will then cradle the head in her hands.
{{Chat|Miniel Ubast|Had he not fled and conspired against the Queen, I would have let him live. For a while. You have your duty today, (you). Take this blade and wield it in the Dark Queen's name.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Iron Render]] from [[Miniel Ubast]].}}
Monks will receive a different item:
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Tarnished Iron Bo]] from [[Miniel Ubast]].}}
{{exp}}<br>
You gain faction with [[House Xal'tharn]].<br>

'''She will then nod, affirming your good work. If you hail her after receiving the [[Iron Render]], she will say the following:'''<br>
{{Chat|say|Hail, Miniel Ubast.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Miniel Ubast|Carry the weapon of the Queen's chosen with pride, (you).}}
|-|Monk=
{{QuestInfo|Need dialogue, faction hits, rewards, NPCs, etc}}
</tabber>

Perilous to Leave by Oneself.content:
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = A_wise_elder.png
| width             = 100px
| caption           = a wise elder
|Start Zone         = [[Night Harbor]]
|Quest Giver        = [[a wise elder]]
|Minimum Level      = 1
|Classes            = All
|Related NPCs       = 
|Quest Rewards      = [[Wooden Bow]]; [[Wooden Claw]]; [[Wooden Club]]; [[Wooden Dagger]]; [[Wooden Scythe]]; [[Wooden Sword]]
}}

{{QuestInfo|This quest is repeatable, but only if you do not posses a wooden weapon.}}

== Walkthrough ==

{{QuestNote|[[a wise elder]] is located in the large stone building just to the North of the West Bank in [[Night Harbor]].}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, a wise elder.}}
{{Chat|a wise elder|It's perilous to leave by oneself! Take this.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive a wooden weapon from a wise elder.}}
{{Emote|a wise elder looks pleased.}}
{{Chat|a wise elder|Also, take someone with you, a companion you can trust to guard your back. Your survival will depend on it.}}

== Trivia ==

* The line "It's perilous to leave by oneself! Take this." is a nod to the famous "[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/It%27s_dangerous_to_go_alone! It's dangerous to go alone!]" quote from the Legend of Zelda series. 

