House Varros (Quest).content:
{{NeedsInfo}}
{{Quest
| name          = House Varros
| Quest Giver   = [[Vaslir Naiyth]]
| Start Zone    = [[Ail'Vorith]]
| Related NPCs  = [[Vaslir Vharkith]]; [[Laeran Birchshade]]; [[Vaslir Maryn]]; [[Vaslir Kiannes]]; [[Nyxia Ak'kin]]; [[Mournful Outcast]]; [[Miral the Dark Elf]]; [[Freysia Riftrend]]; [[Belot]]; [[Senior Apprentice Syrsil]]
| Related Items = [[Naiyth's Mushroom Pouch]]; [[Vharkith's Research Notes]]; [[Corpse Dust]]; [[Essence of Elemental Air]]; [[Essence of Elemental Earth]]; [[Sample of Tainted Water]]; [[Flask of Essairyl]]; [[Bottle of Nerolir]]; [[Letter to Freysia Riftrend]]; [[Vharkith's Order]]; [[House Varros Senior Apprentice Robe]]
| imagefilename = phicon.png
| width         = 100px
| caption       = Placeholder Image
| Minimum Level = 1
| Classes       = ELE NEC
| Races         =
| Quest Rewards = (exp); [[Faction|House Varros]];
}}

== Walkthrough ==
{{QuestNote|This quest starts at the conclusion of the [[Ail'Vorith Starter Quest]] after you receive your [[Obsidian Shackle]].}}

=== Part 1 ===
{{QuestNote|[[Vaslir Naiyth]] is located in the Obsidian Academy. As you enter the academy, she is located near the stairs in the back of the room on the right.}}

{{Emote|Vaslir Naiyth meets your eyes with a penetrating stare. An involuntary shiver runs through your body. There is a touch of something about her gaze that is not of this realm.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|[Player], young aspirant. What brings you to this vaslir of House Varros?}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Does your ambition lead you towards the path of the vaslir?}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|All Airtrist must have ambition if they wish to survive, let alone thrive. We are not like zor'thez cousins, content to frolic in their woods or sit pompously on their mountain.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Naiyth shows you a macabre smile.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|As you have yourself, it is kill or be killed.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|The work of House Varros can break a lesser mind. Let's put you to a little test.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|There are many species of fungi here in the Deep. I seek a specific kind. Do you think you could find a patch for me? Or is that task beneath you?}}
{{Chat|say|I can find a patch}}
{{Faction|House Varros|+}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Excellent. Those oafs in House Vael'Xirith might care only about your prowess in battle, but in House Varros, we value mental strength.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Those with weak minds soon find themselves unraveled by the dark realms that we explore.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Here's a test of your perspicacity. There's a book on the shelves next to me, Thelyen's Encyclopedia. It is the most complete compendium of the flora of the Deep. Find the page on Vhelzzil's Vow and tell me what power causes these mushrooms to grow.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Go on—look at the bookshelf and open the encyclopedia.}}
(you need to do "/open encyclopedia" after looking at the bookshelf behind her)

{{Emote|You page through to the entry for Vhelzzil's Vow. It contains a sketch of the mushroom and a detailed description of its appearance. The passage also explains that these mushrooms feed on the remains of beings that were once animated by necromancy. The mushrooms take about a week to appear on the remains of the undead.}}
{{Chat|say|necromancy}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|House Varros|+}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Naiyth gives you the first genuinely warm smile you have seen from her.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Indeed. This particular species is nourished by the necromantic energies that linger after an undead body has been disanimated.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|The anarchic wilds beyond the walls of the Foreign Quarter are rife with walking skeletons that have been dispatched by ambitious young Airtrist such as yourself.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Naiyth|Go there and find remains old enough for Vhelzzil's Vow to have sprouted. Put a handful of the mushrooms in this pouch and bring it back to me.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Naiyth's Mushroom Pouch]] from Vaslir Naiyth.}}

Collect the mushrooms from the fallen skeleton corpse in the noob yard under that big lit mushroom. /inspect /search and /take mushroom

Next, she tells you to go collect a "special corpse"
Head out to the noob area and go south like you did when you mined the rocks; go a bit past, and you will find a "Mournful Outcast" (not the Wrathful Outcast, I think that's the SK one, keep going past him, the Mournful Outcast is a little further down). Kill the Mournful Outcast; they will drop a corpse item. Take this back to her.

Last part: once you hand in the corpse, she will give you those dried mushrooms you just picked for her. She will hand you a mortar and pestle; grind the mushrooms twice (the first time is coarse, the second is fine). She wants them finely ground. Then return the mortar and pestle, along with the finely ground mushrooms, and you're done. Welcome to House Varros. Here are your introductory letter to Vaslir Vharkith, and a slightly used, but washed set of white robes; now get out.

'''You can now cross the bridge into the city without getting killed by the guards.'''

=== Part 2 ===

{{QuestNote| [[Vaslir Vharkith]] is located near the top of [[Ail'Vorith]] proper, next to some other Vaslir NPCs.}}
Hand in the note to Vaslir Vharkith.

Note: To find this guy, from the FQ, run across the bridge into the city proper. Turn right inside the city gates, go down until you see the bank. Face the bank entrance. Behind you is a large vaulted tunnel opening that leads to the city's interior (docks area); go through it. At the end of the tunnel, turn right and stop. On your right is a building with a teleporter. The ramp is a few steps down the walk; it's dark, and the ramp is easy to miss. Take the teleporter up. Once up top, you will see the octagonal castle-looking place as you walk out of the teleporter building. Turn and look over your right shoulder, and there is a steep incline. Go up. Once that levels off, another ledge and buildings are just in front of you. Vharkith is up there. There are two ramps, left and right; pick your path, head up top there, and smack him in the mouth with that letter. Let him know he sucks for wasting 8 hrs of my life walking around the city looking for him.

{{Exp}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith tosses the letter aside without reading it. He speaks in a nasally drawl.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Hmm... another hopeful apprentice, is it? Excellent, that last fool Naiyth sent me got herself torn apart by elementals. Or was it vivisected by deep gnomes? It's hard to tell one apprentice from another.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|So let's see what we have to work with.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith looks you up and down with disinterested disdain.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Well you're a weak looking thing. Do you believe one such as yourself can be of service to me, a vaslir who has dared to speak the Winding Words only to come out stronger?}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Hmm... so you know how to cleave yourself to power. Good. There may be some honor in helping your ascent. But if you want the patronage of the great Vaslir Vharkith, you will need to prove you are more than just a good judge of character. Let's see how far that ambition can take you.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|How would you feel about a little quid pro quo? And in the process we will test your mettle a bit.}}
{{Chat|say|mettle}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Good. I had a slave, a young Faelewyn, who was going to be used in a summoning. Ah, I had the most exquisite excruciation planned for him: it would have been perfect!}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Sadly, the creature proved uncommonly clever and escaped while I was at a seminar hosted by the neth'vaslir himself.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith grins at you smugly.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Yes, I am a student of the immortal head of our house himself! Now you are realizing just how beneficial it will be for you to serve one with my connections.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|To that end, you shall find this escaped slave. Don't bother bringing him back alive. The requisite conjunction for the summoning has passed.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith makes a gesture of acceptance and then straightens his robe.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|However, there is the matter of some notes which that zor'thez stole from me. Reports are that he was headed towards the Great Cavern Sea. Find him and bring the notes back to me.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Do this and you shall have earned my patronage. Hunt well, young one!}}

==== Find the Escaped Slave ====

The escaped Faelewyn slave [[Vaslir Vharkith]] is referring to is [[Laeran Birchshade]], a male Wood Elf found near the [[Great Cavern Sea]].

'''Directions to Laeran Birchshade:'''

From the entrance to the area, travel south toward the [[Great Cavern Sea]], passing the cultists and continuing toward the waterfall.

Once near the Great Cavern Sea, keep the cavern wall on your '''left''' and continue following it. Invisible Deepgulp Goblins can be encountered along this route.

Continue following the wall until you see a small island with [[Laeran Birchshade]] standing on it.

'''Warning:''' There is an invisible '''Thug''' near Laeran which is KOS and may attack unexpectedly. [[See Invisibility]] is recommended while approaching the island if available.

{{QuestNote|Although [[Laeran Birchshade]] cons as "Ready to attack", he does not attack on sight. He may either be killed for [[Vharkith's Research Notes]] or spoken with instead. Speaking with him also begins a separate optional quest involving the [[Birchshade Family Bracelet]]. See [[Laeran Birchshade]] for details.}}

Obtain [[Vharkith's Research Notes]] from [[Laeran Birchshade]] and return them to [[Vaslir Vharkith]].

=== Part 3 ===

Return [[Vharkith's Research Notes]] to [[Vaslir Vharkith]].

{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|My research!}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith grabs the pages from you greedily.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Senior was sure you'd get yourself killed like the others.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith begins looking over his newly recovered notes.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Now, I don't suppose you know what essairyl is? Of course you don't. You'll have to start knowing these things if you expect to become a senior apprentice. Run along to Vaslir Maryn and tell her I need another flask of it.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Give her this in exchange.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive a bag of [[Corpse Dust]] from [[Vaslir Vharkith]].}}

==== Speak with Vaslir Maryn ====

Take the [[Corpse Dust]] to [[Vaslir Maryn]].

{{QuestNote|[[Vaslir Maryn]] is located near [[Vaslir Vharkith]] in the upper area of [[Ail'Vorith]], standing beside the large fountain. [[Vaslir Kiannes]] is also located nearby.}}

{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|Karzzul, apprentice. I trust you have a good reason for interrupting my research?}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|Corpse dust, is it? I assume that means the idiot sent you and that he needs more essairyl.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|I'm afraid I used up the last of my stock on yesterday's binding.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|You'll have to talk to Vaslir Kiannes... unless you feel like gathering more essences for me.}}

{{QuestNote|At this point there are '''two confirmed routes''' for obtaining [[Flask of Essairyl]]. You may gather elemental essences for [[Vaslir Maryn]], or speak with [[Vaslir Kiannes]] and complete his water-sample task instead. You only need to complete one route.}}

==== Route A: Gather Essences for Vaslir Maryn ====

Continue speaking with [[Vaslir Maryn]] about the essences.

{{Chat|say|I will gather essences for you.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|Yes, we elaborate essairyl from the essences left behind when an elemental is destroyed.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|If you wish to hone your skills somewhat, I suggest traveling beyond the walls of the city and hunting down elementals in the southern part of this cavern. A rogue group of summoners has established a presence there. The type of elementals they are summoning are ideal sources of reagents.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|Kill them and harvest four air and four earth essences. Give them to me along with the corpse dust.}}

===== Gather the Elemental Essences =====

You need to collect:

* 4 [[Essence of Elemental Air]]
* 4 [[Essence of Elemental Earth]]

{{QuestNote|Only the '''Air''' and '''Earth''' elementals are needed for this step. Water elementals can also be found around the shores near Ail'Vorith proper, but they do not provide the essences Maryn requests.}}

'''Directions to the elementals:'''

Travel toward the bridge leading into [[Ail'Vorith]] proper.

At the bridge, before you go across to [[Ail'Vorith]] proper, turn '''left/south''' and follow the path which leads toward [[Miral the Dark Elf]], then jump down into the moat/water. Swim in the direction Miral is facing toward the '''southern wall of the cavern'''.

Continue along the south side of the cavern heading west along the southern wall. Air and Earth elementals can be found in this area, along with ghosts and other creatures.

Kill Air and Earth elementals until you have collected '''four [[Essence of Elemental Air]]''' and '''four [[Essence of Elemental Earth]]'''.

{{QuestNote|There are also Water elementals along the shoreline surrounding the city. Make sure you are hunting '''Air Elementals''' and '''Earth Elementals''' for this quest.}}

===== Return to Vaslir Maryn =====

Return to [[Vaslir Maryn]] with:

* 4 [[Essence of Elemental Air]]
* 4 [[Essence of Elemental Earth]]
* the [[Corpse Dust]] given to you by [[Vaslir Vharkith]]

Hand the essences and [[Corpse Dust]] to Vaslir Maryn.

{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|You return with the essences. That is a welcome surprise, although competence while in the service of the idiot may not work in your favor.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Maryn begins feeding the essences into a series of tubes and glass receptacles. After some time she fills a flask with a silvery liquid and hands it to you.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|You are a promising young elementalist. In the future, should you desire to work for a competent instructor, you know where my laboratory is.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Maryn|May you hear, kulzzan.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Flask of Essairyl]] from [[Vaslir Maryn]].}}

==== Route B: Earn Essairyl from Vaslir Kiannes ====

Instead of gathering elemental essences for [[Vaslir Maryn]], speak with [[Vaslir Kiannes]].

{{QuestNote|[[Vaslir Kiannes]] is located near [[Vaslir Maryn]] and [[Vaslir Vharkith]] in the upper area of [[Ail'Vorith]], near the fountain.}}

{{Chat|say|Hail, Vaslir Kiannes.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|Karzzul, varsa ai Neth'xan! What brings you to me today?}}
{{Chat|say|Can you help me get essairyl?}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|You want essairyl? I need it for my bindings, and you are obviously not ready to perform a binding of your own.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Kiannes laughs heartily.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|I assume you are one of our dear Vharkith's pawns. He's always sending you poor fellows to ask for the fruits of our labor. I assume you are hoping to trade us some corpse dust for the essairyl, as usual.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Kiannes makes a disapproving sound in his throat.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|Well, I'm afraid my price has gone up. If you want to please your master, you'll have to earn my essairyl.}}
{{Chat|say|I will earn it.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|There are a group of deep gnomes near the northern edge of our great cavern. They are conducting experiments on the impurities in the water there.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Kiannes nods his head approvingly.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|Industrious little fellows. Almost a shame to dispose of them. Quite useful, they can be. Yes, indeed. Quite useful.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|But research needs as they say. Research needs. Bring me some of their water samples. Ten should be enough for my current project.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|Give me the samples along with the corpse dust, and you'll have your essairyl.}}

===== Gather the Water Samples =====

Travel toward the '''northern edge of the Great Cavern''' and locate the deep gnomes conducting experiments on the water.

You need to collect:

* 10 [[Sample of Tainted Water]]
* [[Corpse Dust]]

{{QuestNote|This is an alternative to gathering [[Essence of Elemental Air]] and [[Essence of Elemental Earth]] for [[Vaslir Maryn]]. You do '''not''' need to complete both routes.}}

Once you have collected ten water samples, return to [[Vaslir Kiannes]] with the [[Sample of Tainted Water]] and the [[Corpse Dust]].

{{exp}}
{{Faction|House Varros|+}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Kiannes uncorks one of the sample vials, takes a dropper from a nearby flask of red liquid, and adds a bit to the sample.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Kiannes swishes the vial and watches intently as the red drops become a blue swirl.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|Fascinating. This may be useful indeed.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Kiannes turns back to you with a satisfied chuckle.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Kiannes|Here is a vial of essairyl as promised, my dear gnome slayer.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Flask of Essairyl]] from [[Vaslir Kiannes]].}}

=== Part 4 ===

==== Obtain a Bottle of Nerolir ====

After obtaining the [[Flask of Essairyl]] from either [[Vaslir Maryn]] or [[Vaslir Kiannes]], return it to [[Vaslir Vharkith]].

Hand the [[Flask of Essairyl]] to [[Vaslir Vharkith]].

{{exp}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith looks annoyed.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|I don't know what took you so long. Next time I give you a task, I expect you to focus on that task alone. You've probably been wasting my time getting drunk in the Veiled Door with the other apprentices.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Speaking of which, now that I have the essairyl, I need a good source of malic acid. Nerolir, an elven cider, has the perfect level of acidity for what I have in mind. As with most things elven, it is banned in the city, but you can sometimes find it in the Foreign Quarter. Go get me a bottle.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Don't bother me again until you have some.}}

===== Ask Nyxia Ak'kin About Nerolir =====

Travel to [[Nyxia Ak'kin]] in the Foreign Quarter bar.

{{Chat|say|Hail, Nyxia Ak'Kin}}
{{Chat|Nyxia Ak'Kin|What's your poison?}}
{{Chat|say|Have any Nerolir?}}
{{Chat|Nyxia Ak'Kin|Nerolir? That fancy elven swill from up top? Don't have any. Not much call for such things with this clientele.}}
{{Emote|Nyxia Ak'Kin thinks for a moment.}}
{{Chat|Nyxia Ak'Kin|The dark elf might have some.}}

===== Purchase Nerolir from Miral =====

Travel to [[Miral the Dark Elf]] on the west side of the Foreign Quarter overlooking the water.

{{Chat|say|Hail, Miral the Dark Elf}}
{{Chat|Miral the Dark Elf|Karzzul. You another bounty hunter or you looking to volunteer?}}
{{Chat|say|I'm looking for some Nerolir}}
{{Chat|Miral the Dark Elf|Ah you heard about the raid, I take it? That was a fun one. Caught the fools flat footed heading towards the Bight.}}
{{Chat|Miral the Dark Elf|I did snag a crate of Nerolir from them. Price is 10 silver a bottle.}}

Give [[Miral the Dark Elf]] 10 silver.

{{Chat|Miral the Dark Elf|Enjoy. One of the only things I miss from home.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Bottle of Nerolir]] from [[Miral the Dark Elf]].}}

===== Return the Bottle of Nerolir to Vaslir Vharkith =====

Return to [[Vaslir Vharkith]] and give him the [[Bottle of Nerolir]].

{{exp}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith snatches the bottle out of your hand.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Warsa ai neth'zan, a competent apprentice! And about time. Senior isn't back from the errand I sent him on, which probably means he got himself killed as usual.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|So, I need you to pick up where he left off. I've sent for a special order from Night Harbor. No human nirsavh can match the skill of an Ail'trist elementalist, of course, even with the pathetic examples we currently have at our disposal.}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith shudders.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Getting killed by the object of your own summoning. What an embarrassment!}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Anyway, my point is that inadequate as they may be, our elementalists are superior to those in Night Harbor in all ways save one: the humans are removed from the politics of our house.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|And that is important when discretion is needed. Therefore, you will go to Night Harbor. Find an elementalist in the Underdocks named Freysia Riftrend. Give her this note. And bring me back my package.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Letter to Freysia Riftrend]] from [[Vaslir Vharkith]].}}

The next assignment requires traveling to the [[Underdocks]] and delivering the letter to [[Freysia Riftrend]] to collect Vharkith's package.

=== Part 5 ===

==== Deliver the Letter to Freysia Riftrend ====

After completing the Nerolir task in Part 4, take the [[Letter to Freysia Riftrend]] from [[Vaslir Vharkith]] to the [[Underdocks]] in [[Night Harbor]].

Travel to the eastern Underdocks in [[Night Harbor]].

[[Freysia Riftrend]] is located in the east Underdocks and is accompanied by her Fire Elemental.

Hand [[Letter to Freysia Riftrend]] to [[Freysia Riftrend]].

{{QuestNote|Handing the [[Letter to Freysia Riftrend]] to Freysia does not award experience or faction.}}

{{Chat|Freysia Riftrend|Varkith sent you, did he? I'll tell you the same thing I told his last messenger. I don't have his order. If you want it for your master, you'll have to retrieve it yourself.}}
{{Chat|say|Where is his order?}}
{{Chat|Freysia Riftrend|One of our number, an elementalist named Belot, betrayed us to the Deepcut bandits and got several of her brethren killed. She also absconded with several valuable items including the package for your master.}}
{{Emote|Freysia Riftrend crosses her arms.}}
{{Chat|Freysia Riftrend|Now, the Descendian Order are mercenaries. I can't be sending our lads out to fight for free, but I also can't have the word getting out that you can double cross us.}}
{{Chat|Freysia Riftrend|So maybe we can help each other. The scuttlebutt is that Belot is holed up at one of the Deepcut Bandit camps... or maybe in the mines behind them. If you put down enough of them, you should find her. Once that treacherous little snake is dead, we save face and you get your master's package.}}
{{Chat|say|Where are the bandits?}}
{{Chat|Freysia Riftrend|Go out that big gate that the ships use and head into the caverns to your right, if you go in far enough, the place is lousy with them.}}

==== Retrieve Vharkith's Order ====

Leave the east Underdocks through the large gate used by the ships.

Head into the caverns to the right and fight Deepcut bandits until you locate [[Belot]].

Kill [[Belot]] and recover:

* [[Vharkith's Order]]

{{NeedsInfo}}

{{QuestNote|Belot's exact location, level, NPC class, spawn conditions, and complete loot table still need to be documented. It should also be confirmed whether [[Vharkith's Order]] is a guaranteed drop.}}

==== Return Vharkith's Order ====

Return [[Vharkith's Order]] to [[Vaslir Vharkith]] in [[Ail'Vorith]].

{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|My order! At last!}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith is practically hopping with excitement.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Varsa ai Neth'xan! You have finally lived up to my expectations, Senior. Yes, that's right. Since you completed Senior's task, you are now my new senior apprentice. If the old one should somehow find his way back here, you may do with him as you will.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|I don't have any more senior apprentice robes, so you'll have to find one for yourself. I mean really, I can't believe I was only given 20! How am I supposed to make do with only 20 robes when apprentices die so often?}}
{{Emote|Vaslir Vharkith shakes his head in disgust.}}
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Yet another thing I'll have to straighten out when I am in charge. For now, I must attend to my research. Come back later, and I'll have another task for you.}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|House Varros|+}}

{{QuestNote|Vaslir Vharkith promotes you to senior apprentice, but does not provide senior apprentice robes. To obtain the robe worn by his former senior apprentice, see Part 6 below.}}

After completing Part 5, hail [[Vaslir Vharkith]] again.

{{Chat|say|Hail, Vaslir Vharkith.}} <!-- Original chat channel: Deep Common -->
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Karzzul, Senior. I am still busy with my project. Return to me later.}}

=== Part 6 ===

==== Take Your Rightful Place as Senior Apprentice ====

'''Time to get your senior apprentice robe. 😈'''

After returning [[Vharkith's Order]] in Part 5, [[Vaslir Vharkith]] promotes you as his new senior apprentice but provides no robe. He explains that he has run out of senior apprentice robes and says that if his previous senior apprentice ever returns, you may do with him as you will.

The missing apprentice is [[Senior Apprentice Syrsil]], who is still alive in the [[Underdocks]]. Players can obtain the [[House Varros Senior Apprentice Robe]] by defeating Syrsil and looting it. This is a separate loot acquisition rather than an item automatically awarded when Vharkith promotes you.

{{QuestNote|'''Deep Elf robe:''' The [[House Varros Senior Apprentice Robe]] is restricted to Deep Elves (DEF). The robe can be pursued without completing the earlier House Varros assignments; Parts 1–5 explain the story and the player's promotion, but no quest-completion flag has been verified as necessary to loot the robe.}}

==== Find the Former Senior Apprentice ====

Travel to the [[Underdocks]] Citadel. [[Senior Apprentice Syrsil]] stands in the tavern inside the inn, one floor below [[Innkeeper Adrella]] and one floor above the guest rooms.

Syrsil is the missing senior apprentice mentioned by Vharkith. Speaking to him reveals that Vharkith sent him to retrieve an order from the Descendian Order and that [[Belot]] stole the package. Syrsil is unable to fight through the Deepcut bandits or afford help.

More importantly, he admits he hired an assassin against a junior apprentice who seemed too capable, hoping to protect his position within House Varros.

{{Chat|say|assassin}}
{{Chat|Senior Apprentice Syrsil|In Ail'vorith I am the senior apprentice to Vaslir Vharkith of House Varros. The junior apprentice was a little too competent, so I hired someone to nip that problem in the bud. Cannot have any upstarts coveting my position.}}
{{Chat|Senior Apprentice Syrsil|In hindsight, I should have just killed the newcomer myself, but I was trying to do things the right way and maintain deniability.}}
{{Emote|Senior Apprentice Syrsil grimaces.}}

{{QuestNote|See [[Syrsil's Stolen Package]] for the full documented conversation and the complete dialogue tree, which includes '''problems''', '''curse''', '''packages''', '''bandits''', '''assassin''', '''help''', '''Ail'vorith''', and '''House Varros''' keywords.}}

==== Choose: Help Syrsil or Claim His Robe ====

'''Help Syrsil:''' Players who wish to assist Syrsil can give him [[Vharkith's Order]], as detailed in [[Syrsil's Stolen Package]]. This hand-in rewards experience and improved House Varros faction but does '''not''' award the senior apprentice robe. It provides a separate use for the package and can be pursued by players who do not intend to take the robe.

{{exp}}
{{Faction|House Varros|+}}

'''Claim your robe:''' For the Deep Elf senior apprentice, defeat [[Senior Apprentice Syrsil]] and loot the [[House Varros Senior Apprentice Robe]] from his corpse. This is how the robe is obtained, rather than receiving it from Vharkith at the end of Part 5.

{{QuestNote|'''Faction and nearby NPCs:''' During the recorded encounter, killing Syrsil did not decrease faction, and the other tavern occupants did not attack in response. Syrsil and nearby NPCs can nevertheless be dangerous in combat. These observations do not establish that every possible pull or combat situation is safe.}}

Vharkith has already given you the rank of senior apprentice. With the former senior apprentice defeated and his robe obtained, you can now dress the part as well.

'''The old senior apprentice had his chance. Now the robes are yours.''' 😈

==== Quest Status After Promotion ====

After completing Parts 5 and 6, hail [[Vaslir Vharkith]] again.<br>
{{Chat|say|Hail, Vaslir Vharkith.}} 
{{Chat|Vaslir Vharkith|Karzzul, Senior. I am still busy with my project. Return to me later.}}

{{Chat|say|What Robe?.}}<!-- Original chat channel: Deep Common -->
{{Chat|Vawslir Vharkith|"Exactly. The Shadow rewards those who take initiative. Especially ruthless initiative. Now get going. I'm sure if you put your mind to it, you can think of someone who might have a robe that would look better on you.}}
In the Underdocks, there is a Deep Elf in the tavern on the NH side of the city named [[Senior Apprentice Syrsil]]. Killing him changes no factions, and he drops [[House Varros Senior Apprentice Robe]]. Handing the robe to [[Vaslir Vharkith]]  at level 15 results in the item being returned, saying he does not want those items. Maybe wearing it and hailing? 

{{QuestNote|'''Quest Progression Status (October 27, 2026):''' At level 32 with '''Amicable''' House Varros faction, Vharkith did not offer another assignment after the promotion to senior apprentice. The robe can be obtained from Syrsil independently of this dialogue. Whether Vharkith has any additional quest unlocked by a higher level, higher faction, or another prerequisite remains unknown.}}

