== Walkthrough ==
{{QuestNote|This quest starts at the conclusion of the [[Ail'Vorith Starter Quest]] after you receive your [[Obsidian Shackle]].}}

=== Part 1 - Goblin Scalps ===
{{QuestNote|Laren is located in the Military Outpost with the melee class instructors. From the bridge and gate into the Foreign Quarter, enter the building across, second on the left (not the bank tunnel). He is on the right, near back of the room.}}

{{Chat|say|Hail, Laren Drin'dar.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|Few may join the ranks of the Eternal Martyrs. Have you some skill with blade or bow?}}
{{Chat|say|I definitely have skill with bow!|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|Every soldier must be ready for the day when all the Ail'trist are called to war.}}
{{Emote|Laren Drin'dar considers you for a moment.}}
{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|The lesser houses diminish our people by clinging to their fruitless names and petty holdings. If you can prove yourself a true Archer of the Ail'trist once more, I will grant you leave to enter the city as a conscript of House Vael'xirith.}}
{{Chat|say|I will prove myself!|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|I would not take you into battle today, were the Enemy at the gate. But every capable soldier will be needed in the days to come.}}
{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|Goblins infest the reaches of the Deep. Look for their breeding grounds in the east. Bring me the scalps of their young, enough to fill this pouch.}}

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Scalp Pouch]] from Laren Drin'dar.}}
{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|Do not underestimate them.}}


{{QuestNote|Go kill a bunch of goblins and return.}}


You begin crafting Pouch of Goblin Scalps.<br>
<span style="font-weight:bold;color:#FF0000;">Scalp Pouch is consumed while crafting.</span>
{{ReceiveItem|You craft [[Pouch of Goblin Scalps]].}}

{{exp}}
{{Faction|House Vael'xirith|+}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Ail'Vorith|+}}

{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|Ah, a pleasant sight. You have proven to me that you can wield a weapon, and that is more than can be said of many.  If you will pledge your fealty to the high lord, Ral Vael'xirith, you may be permitted to enter the city among our ranks, though you will hold no rank or title until it is earned.}}
{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|Will you pledge to serve the great house of Vael'xirith?}}
{{Chat|say|I pledge to serve.|Deep Common}}

{{exp}}
{{Faction|House Vael'xirith|+}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Ail'Vorith|+}}

{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|It is a sacred oath, Player.  When you are called to serve, you shall have a chance to prove your mettle.  Until then, you may wear this tunic, which was worn by one who fell in battle.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Bloodied Chainmail]] from [[Laren Drin'dar]].}}

'''You can now cross the bridge into the city without getting killed by the guards.'''

=== Part 2 - Lvl 14+ ===
{{Chat|say|Hail, Laren Drin'dar.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Laren Drin'dar|You have not seen enough battles, Ranger.  Return when you are stronger and you may be of further service to House Vael'xirith.}}

When level 14+, continues with [[Stolen Gems]].

