== Reward Notes ==
*[[Lexicon of Mysteries]] -> [[Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries]] -> [[Advanced Lexicon of Mysteries]]
*Faction with House of Drezzorith increased to High Indifferent
*Faction with Citizens of Ail'vorith increased to High Amicably
*Access to the city (Update 0.30.0.0)

== Walkthrough ==
{{QuestNote|This quest starts at the conclusion of the [[Ail'Vorith Starter Quest]] after you receive your [[Obsidian Shackle]].}}

=== House Acceptance ===

{{QuestNote|[[Zalethra Drezzorith]] is located in the Obsidian Academy upper floor. From the bridge and gate into the Foreign Quarter, enter the building straight ahead with caster trainers and go upstairs.}}

{{Chat|say|Hail, Zalethra Drezzorith.|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Power and strength, directly leads to standing.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|We may be here serving the Shadow and Gods, but it's politics that moves this place.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Our House is the one that unites Ail'vorith with its beliefs. While we follow the Queen, our dedication lies with the dark gods.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Your shadow is dim, all but extinguished, exiled from a lesser house that was like a flea on a dog's back. Show me your mettle. Solve a minor problem I am dealing with and I will look upon you favorably.}}
{{Chat|say|What problem?|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Some castaways, like yourself, deemed themselves important.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Started assembling and gathering arms. Chanting throughout the day and night, praying to lost gods.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|To find them, cross the bridge to exit the Foreign Quarter.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|From there, turn right and head down the shoreline.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Head past the sporelings and you will find a cave. And within that cave these miscreants.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Strike down these upstart cultists. Show no mercy.  Bring me their flesh. Fill this bag with their eyes.  You can keep their tears.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Do this or die trying. It matters not to me or my House.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Small Burlap Pouch]] from [[Zalethra Drezzorith]].}}
{{QuestNote|Cross the bridge and turn right at the Toilmaster. Follow the water's edge until your reach a cave full of cultists.  Kill [[an angry cultist]], [[an agitated cultist]], [[a cultist priestess]] to collect 7 [[Cultist Eye]] to fill the bag.}}
{{QuestNote|Combine the container into [[Filled Burlap Pouch]] and return it to [[Zalethra Drezzorith]].}}
{{Emote|Zalethra Drezzorith cackles wickedly with delight.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Not bad for an outcast.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|You are new in your faith so I would like to present this book to you for further study.}}
{{Chat|Zalethra Drezzorith|Take this letter and scurry along to House Drezzorith. May the gods provide strength and ruthlessness to your actions.}}

{{exp}}

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Lexicon of Mysteries]] from [[Zalethra Drezzorith]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Letter for Alarys]] from [[Zalethra Drezzorith]].}}
{{Faction|House of Drezzorith|+}}
{{Faction|Citizens of Ail'vorith|+}}
{{QuestInfo|Faction with [[House of Drezzorith]] increased to High Indifferent}}
{{QuestInfo|Faction with [[Citizens of Ail'vorith]] increased to High Amicably}}

=== Goblin Samples ===

{{QuestNote|[[Alarys Drezzorith]] is located in a building in the main city of [[Ail'Vorith]], 4th floor, south side... just southeast of the high level Paladin and Cleric trainers.  You can see it on the left side standing on the main bridge leading into the city.}}

{|cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="border: 1px solid gray; max-width: 500px;" width="100%"
|-
|style="background:#F5F0E8;padding:10px;"|
[[File:alarys_location.jpg|right|border|600px]]<br>
|}

{{QuestNote|Hand [[Alarys Drezzorith]] your [[Letter to Alarys]].}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|You've seem to have impressed Zalethra with your dealings against the cultist uprising.}}
{{Emote|Alarys Drezzorith looks at you coldly.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Our house and it's members are of high value in this city.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|We help and heal the militia, lead the masses to their gods, and coax others on their journey to the Shadow.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|My lord holds dominion over subjugation. The act of bending others to your will.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|I have a task. Are you interested?}}
{{Chat|say|I am interested!|Deep Common}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|There is a band of Deep Gnomes, across the bridge, conducting experiments on goblins.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Reports indicate that they are utilizing secretions from the fungus men on goblin suubjects.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|This leads to hallucinations, weakening of will, and eventual domination.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Seek them out. Gather samples of this concoction.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Bring them back to me in this box that will hold the samples.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Empty Sample Box]] from [[Alarys Drezzorith]].}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|I do not care how you acquire them.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Through guile, deception or outright violence. It matters not to me or our house.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Go and remember who your serve.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|For in remembering, you may yet survive for a time longer.}}

{{QuestNote|Kill [[a Deepgulp warrior]], [[a Deepgulp scavenger]], [[a Deepgulp hunter]], [[a Deepgulp berserker]] to collect 6 [[Sample of Mind Control Substance]] and combine them to create [[Full Sample Box]].}}
{{QuestNote|(Alternately, you can complete the [[Thanetal's Samples]] quest handing in 1 Deep Ale and 10 silver to acquire 6 [[Sample of Mind Control Substance]].)}}
{{QuestNote|Hand [[Full Sample Box]] to [[Alarys Drezzorith]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Any faction hits? EXP?}}
{{Emote|Alarys Drezzorith looks at you intently.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|I am surprised that you have returned. And so soon.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Excellent. Our alchemists can now analyze this mixture and improve upon it.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|You have done well for a small, insignificant thing.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Continue to work hard and your standing may improve.}}
{{Emote|Alarys Drezzorith calls for a runner. He hands them a box and you hear him whisper something about House Xal'tharn into their ear.}}
{{Emote|Alarys Drezzorith nods in your direction.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Hand me your prayer book so that I may update it.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand [[Lexicon of Mysteries]] to [[Alarys Drezzorith]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries]] from [[Alarys Drezzorith]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Any faction hits? EXP?}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|I'd like to introduce you to our benefactor. His name is [[Tal Drezzorith]].}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|If you offend him in any way, he will snuff you like a fly.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|Seek him out and make yourself known.}}

== Continuation - Part 2 ==

{{QuestNote|[[Tal Drezzorith]] is located in the building next to Alarys Drezzorith, directly across from the cleric/paladin guild}}
{{QuestNote| Hand the [[Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries]] in to [[Tal Drezzorith]].}}
{{Emote|Alarys Drezzorith receives your book, flips to a page and writes down several items.}}
{{Chat|Alarys Drezzorith|I would like you to report to [[Marshal Xyvher]] for your next assignment.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Advanced Lexicon of Mysteries]] from [[Tal Drezzorith]].}}


{{QuestInfo|Any follow-up breadcrumbs?}}

House Velgarrith (Quest).content:
{{NeedsInfo}}
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = phicon.png
| width             = 100px
| caption           = Placeholder Image
|Start Zone         = [[Ail'Vorith]]
|Quest Giver        = [[Xilonen Velgarrith]]
|Minimum Level      = 1
|Classes            = SHD
|Related NPCs       = [[Cook Vashuk]];[[Kulzzara]]; [[Supplier Jul]];[[juvenile shark]];[[Vhalrek Velgarrith]]
}}

=== Rewards ===
* Shadow Knight - [[Frayed Cloak of House Velgarrith]]
* Faction with [[House Velgarrith]].

=== Related Items ===
* [[Cracked Shell]]
* [[Rusted Cleaver]]
* [[Shoddy Dagger]]
* [[Spool of Spider Silk]]
* [[juvenile shark fin]]
* [[Dark Note]] ?

== Walkthrough ==
{{QuestNote|This quest starts at the conclusion of the [[Ail'Vorith Starter Quest]] after you receive your [[Obsidian Shackle]].}}

=== Part 1 - Req. Lvl 2 ===
{{QuestNote|[[Xilonen Velgarrith]] is located upstairs in the martial trainer building}}
{{chat|say|Hail, Xilonen Velgarrith.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|<player>. Looking to become an exile no longer?}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|The House Velgarrith can give you that chance, so long as you’re willing to prove yourself.}}
{{chat|say|Prove myself.}}
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith grins wide, revealing a set of charred black teeth}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Eager, are we? Good.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|As you’ve no doubt noticed, House Velgarrith is the only reason exiles like yourself are even given the chance to regain your former shadow.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|We are the Hand of the Deep. A hand that is not afraid to dirty itself, so long as we can profit from it. That includes manipulating and dealing with the x’arana; the lesser races.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|To that end, I’m going to give you a little test.}}
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith pulls out a plain-looking shell that carries a soft, luminescent interior. He tosses it over to you.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|You ready?}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Cracked Shell]] from Xilonen Velgarrith.}}

{{chat|say|I am ready.}}
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith grins.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Good.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Your goal is to turn that useless shell into something worth at least one whole silver piece. Not an impossible task for someone shrewd and competent.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Travel the foreign quarter and find a merchant who's willing to take or trade that worthless shell in exchange for something of more value.}}
{{QuestNote|You do not need to return to Xilonen after each trade. Just move to the next person and return to Xilonen once you have the thread.}}

== Take the cracked shell to Cook Vashuk. ==

{{emote|Cook Vashuk inspects the shell with one eye much larger than the other.}}
{{chat|Cook Vashuk|Splendid! Such fine luster! Fit for the Queen in all Her glory!}}
{{chat|Cook Vashuk|What do I have to trade for such a fine piece? Hmm. Ah!}}
{{emote|Cook Vashuk grabs an old, rusted cleaver and offers it to you.}}
{{chat|Cook Vashuk|A fine blade to pay for such a fine shell. The Shadow blesses me this day!}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Rusted Cleaver]] from Cook Vashuk.}}
{{QuestNote|Take the [[Rusted Cleaver]] and hand it in to Xilonen Velgarrith.}}
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith narrows his eyes.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|You think this is worth at least one silver piece? Not even close, exile.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|You're going to need to try harder than that to earn a profit around here. Or maybe you're just not Velgarrith material.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from Xilonen Velgarrith.}}

== Take the rusted cleaver to Kulzzara ==

{{emote|Kulzzara inspects the cleaver with a look of disgust.}}
{{chat|Kulzzara|Where did you find this hunk of scrap? Listen, I can tell that you're desperate, so I'll cut you a deal.}}
{{emote|Kulzzara produces a shoddy dagger which she offers to you.}}
{{chat|Kulzzara|A client dropped this off earlier. Apparently the blade is hot, meaning it was recently used in an assassination.}}
{{chat|Kulzzara|I don't want Xal'tharn inspectors breathing down my neck about it, so it's all yours and no longer my problem.}}
{{chat|Kulzzara|Now get lost!}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Shoddy Dagger]] from Kulzzara.}}
{{QuestNote|Take the [[Shoddy Dagger]] and hand it in to Xilonen Velgarrith.}}
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith spins the dagger on a finger and then hands it back to you.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Not quite there yet, exile. I'd say it might be worth half a silver on the best of days. I'm sure that you can do better.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from Xilonen Velgarrith.}}

== Take the shoddy dagger to Supplier Jul ==
{{emote|Supplier Jul eyes the dagger sharply.}}
{{chat|Supplier Jul|You know what? I think I do have a use for something like that.}}
{{chat|Supplier Jul|Here. In exchange, you can have...}}
{{emote|Supplier Jul produces a spool of spider's silk.}}
{{chat|Supplier Jul|Hard to come by in these parts, but I'm willing to part with it to get my hands on a useful blade right about now.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Spool of Spider Silk]] from Supplier Jul.}}
{{QuestNote|Take the [[Spool of Spider Silk]] and hand it in to Xilonen Velgarrith.}}
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith gauges the silk and offers a begrudging shrug.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Not an impressive haul, but I suppose this does meet the threshold I set for you. If only just.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|I probably shouldn't have expected too much from someone straight out of the quarry, but I think you're still capable enough to be honed into something more potent.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|So with that said, are you ready to move on to the second part of your test?}}
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith grins.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|What, did I forget to mention this was a two-parter?}}
{{Faction|House Velgarrith|+}}
{{chat|say|Move to the second part of the quest.}} (Deep Common)
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith shrugs casually.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|You've shown that you have at least some drive and guile, but the Hand of the Deep must also be able to maintain a firm hold over what is ours.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Velgarrith mercenary forces rival that of any other military, so part two is a much more straightforward one: a test of your combat ability.}}
{{QuestInfo|Do you need to speak Deep Common? And is this the correct way to move to the next part of the quest? More info is needed here.}}

=== PART 2 ===
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Our smugglers have been complaining that the thresher population near the harbors of the foreign quarter have been disrupting their routes.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Show me that you can brave the waters of the Deep and bring me four juvenile thresher fins.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|And try not to become just another floating corpse.}}
{{QuestNote|Kill [[juvenile shark|juvenile sharks]] found in water around the bridge to the Foreign District, and other bridges. Loot 4 [[juvenile shark fin]].}}
{{QuestNote|Hand 4 [[juvenile shark fin]] to Xilonen Velgarrith.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|So it turns out that you both have a brain and a strong arm. Good.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Less vermin disrupting our trade means more profit. I think you'll fit in nicely.}}
{{emote|Xilonen Velgarrith writes out a quick note and hands it over to you.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|Bring this to my cousin, Vhalrek, down in our harbor stronghold. You won't be able to miss his grin.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|If you're going to be part of House Velgarrith, you'll need to learn the tunnels beneath the foreign quarter eventually.}}
{{chat|Xilonen Velgarrith|That will be your next test.}}
{{ReceiveItem| You receive a [[Dark Note]] from Xilonen Velgarrith.}}
{{QuestInfo|Need confirmation if this is the correct item received, as the original posting here did not say.}}

== Find Vhalrek Velgarrith ==
{{QuestNote|Vhalrek Velgarrith is located in the tunnels down below; he is the Shadow Knight skill trainer near the Shadow Knight spell vendor.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand in your [[Dark Note]]. Need confirmation this is the correct name for the item.}}
{{emote|Vhalrek Velgarrith looks over the note and offers a chuckle.}}
{{chat|Vhalrek Velgarrith|My cousin has an eye for talent, or so they say. I suppose I will see for myself soon enough.}}
{{chat|Vhalrek Velgarrith|It seems that your efforts have earned you a position as a low ranking member of our great House Velgarrith.}}
{{chat|Vhalrek Velgarrith|Congratulations, you are an exile no longer.}}
{{chat|Vhalrek Velgarrith|You will wear our colors and as such be one of our representatives, though expect no fanfare if you are to enter the city.}}
{{chat|Vhalrek Velgarrith|Many still view ours as the Bastard House due to our dealings with foreigners.}}
{{emote|Vhalrek Velgarrith smirks and tosses you a bundle containing a purple cloak.}}
{{chat|Vhalrek Velgarrith|It is a moniker we gladly accept, given our strength.}}
{{chat|Vhalrek Velgarrith|Now, I can provide you with instruction if you wish, else you are free to make your own profits for a time.}}
{{chat|Vhalrek Velgarrith|We will have use of you should you stay alive long enough.}}
{{QuestInfo|You can now enter the city proper - guards will con disdain to you.}}
{{QuestInfo|More information is required...}}

