Tig's Measuring Quest.content:
{{NeedsInfo}}
{{HasQuickGuide}}
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = phicon.png
| width             = 100px
| caption           = Placeholder Image
|Start Zone         = [[Sungreet Strand]]
|Quest Giver        = [[Tig Pebblebank]]
|Minimum Level      = 15
|Classes            = All
|Related NPCs       = [[Sproggets Bedsprings]]
|Quest Rewards      = (exp); [[The Measure Stick]]; [[Lead Disk of the Apprentice]]
}}

* Faction gained with [[Congregation of Trem]].
* Faction gained with [[City of Night Harbor]].

== Walkthrough ==
=== Part 1 - Rope for the Job ===

{{QuestNote|You can only engage in the quest dialogue after reaching level 15 or higher.}}
{{QuestNote|You may first find [[Tig Pebblebank]] at the quarry of [[Sungreet Strand]].}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Tig Pebblebank.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|No, Mr. Brookturner. Give me a moment and I'll help you look for it.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank sighs, looking visibly stressed.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|What? Oh! Hi there. I'm Lead Measurer Tig Pebblebank.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|I'm sorry about all that. We've been really behind lately with all the delays.}}
{{Chat|say|What delays?}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Don't get me started. The foreman should have secured the site, and our camp should have been set up days ago.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank shakes her head.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Safety is a high priority for us, we must be allowed to do our delicate work unhindered!}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Now, I must check our equipment and send word to the Church of Trem about what's missing. Someone else will have to take the measurements... there's just too much to do.}}
{{Chat|say|What measurements?}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Part of our charter as representatives of the Measure is to map an exact layout of the quarry. It's a complicated process to complete, but it starts off simple enough.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|First we find the surface area of the plot for the purchase records, then we measure the overall volume to determine how much stone has already been excavated.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|If I weren't so busy, I'd make these measurements myself, but...}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank sighs.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|If only I had an apprentice...}}
{{Chat|say|I am interested in being your apprentice.}}
{{QuestInfo|Note that if you're not level 15, the conversation stops here after a few sentences. Need Dialogue}}
{{QuestNote|If you are level 15+...}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|You're interested? I could field commission you as an apprentice in service of the Measure. It would be an official errand!}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank stares into your eyes intently, as if searching for something.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|There's one condition though... it would require you to take an oath. Are you willing?}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|If so, I'll swear you in and you can get started immediately. You'll be paid, of course, as befitting a junior member of the Measure.}}
{{Chat|say|I am willing.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Good! Then place your hand over your coin purse. Yes, just like so.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank places her hand over her coin purse.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Do you, by the stars that guide us and the sands beneath our feet, under the watchful eye of Trem, god of trade and tradesmen alike, pledge your time and work to the Guild of the Measure?}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Do you promise to chart the unknown with clarity and precision, mark the borders, and endeavor to uncover the secrets of the land?}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Do you vow to uphold the truth in all your measurements, honor the trust placed in you, and serve with diligence and integrity?}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Do you swear, as long as the sun rises and sets, and by the grace of Trem, to remain steadfast and true, to become a beacon of knowledge, and a protective curator of all tools loaned to you for an assigned task?}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank smiles and raises her eyebrows.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|This is the part where you say I do.}}
{{Chat|say|I do.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|With this oath, I bind your spirit to the Measure and the service of Trem, for now and forever, until the terms of your commission have ended.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank presents you with a metal disk.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Lead Disk of the Apprentice]] from [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|This disk represents your apprenticeship with the Measure. You'll make good use of it, I'm sure.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Alright then, that's settled. For your task, I have just about everything you need, with the exception of rope.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Go to Night Harbor and visit the Night Market. There's a general store there owned by Sproggets Bedsprings. Tell him I sent you.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|We need ten hemp ropes at fifty length each. He should have it in stock. Bring me the ropes and we'll get started.}}
{{QuestNote|Travel to [[Night Harbor]] and visit the Night Market. You can find [[Sproggets Bedsprings]] inside one of the building just to the left as you enter the Night Market from West Gate.}}
{{Chat|Sproggets Bedsprings|Heyo! Looking to get into some adventuring? Take a look at my wares.}}
{{Chat|say|Tig Pebblebank sent me.}}
{{Chat|Sproggets Bedsprings|Oh she did, did she? What does she want this time?}}
{{Chat|say|She needs rope.}}
{{Chat|Sproggets Bedsprings|Rope you say. Well, I do have rope for sale, but I'm guessing you're seeking the Guild of the Measurer's standard discount.}}
{{Chat|Sproggets Bedsprings|Fine. Two silver coin and you can have ten ropes of fifty length. I'll even throw in a small field pack to carry them in.}}
{{Chat|Sproggets Bedsprings|Just give me the coin when you're ready. I'll set them aside until you return.}}
{{QuestNote|IMPORTANT - Do NOT purchase the rope from Sproggets. Simply take 2 silver from your inventory and hand it to Sproggets.}}
{{Chat|Sproggets Bedsprings|Good doing business with you! May Trem's fortune find you.}}
{{Emote|Sproggets Bedsprings retrieves a small field pack from behind the counter and hands it to you.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Small Field Pack of Ropes]] from [[Sproggets Bedsprings]].}}
{{QuestNote|Travel to [[Sungreet Strand]] and return to [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}
{{QuestNote|Hand [[Small Field Pack of Ropes]] to [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Excellent! Let me prepare the rope for you.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank pulls out the ropes one by one and ties them together end to end, creating one long rope.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank stretches the rope from foot to head, marking it with knots, and repeats the process until she reaches the end.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Here you go. One knotted rope at about five hundred length. This should be long enough to do the job.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Now, make some room in your pack because there's quite a few items you'll need for the task. Let me know when you're ready!}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]] from [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}

=== Part 2 - It's actually quite large! ===

{{Chat|say|I am ready.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Good! Here's the survey form to fill out. Use your apprentice disk to mark down any measurements you've taken.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Tig's Survey Form]] from [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Also, this is a surveying book written by yours truly. You'll find it useful.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[The Joy of Surveying]] from [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|And here's an advanced book on surveying.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Advanced Surveying Volume I]] from [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|I know this is a lot of information, but I believe in you. You're also the only one who can do this right now... so there's that too. In Trem we trust, as I guess we must!}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|For your first task, you'll need to find the surface area of the quarry. The books cover this, so I wont bore you with the details.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Seek out the markers at the quarry. They've got bright green cloths on them so they should be easy to see, but you might need to take a closer look to see the numbers on them.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Look for marker number one. Secure one end of the rope there, then stretch it all the way to marker two.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Take the first measurement and bring it back to me to check your work.}}

==== Markers 1 and 2 ====

{{QuestInfo|Need to verify if [[Tig's Survey Form]] auto-updates as you capture measurements.}}
{{QuestNote|Read over [[The Joy of Surveying]], as it will provide instructions on how to capture measurements and how to identify piton objects in-game.}}
{{QuestNote|You now have to locate the various pitons around the quarry and use MUD commands with your [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]] to capture measurements.}}
{{QuestNote|Location 1(marker #2) is at the south eastern corner of the Quarry along the rim (Left of the ramp in and out).}}
{{QuestNote|When you are at a given location, hold [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]] on your cursor and use the MUD command `/place Rope` to attach the rope to the marker.}}
{{Chat|mud|/place Rope}}
{{Emote|You tie one end of the rope to the marker one.}}
{{QuestInfo|This updated the rope to Knotted Rope Tied to Marker Two}}
{{QuestNote|Location 2(marker #1) is at the south western corner of the Quarry along the rim (near the ramp in and out of the quarry).}}
{{Chat|mud|/place Rope}}
{{Emote|You tie the other end of the rope to the second marker.}}
{{Emote|You carefully count the number of knots between the first marker and second marker.}}
{{Emote|After a few moments you have counted a total of <b>240</b> knots, each marking a length. You quickly make a note of this upon the parchment.}}
{{QuestNote|Travel back to the piton locations and use the MUD command `/take Rope`. The final result should be a [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]] in your bags and not another named rope.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take Rope}}
{{Emote|You untie one end of the rope from the first marker.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take Rope}}
{{Emote|You untie one end of the rope from the second marker.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Tig Pebblebank]] and hand in the updated [[Tig's Survey Form]] as well as [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]].}}
{{QuestNote|If you forget to undo the rope with the MUD Command `/take Rope` you are met with the following:}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank looks you over and scratches her head.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Where's the knotted rope? Did you know that you left some rope attached to a marker?}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|You must untie the rope from the marker and bring it back with you.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Go ahead. I'll be here when you return.}}
{{QuestInfo|Special Note: If you need to zone from aggro after taking off just one part of a rope, you can zone back and just take the other part off. You will not need to start over. This may be helpful for the last part if you are solo (w/ no FD) - since putting on and taking off the rope drops invis.}}

==== Markers 2 and 3 ====

{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank looks over the survey and nods.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|This is a good start. You just need one more measurement and we'll have what we need to figure out the area.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank hands back the survey form.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Now, go back to marker two and get the length from marker two to marker three. Once you've written down the length, bring the survey back to me to check.}}
{{QuestNote|Location 2 is at the south eastern corner of the Quarry along the rim (near the ramp in and out of the quarry).}}
{{QuestNote|When you are at location 2, hold [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]] on your cursor and use the MUD command `/place Rope` to attach the rope to the marker.}}
{{Chat|mud|/place Rope}}
{{Emote|You tie one end of the rope to the marker two.}}
{{QuestNote|Location 3 is at the North Eastern corner of the Quarry along the rim (Follow the rim North of the ramp in and out towards the Glass Flats zone).}}
{{Chat|mud|/place Rope}}
{{Emote|You tie the other end of the rope to the third marker.}}
{{Emote|You carefully count the number of knots between markers two and three.}}
{{Emote|After a few moments you have counted a total of <b>416</b> knots, each marking a length. You quickly make a note of this upon the parchment.}}
{{QuestNote|Travel back to the piton locations and use the MUD command `/take Rope`. The final result should be a [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]] in your bags and not another named rope.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take Rope}}
{{Emote|You untie one end of the rope from the second marker.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take Rope}}
{{Emote|You untie one end of the rope from the third marker.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Tig Pebblebank]] and hand in the updated [[Tig's Survey Form]] as well as [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]].}}

==== Markers 4 and 5 ====

[[File:Tigs Quest - Marker 4 5.png|thumb]]
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank looks over the survey and smiles.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Great! You have the measurements needed for the area. Now, we need to get the measurement for the volume.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank hands back the survey form.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Go find markers four and five and measure the distance between them. After you've written down the length, bring the survey back to me to look over.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|After this measurement, you won't need the rope anymore. Hand that in too when you're done.}}
{{QuestNote|Location 4 and 5 are just north of the middle of the quarry. Look for the highest point. When you are at location 4, hold [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]] on your cursor and use the MUD command `/place Rope` to attach the rope to the marker.}}
{{QuestNote|Location 4 can be easily done through invisibility unless [[a cinder herald]] is roaming, his agro radius is massive.}}
{{Chat|mud|/place Rope}}
{{Emote|You tie one end of the rope to the fourth marker.}}
{{QuestNote|Location 5 can be a challenge. The path up can be traveled invisible and is generally free from kill on sight mobs. At the top, there are 2 Spellshooters that SEE INVISIBLE, 4 goblins total near the marker.}}
{{QuestNote|If you are doing the quest at level 15, these goblins will be deep red. You can agro them and train them around if you need, but remember you need to place and then return to TAKE back the rope.}}
{{Chat|mud|/place Rope}}
{{Emote|You tie one end of the rope to the fifth marker.}}
{{Emote|You carefully count the number of knots between markers four and five.}}
{{Emote|After a few moments you have counted a total of <b>42</b> knots, each marking a length. You quickly make a note of this upon the parchment.}}
{{QuestNote|Travel back to the piton locations and use the MUD command `/take Rope`. The final result should be a [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]] in your bags and not another named rope.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take Rope}}
{{Emote|You untie one end of the rope from the fourth marker.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take Rope}}
{{Emote|You untie one end of the rope from the fifth marker.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Tig Pebblebank]] and hand in the updated [[Tig's Survey Form]] as well as [[Rope, Knotted, 500 Length]].}}

=== Part 3 - Math? I hate math ===

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Tig's Survey Form]] from [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|You have the lengths! Great! I hope it wasn't too difficult.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank puts the knotted rope back into her field pack.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Now, all I need to do on my end is verify the form. The results are, honestly, as I expected.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank writes something on the form and hands it back to you.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|We're not done though. The surface area needs to be added to the form. Based on your measurements, I know what the area is... but do you?}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Consider this a test of your skill, apprentice. Think carefully about the answer and take your time to get it right. Once you've got it, tell me your answer.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Or, if you just want to be done with the survey, you can hand me the form and go.}}
{{QuestNote|Review [[Advanced Surveying Volume I]] provided by [[Tig Pebblebank]] earlier in the quest.}}
{{QuestNote|This book provides the basic mathematical formulas to calculate the correct answer to Tig's question.}}
{{QuestNote|Inspect [[Tig's Survey Form]] for the values captured by your measurements.}}
{{QuestNote|For this question, Tig wants the surface area, noted as A &equals; L x W.}}
{{QuestNote|In [[Tig's Survey Form]], this should equate to A &equals; Length 1 x Length 2.}}
{{QuestNote|240 x 416 &equals; 99,840.}}
{{Chat|say|The surface area of the quarry is 99,840.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Well done, that's correct!}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|If you don't mind, I'll jot that down on your form.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank snatches the form from your hand and quickly scribbles down the answer, then promptly returns it to you.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|There, now you have the area of the quarry filled in.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|I must say, I'm impressed with your skill so far. Advanced surveying concepts don't come easily.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|I wonder... do you happen to know the last measurement, the volume of the quarry? Tell me, and we can finish this form properly.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Once again, this is quite an advanced surveying technique. If it's too much for you, you can hand me the form and go. I'll understand.}}
{{QuestNote|For this question, Tig wants the volume, noted as V &equals; L x W x H in [[Advanced Surveying Volume I]].}}
{{QuestNote|In [[Tig's Survey Form]], this should equate to V &equals; Length 1 x Length 2 x Length 3.}}
{{QuestNote|240 x 416 x 42 &equals; 4,193,280.}}
{{Chat|say|The volume of the quarry is 4,193,280.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Trem's fortune favors you, my apprentice! That is correct!}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Hand me the survey. Let us put an end to this task.}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Tig Pebblebank]] your completed [[Tig's Survey Form]].}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank takes the note from you and scribbles down a few more words.}}
{{Emote|Tig Pebblebank folds up the survey and tucks it gently into her robe, smiling.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|This will be a great help to not only the Measure, but also to Trem's faithful.}}
{{Chat|Tig Pebblebank|Please take this as thanks for your efforts. Rest well, knowing you've served a higher purpose this day. Trust in Trem.}}
{{exp}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[The Measure Stick]] from [[Tig Pebblebank]].}}
{{QuestInfo|Your faction standing with Congregation of Trem got better.}}
{{QuestInfo|Your faction standing with Citizens of Night Harbor got better.}}


