The Yowling.content:
{{Quest
|Start Zone         = [[Night Harbor]]
|Quest Giver        = [[an ashira shapeshifter]]
|Minimum Level      = 1
|Classes            = All
|Related NPCs       =
[[Mayana]]
[[an ashira shapeshifter]]
[[Leatherworker Haiat]]
[[Jalwa Noor]]
[[General Overlord Bloodynose]]
[[Seeress Hamana]]
[[Qassem Brolt]]
[[Overseer Shuk'Naru]]
[[Jens Vermahn]]

|Related Items =
[[Unusual Jackal Pelt]]
[[Ashira Pelt]]
[[Broken Lute]]
[[Ancient Chant]]
[[Bloodynose Goblin Ear]]
[[Bloodynose Goblin Head]]
[[Head of General Overlord Bloodynose]]
[[Sealed Note]]
[[Hidden Note]]
|Quest Rewards =
<ul>
<li>[[Ashira Pack Ring]]</li>
<li>[[Refined Ashira Pack Ring]]</li>
<li>[[Delicate Ashira Pack Ring]]</li>
<li>[[Great Ashira Pack Ring]]</li>
<li>[[Ring of the Ashira Protector]]</li>
</ul>
}}

{{QuestNote|Warning, the stages of this quest are NOT repeatable. DO NOT MISPLACE ANY RING. If you lose the ring, you cannot progress.}}

== Walkthrough ==

=== Part 1 - An Unusual Pelt - Req. lvl 1 ===

{{QuestNote|This quest starts by looting an [[Unusual Jackal Pelt]] from [[an ashira shapeshifter]].}}
{{QuestNote|Inspecting the [[Unusual Jackal Pelt]] item tooltip directs the player to interact with someone familiar with pelts.}}
{{QuestNote|Seek out [[Leatherworker Haiat]] at the Tannery near West Gate in [[Night Harbor]] and hand him the [[Unusual Jackal Pelt]].}}
{{Chat|Leatherworking Haiat|These markings are typical for ashira leather. What's made you curious about it, friend?}}
{{Chat|Leatherworking Haiat|Ashira are known to shapeshift into jackals, their animal form, so to speak, which is probably how you came by it.}}
{{Chat|Leatherworking Haiat|You seem surprised. Don't believe old me? Show the pelt to a seasoned bard, they can tell you more tales about the ashira folk.}}
{{Chat|Leatherworking Haiat|Or if you don't want it, we'll take it off of your hands for a few copper. They're tough and make for a solid base to work with!}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Ashira Pelt]] from Leatherworker Haiat.}}
{{QuestInfo|You can turn in the [[Ashira Pelt]] to [[Leatherworker Haiat]] for 3 copper.}}
{{QuestNote|Seek out [[Jalwa Noor]] in Glimmermoon Hall (The Bard's Guild in the Night Market) and hand her the [[Ashira Pelt]].}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|An ashira's pelt? Mayhaps you could tell me why you're showing me this?}}
{{Chat|say|I wish to learn more about the tales of the ashira folk.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|The ashira are a race of jackalweres, indigenous to the deserts and foothills of southwestern Aêthoril. They've inhabited these dunes long before us, wanderer.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|They live harmoniously with nature and loathe the unnatural. In times past, our kin were both at war with and friendly to each other.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|Trade with them was once common, but of late, you don't see them interacting with the people of Night Harbor anymore. For reasons unknown to me, they've grown wary of us and mostly retreat to their home deep in the gorges of Ain Golot.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|A shame, truly. Their race is as ancient as the stars themselves, and their abilities are equally extraordinary.}}
{{Chat|say|What abilities?}}
{{Emote|Jalwa Noor leans closer, as shadows from the torchlight dance across her face.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|Oh yes... the ashira have mastered the mystical art of shapeshifting. It was bestowed upon them through the Yowling, a spiritual heritage passed down from their revered ancestors. With a whisper to the wind and a call to the wild, the ashira can transform, taking the form of jackals or even... that of a human.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|Rumors abound of ashira hiding their true form beneath a veneer of human flesh, weaving through the throngs of cityfolk... even here in Night Harbor. So perfect is their mimicry that one might never know the person beside them is not of human kin.}}
{{Emote|Jalwa Noor lowers her voice to a reverent hush.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|But heed this tale well, for the Yowling is no mere parlor trick, It's the echo of their lineage, a bond with the primeval forces that crafted the very essence of our world. To witness an ashira shift is to gaze upon the ancient dance of spirit and flesh, a secret rite as old as time itself.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|As keepers of this world's ancient tales, some bards hold the secret of a rare chant learned from times of mistrust, one that forces an ashira back to their true form.}}
{{Emote|Jalwa Noor lets out a sorrowful sigh.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|Alas, the chant is not known to me, only to the most gifted of bards. My muse and lifelong partner, Alisar, was one of them.}}
{{Chat|say|Who was Alisar?}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|Alisar was a wonderful musician and storyteller. Many moons ago, I couldn't help but fall deeply in love with his beautiful soul. We wed not long after and voyaged across the continent together.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|Unfortunately... he is no longer with us. He took his instruments and musical sheets with him to the grave.}}
{{Emote|Jalwa Noor shakes visibly as her voice cracks.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|His last voyage took him to the Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane. He fought alongside his companions to recover a unique pipe organ that had been lost deep below the sands.}}
{{Emote|Jalwa Noor gazes into the distance, lost in memories long past.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|I've never heard, nor seen him again since...}}
{{Emote|Jalwa Noor whimpers quietly as a solemn tear runs down her cheek.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|If you dare tread the cursed halls of the tomb to reclaim Alisar's belongings, I'll be in your eternal debt. IF the chant you seek is among them, I'll teach it to you as payment.}}

=== Part 2 - The Lute - Req. lvl 3+ === 
'''The Lute can be acquired without turning in the pelt for step 1.'''
<br>
<br>
{{QuestNote|In [[Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane]] take the hidden path '''(not the hidden path leading to Ancient Crypts)''' in the builder room across from [[Quartermaster Boothroy]], and drop down onto the terrace with the pipe organ in the chapel.}} 
{{QuestNote|Overlooking [[Timmon Bell]] spawn location in the chapel. With your back to Bell, '''/look''' at the organ then proceed to the cobweb corner to the right and ahead and '''/take lute.}}
{{QuestNote|If a player recently already picked it up, it may take a few minutes for it to respawn}}

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Broken Lute]].}}

Return [[Broken Lute]] to Jalwa

{{Chat|Jalwa Noor| You... have returned from the shadowed depths of the tomb, bearing treasures long mourned as lost...}}
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Jalwa Noor trembles with reverence as she receives Alisar's lute, with the musical sheets hidden inside.</span>
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor| In these strings and parchment, the spirit of Alisar Noor dances once more. You've brought back more than just keepsakes, you've restored the echoes of a love that time itself could not silence. Thank you, kind adventurer.}}
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Jalwa Noor sifts through the musical sheets and gently removes one, her gaze meeting yours.</span>
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|Listen closely playername.}}
: <span style="font-weight:bold;color:#ff7933;">Jalwa Noor raises her voice in song, reciting words long lost with a tone of gratitude and rememberance.</span>
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|This is the chant you seek. I'll transcribe the words onto parchment for you. Recite them faithfully to activate its intended use... but use it with the utmost care.}}
{{Chat|Jalwa Noor|A word of warning... I don't know how the ashira will react if you disrupt their shapeshifting. Be careful.}}

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Ancient Chant]] from Jalwa Noor.}}
{{Faction|Residents of Ain Golot|+}}

=== Part 3 - Find Mayana === 

{{QuestNote|Find [[Mayana]] in Saltbreeze Park.}} 
{{QuestNote|Note: Mayana must be alone out of sight of other NPCs for the chant to work. She paths between three locations and it will not work if she is standing at the sojourner campfire or the pool of water by the monk trainer.}}
{{QuestNote|Inside the park, try to click the Chant. It'll either work or give an emote.}}

{{emote|You begin casting Ancient Disrupting Chant.}}
{{emote|You purge Mayana with a magical chant. (Human Form)}}
{{Chat|say|Hail, Mayana.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|What have you done, biped?! My form...}}
{{emote|Mayana glances around nervously, then takes a combative stance.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|State your intent, quickly! are you friend or foe?!}}
{{emote|Mayana growls at you.}}
{{Chat|say|Friend.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|You would keep my identity a secret? Why?}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Ancient Chant]] to [[Mayana]].}}
{{emote|Mayana immediately tears up the chant, then lightly bows her head with apparent relief.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|It is unexpected... but I cannot deny this show of trust.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|Please, take this as a token of our mutual understanding.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Ashira Pack Ring]] from Mayana.}}
{{Faction|Benu Memza|+}}
{{Faction|Residents of Ain Golot|+}}
{{Chat|Mayana|I cannot leave the city due to... obligations. My pack is at great risk, both from folk in Night Harbor and within our home in Tel Ekir.}}
{{emote|Mayana assumes her human form once more.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|Will you assist us where we suffer most?}}
{{Chat|say|Assist}}
{{Chat|Mayana|Those crazed goblins who call themselves the bloodynose clan have invaded our home in Tel Ekir. They only seek to slaughter us and summon the unnatural.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|Please... help us protect the Life Font and drive them out. It would ease our spirits' burden.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|If you do this, bring me any goblin ears and heads you take. The pack will reward you for proving your worth to us.}}
{{Chat|Mayana|And be sure to wear the ring when you bring them to me, so that I may see your conviction to our cause.}}
<br>
'''The bloodynose goblins are level 8+. You are looking for a [[Bloodynose Goblin Ear]] and a [[Bloodynose Goblin Head]] that drop from goblins in [[Sungreet Strand]] and [[Tel Ekir]].'''

=== Part 4 - Head of General Overlord Bloodynose ===
{{QuestNote|[[Seeress Hamana]] is in [[Tel Ekir]], at the back of the zone near the Guardian of the Life Font.}}
{{QuestNote|Above the waterfall, do not venture far into the wooded area. Wisps will aggro, and the Ashira will assist them even if you have maximum faction. Sneak along the right wall to [[Seeress Hamana]], complete the turn-in, and leave.}}
{{QuestNote|The faction requirement is unknown (success at Kindly with Benu Memza). The two relevant factions in the zone are Benu Lakhim and Benu Memza.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|You honor the pack.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|A most urgent matter has reached my ears. Will you lend us a hand once more?}}
{{Chat|say|I will help.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|You have lessened the goblin presence here, and now we must drive them out for good.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|Their general hides in the tunnels of Mount Tel Ekir. Find him and dispose of him.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand [[Head of General Overlord Bloodynose]] and [[Ashira Pack Ring]] to [[Seeress Hamana]].}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|The pack cannot thank you enough. This will give our young ones much-needed respite.}}
{{QuestNote|Reward: [[Refined Ashira Pack Ring]].}}

=== Part 5 - Fallen Pass - Req Lvl 19+ ===
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|You Honour the pack.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|A most urgent matter has reached my ears. Will you lend us a hand once more?}}
{{Chat|say|Lend a hand}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana |Fallen Pass is home to the wretched. These monsters are poisoning our lands and need to be stopped.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana |Put an end to their evil deeds. We would be eternally indebted to you.}}
'''[[Fallen Pass]] zone is level 19+.'''
<br>
<br>
{{QuestNote|Obtain [[Sealed Note]] from [[Qassem Brolt]] }}
{{QuestNote|Obtain [[Hidden Note]] from [[Overseer Shuk'Naru]] }}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Sealed Note]] to [[Seeress Hamana]].}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|You found this note while fighting off wererats?}}
{{emote|Seeress Hamana ponders the message within.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|It is clear that they are working for someone with grander schemes in mind.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|We must learn what these shipments are for... and for whom.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|For now, keep this precious bit of evidence with you, but please return to me if you are able to find out more on this matter.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sealed Note]] from Seeress Hamana.}}
{{Faction|Benu Memza|+}}
{{Faction|Residents of Ain Golot|+}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|Please, hand me the other note you found as well. I think I see the connection!}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from Seeress Hamana.}}
{{QuestNote|Give both notes to [[Seeress Hamana]].}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|The concoctions, the timing... it all aligns.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|This confirms it. Jens Vermahn, the wererat, must be the agent who produced the disease that threatens us all!}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|We must put an end to his atrocities. Find Jens' whereabouts and rip his throat out!}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|But before you go, hand me your pack ring. I shall transform it to bear the mark of one of our own, for you are a true member of the pack!}}
{{Faction|Benu Memza|+}}
{{Faction|Residents of Ain Golot|+}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|There, a just reward.}}
{{Chat|Seeress Hamana|Now, go quickly. We must not delay any longer.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You recieved [[Delicate Ashira Pack Ring]] }}

===part 6 - ?? ===
{{QuestNote|Find [[Jens Vermahn]] }}
{{QuestNote|jens is not in the game, so im thinking you need to find information on his whereabouts..?? }}

{{QuestNote|to be continued....}}
Sounds like he has just recently been added to the game actually, and the 5th ring now exists. Need info
