Shaman Starter Quest (Faelindral).content:
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = none
| width             = 100px
| caption           = none
|Start Zone         = [[Faelindral]]
|Quest Giver        = [[Varilis Thornvine]]
|Minimum Level      = 1
|Classes            = [[Shaman]]
|Related NPCs       = [[a mischievous faerie]], [[a rotting skeleton]]
|Related Items      =
[[Bone Chips]]
[[Shattered Skull]]
|Quest Rewards      = (exp); [[Novice Hoop of the Listener]]; [[Apprentice Hoop of the Listener]]; [[Spirit-Blessed Headdress]]; [[Robes of the Listener]]; [[Hoop of the Listener]];
}}

__TOC__

== Walkthrough ==
=== Part 1 - Preserve the Balance ===

{{QuestNote|Read the [[Folded Leafscroll]] that you start with as a new Shaman Character in [[Faelindral]].}}
<pre>
      Do you hear the whispers through the boughs?
           Yes, this is because you Listen.

   Do you hear the whimsy hidden in the fae's wisdom?
           Yes, this is because you Listen.

Do you hear the songs of our history yearning to be told?
           Yes, this is because you Listen.

We invite you to learn from these whispers at the 
Balanced Branch lodge.

To reach us, set out toward the Willows Whisper and
ascend the ramp on the left to Traders Terrace. Once 
there, traverse the lone bridge and you will find us across 
from our Ranger cousins. Any of the city guard can 
provide further direction if required. 

When you arrive, present this note to our Listener 
mentor, Varilis Thornvine.

                                        Eraeldor Lowmist,
                        Elder Whisperer of the Preservers
</pre>
{{QuestNote|Head to the Shaman Guild (the Balanced Branch, follow signs or review [[Faelindral]] map).}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Folded Leafscroll]] to [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Faction|Fellstone Orcs|-}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine cracks open a well-wizened gaze as you offer him the scroll, which he accepts at the pace of an old treant.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|The whispers of your arrival have reached my ears well before this scroll ever did, young shaman.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I have been preparing for you. Here, please accept this mortar and pestle. You will need it for your first task.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Old Mortar and Pestle]] from Varilis Thornvine.}}
{{Chat|say|What task?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Old forces threaten the balance of the Weald and beyond. The fae grow restless and resentful. The spirits of the dead find no rest.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|We must do what needs be done to preserve the balance, young one. My old bones are not up to this task, but perhaps a young listener such as yourself could quell some of these... disturbances.}}
{{Chat|say|What disturbances?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|You should start with the undead that have begun to crawl out from long forgotten places.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Gather four chips of their bones, along with two of their skulls. Crush them within your mortar and return the dust to me.}}
{{Chat|say|What undead?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|The spirits of young adventurers, or those long since left behind, disturbed of their rest.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Beneath our forest once stood an empire, of which the fallen are all too willing to rise.}}
{{Chat|say|What empire?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|That of the Calafrey Conglomerate, which ruled before even my time.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|The Heartwood Archive could teach you more, if you are interested.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to the newbie area and kill [[a rotting skeleton]] until you get 4 x [[Bone Chips]] and 2 x [[Shattered Skull]]. Combine these in the [[Old Mortar and Pestle]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You craft [[Mortar of Bone Dust]].}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Varilis Thornvine]] and give him [[Mortar of Bone Dust]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Faction|Fellstone Orcs|-}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine carefully reaches out to collect the mortar of ground up, chalky bone dust. He carefully pours the dust into a small pouch, whispering out soft unheard words as he does.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Well done, young Listener. These spirits can now return to the rest that they rightly deserve.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|For this, you deserve to be recognized as a novice of our order, and so I shall present to you this hoop.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Our task is not yet complete, however. It is not just the spirits of the dead that are crying out, but those of the living as well.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Novice Hoop of the Listener]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Pouch of Bone Dust]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}

=== Part 2 - The Malicious Faerie ===

{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|You shall take what remains of those who were scorned and have them reveal the source of the wolves' agony. Can you hear their cries?}}
{{Chat|say|I can hear their cries.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|The mournful howls of the Weald's wolves haunt my dreams of late. More of their number fall to savagery and madness by the day.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I have altered the bone dust that you collected, so that it may cling to the dismal agonies of woeful spirits.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|There is a wolf pack amongst the western cliffs whose cries concern me most. Locate and scatter the dust at the entrance of their den to reveal the source of this dismay.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Throw, or simply pour out the contents of the pouch. It should make no difference. Once revealed, you must confront the spirit and, if need be, cleanse it. Do you understand?}}
{{Chat|say|I understand.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Good. You may wish to conceal yourself from the gaze of any wolves who have fallen to madness, as they can be vicious foes.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Return to me with anything that you uncover, along with your novice hoop. You may also return and ask me for more dust, should you lose what you have.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you run out of dust and need more...}}
{{Chat|say|I need more dust.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Very well. Be mindful of where you choose to scatter it, young Listener, as well as what threats iy may reveal.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Pouch of Bone Dust]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{QuestNote|Go down the Pixie Lift (Fungi lift) and turn left. Head past the druid ring, fungal ring, cross the bridge, and pass through the ruins.}}
{{QuestNote|Down the hill from the ruins you will spot a cave, which is the aforementioned wolf den.}}
{{QuestNote|Be mindful of [[a beguiled wolf]] spawns in the area, as these are high level and aggressive. [[Invisibility]] may be useful here.}}
{{QuestNote|Stand in the entrance of the cave and /look to verify you are in the correct location:}}
{{Chat|mud|/look}}
{{Emote|The den appears to house some local wolves, with traces of bone and viscera lying alongside dozens of heavyset prints and matted clumps of fur.}}
{{QuestNote|Pick up the dust on your cursor and type /throw dust.}}
{{Chat|mud|/throw dust}}
{{Emote|As you scatter the bone dust around the den, you hear a surprised sneeze nearby. The outline of a small, invisible winged creature suddenly appears in the deluge of chalky dust!}}
{{Chat|a mischievous faerie|Achoo! Ahh! Oh no-no-no! It was just a prank, I promise!}}
{{QuestNote|[[a mischievous faerie]] (level 2) will spawn. Kill the faerie and loot [[Strange Toadstool]].}}
{{QuestNote|To avoid agroing the nearby [[a beguiled wolf]] spawns, run back towards the ruins as the faerie will eventually path towards them. When the faerie is a safe distance from the cave, engage in combat with it.}}
{{QuestInfo|Upon attacking the faerie..}}
{{Chat|a mischievous faerie|Ow, hey! It was just a gaff! They actually only ate three people, honest!}}
{{QuestInfo|Upon slaying the faerie..}}
{{Emote|a mischievous faerie slumps to the ground with a pathetic wail.}}
{{Chat|a mischievous faerie|How could a prank... go so wrong...?}}
{{ReceiveItem|You loot [[Strange Toadstool]] from a mischievous faerie's corpse.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Varilis Thornvine]] and hand him your [[Novice Hoop of the Listener]] as well as the [[Strange Toadstool]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Faction|Fellstone Orcs|-}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine furrows his already well-weathered brow as you present the toadstool to him, alongside your novice hoop.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|So the fae have had a hand in this? Their antics grow bolder by the day, despite our tenuous agreement.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|You were not wrong to mete out punishment for the imbalance they caused. I would say you deserve this.}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine proceeds to whisper something into the small hoop, as though it were an ear yearning to hear one of his tales. He smiles softly and offers the hoop back to you, now empowered further by the spirits.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Apprentice Hoop of the Listener]] from Varilis Tornvine.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Well done Listener. Though now we must see about this strange toadstool. Perhaps it can tell us a clue.}}
{{Chat|say|What was the tenuous agreement?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|A pact was made with the fae long ago. They would teach us the means in which to restore our forest, and in exchange, we would grant them land of their own here in Evershade.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Of course, the fae are always looking for means to expand their reach and propagate more of their influence onto the land... through pacts, trickery, or, in some cases, magical beguilement.}}
{{Chat|say|Magical beguilement?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Yes, it is an unfortunate truth that we as Preservers must help navigate. Not all fae are hostile or malicious, but those who cross the line of dominating the freedom of others must be punished for it.}}
{{Chat|say|What clue does the toadstool tell us?}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine slowly brings the toadstool up toward his elongated ear, as though listening to murmurs that only he could hear.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Tell me, young Listener, do you hear the whispers?}}

=== Part 3 - Spore Druids - Req. Level 4 ===
{{QuestNote|You must be at least level 4 to progress past this part.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you are level 3 or below...}}
{{Chat|say|I can hear the whispers.}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine shakes his head back and forth in a languid motion.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I do not believe you truly hear them just yet. Return to me when you have more experience among the spirits of the Weald, then inquire again if you are ready to hear the whispers.}}
{{QuestInfo|If you are level 4 or above..}}
{{Chat|say|I can hear the whispers.}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine pauses to study you for what feels like an age, before a slow and unhurried nod is offered.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I believe you will be capable of hearing a great many things before long, young one. Not just from toadstools, but from all manner of objects in which the spirits reside.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Even from objects that have been with you from the near beginning. Please, allow me to see your apprentice hoop so that I may listen to all it has experienced in your journey thus far.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand Varilis Thornvine your [[Apprentice Hoop of the Listener]].}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Faction|Fellstone Orcs|-}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine takes your hoop and brings it close to his own ear. He nods along with it thoughtfully, as it seemingly tells the Elder Whisperer of your travels.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|An interesting journey you have taken to get here. Your hoop is excited to experience more, so I shall return it to you. Be sure to hold onto it so it can take in more of your continued story.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Apprentice Hoop of the Listener]] from Varilis Thornvine.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|You will also need to bring this toadstool with you for your next task. We are now being whispered toward a group who lives reclusively among the roots of Faelindral.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Tell me, young Listener, do you know of the Circle of Spores?}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Toadstool Box]] from Varilis Thornvine.}}
{{Chat|say|What circle of spores?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|They are a cloistered cult of druids who have a strong connection to fungus and mushrooms. If there are any within the Weal who would be able to tell us the source of this strange toadstool, it would be them.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I have safely packed the toadstool within the box I provided you. Deliver it to a member of the Circle of Spores, who seclude themselves beneath Faelindral in Sporehave Karts.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I know not the name of the particular druid who may be able to help us, but the Circle are not unwelcoming of guests. Their experiments on the other hand...}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I have heard whispers that their experiments have become dangerous during the night time hours. It would be best for you to travel there only during the day.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Spirits watch over you, young Listener.}}
{{QuestNote|Take the Newbie Lift from [[Faelindral]] to [[Evershade Weald]] and head north. When you reach the river, turn right and follow the northern edge of the river to head into the Spore Caves.}}
{{QuestInfo|THE MYOCID ARE AGGRESSIVE DURING NIGHT HOURS IN-GAME. Use an Invisibility ability if traveling at night.}}
{{QuestNote|Follow the left side of the cave until you climb a ramp. Then, hug the right wall and you will find [[Sporeweaver Underviel]] on a raised platform.}}
{{QuestInfo|BEWARE A NUMBER OF SPORELINGS PATH RIGHT PAST THE NPC, DO NOT RISK CONVERSATION WITHOUT INVIS/HIDE HANDY!}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Sporeweaver Underviel]] the [[Toadstool Box]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Faction|Circle of Spores|+}}
{{Emote|Sporeweaver Underveil carefully examines the contents of the box you offer him, pursing his lips in thought. He meticulously removes the toadstool before returning the empty box to you.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Empty Box]] from [[Sporeweaver Underveil]].}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|Hmm... this is quite the interesting specimen that you have brought me, shaman. I can tell at a glance that is has been manipulated by a magical force, not unlike our own myconids.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|Though I could not tell you much more without a thorough examination. Perhaps we could come to an agreement?}}
{{emote|Sporeweaver Underviel looks at you expectantly.}}
{{chat|say|What agreement?}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|I am looking to produce a new strain of fungus that is far more robust than previous generations.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|To further my research, I need some components from out in the Weald. If you can gather them for me, I will look further into the origins of this toadstool for you.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|Does that sound acceptable?}}
{{chat|say|It is acceptable.}}
{{Emote|Sporeweaver Underveil bows his head politely, a faint glimmer reflecting from his shaven scalp.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|Then we have an agreement. You can use the empty box that you brought the toadstool in as a container. It seems sturdy enough.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|All I require are the scales of green drakelings, along with some wax from wasp workers. Five of each should suffice for my needs.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|By the time you return with the box filled and sealed, I should have some more answers for you regarding this mysterious toadstool.}}
{{QuestNote|Loot 5 x [[Green Drakeling Scale]] from [[a green drakeling]], and 5 x [[Wasp Worker Wax]] from [[a wasp worker]].}}
{{QuestNote|Combine 5 x [[Green Drakeling Scale]] and 5 x [[Wasp Worker Wax]] in the [[Empty Box]] to create the [[Box of Scales and Wax]].}}
{{QuestNote|Give [[Box of Scales and Wax]] to [[Sporeweaver Underveil]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Faction|Circle of Spores|+}}
{{Emote|Sporeweaver Underveil examines the contents of the box with a satisfied nod, retrieving the strange toadstool and exchanging it for the materials you collected. He then returns the box to you.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Resealed Toadstool Box]] from Sporeweaver Underveil.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|You return at a most fortuitous moment, young shaman. I have just finished my examination of the toadstool and I must say, the results are quite intriguing.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|You also have my gratitude for your efforts in procuring these components. Drake scales and wax are notoriously resistant to fungus, which shall aid my endeavors to strengthen our strains.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|Though I imagine you must be curious to hear the results?}}
{{chat|say|What results?}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|The toadstool by itself is not so significant; rather, it is the odd hex that seems to be afflicting all of its contained moisture.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|This hexed moisture makes its way into the numerous spores released by the toadstool, and once a great number of these spores are taken into the lungs... well...}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|The victim is afflicted with a terrible malady that assaults the mind directly, causing hallucinations, emotional strain, and potentially even madness.}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|I daresay that whoever conjured such a hex has a sinister imagination. Though, it would appear the moisture is the key to all this, as it is what drips with malice. A malice that feels all too familiar to me...}}
{{Chat|Sporeweaver Underveil|I hope this was as much help to you as your efforts were to the Circle of Spores. Thank you once more, friend.}}
{{QuestNote|Return to Varilis Thornvine and give him [[Resealed Toadstool Box]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Your return was whispered to me, young Listener. As was the conversation you had with the Sporeweaver.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|It seems that moisture is the key to what has been ailing the great bears, yes? If our clues are to be the fae and moisture, then there is only one possible direction to look toward next.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Though that direction must wait for now. I must confer with the spirits on this matter, but you have the thanks of the forest, along with my own, for all that you have uncovered.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Take this headdress so that you might be protected from any intrusions into your own mind. It may prove useful, should this path lead us toward those capable of causing madness and grief.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Spirit-Blessed Headdress]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}

=== Part 4 - ===
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|When you feel you are ready to confront this threat to the Weald, bring me your apprentice hoop while donning the spirit-blessed headdress. I would hear from them both to gauge your capabilities regarding our next task.}}
{{QuestNote|Hand Varilis your earring while wearing the new headpiece.}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine carefully cradles the hoop next to his own ear, closing his eyes and nodding along wordlessly to silent whispers.}}
{{QuestInfo|(At level 4)}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|It appears you have more to learn before I can entrust you with your next task, young Listender.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Return and present me your hoop once you have learned how to effectively dispel harmful magics, and the next task is yours.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive your items back from Varilis Thornvine.}}
{{QuestInfo|(At level 8)}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine carefully cradles the hoop next to his own ear, closing his eyes and nodding along wordlessly to silent whispers. He smiles and presents it back to you.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|It appears the spirits vouch for your capabilities, young Listener. As such, I am confident I can entrust you with the next task.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Apprentice Hoop of the Listener]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{Chat|say|What next task?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|As you already know, spirits of the Weald are succumbing to a terrible malady of the mind.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|From the myconid creatures of the Circle of Spores to the bestial spirits of the great wolf packs, it seems any who settle themselves close to the banks of the river are prone to bouts of inexplicable madness.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|This, I believe, is being perpetrated by the naiads of the Whispering Pools.}}
{{Chat|say|What Whispering Pools?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|The naiads have long since been bound to the Whispering Pools. They are forbidden from leaving, due to a pact with the Queen of the Winter Court herself.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Though being bound does not mean the naiads are without their own ambitions.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Many of them yearn to be free of the Whispering Pools, and this latest act of whimsy is likely an attempt to expand their means without breaking the terms of their pact.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|If we are to do something to counteract the ploys of the naiads, we must first understand what sort of enchantments they are dispersing into the Weald's waters.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I advise you to seek out Laenyth Windharp of the Lambent Wanderers. She is their tale keeper, and the bards are known to study and even conduct performances that mimic the alluring call of a siren.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|If any in Faelindral would know of water nymph enchantments, it would be them. Show her your hoop to present yourself as a Preserver, then glean what you can about the magics of the naiads. Return to me with anything you manage to uncover.}}
{{QuestNote|Off we go to the bard guild (Aka the Lambent Lantern)!}}
{{QuestNote|You will find our gal on the first floor in the bard side of the lantern. It's up the ramp across from the stage. Hand your hoop to [[Laenyth Windharp]].}}
{{Emote|Laenyth Windharp regards the hoop with a smile before offering it back to you.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|Ah, to what do I owe the pleasure of this visit, apprentice? I'm fond of Listeners joining me for a tale. You lot are remarkably attentive to our stories.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|Is there anything in particular that you wish to hear about?}}
{{Chat|say|Naiads.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|The naiads? I'm quite familiar with their tale, as young bards are often stricken by their songs... competitively or otherwise.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|They're a beautiful people, if not prone to wickedness and uncaring whimsy. Their songs can flow as gently as a stream or crash with the cacophonous roar of a waterfall, as befits their mood.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|Do you wish to hear what's known of their Mistress Naelira, or are you more interested in their siren's song?}}
{{Chat|say|What siren's song?}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|The siren's call... it's a popular and powerful technique capable of fully capturing a person's attention. They're also prone to suggestion while captivated, turning a once alluring song into a dangerous one if used with ill intent.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|Many of the faerie courts are impressive singers in their own right, though the naiads' sirens occupy a league of their own. Did you know a voice can carry over great distances when delivered across a span of calm water?}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|The sirens utilize their affinity with water to naturally enhance their own voices, so a mere conversation can cause one to become enraptured if they're not careful.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|Some also believe the naiad sirens are capable of singing into the currents of flowing water, so their voices can reach those downstream. I personally don't believe such a thing is possible... unless you believe the old rumors.}}
{{Chat|say|What old rumors?}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|The naiads have remarkable voices, though even with their affinity for water, they cannot sing with their full cadence while submerged in the very pools they call home.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|A voice, no matter how strong, would be drowned out by the flow of a river as it crashes against the banks and weaves its way through rock and reed.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|However, there were rumors of a technique one could use to protect a song on its journey through a perilous river. Something to enshroud it is a pocket of air, such as... a bubble or river foam.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|I've made notes on such a theory before. Now where did I...}}
{{Emote|Laenyth Windharp searches through her belongings before a moment of recognition strikes her. She then withdraws a section of leafscroll.}}
{{Chat|Laenyth Windharp|Ah, here they are! These notes cover the methods one might use to enhance a siren's call. You're more than welcome to them, should the Perservers have use of my old theories.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Laenyth's Theories]] from [[Laenyth Windharp]].}}
{{QuestNote|Return to Varilis and hand him the theories.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I see that you do not return empty-handed, young Listener. Let us see what knowledge Laenyth has documented regarding the magic of naiads...}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine carefully and slowly peruses Laenyth's notes. His elderly lips purse in interest at some points while frowning at others, accentuating his already weathered features. }}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Voices carried through bubbles or foam... quite curious, indeed. Could the naiads be sending their very voices through the currents of the river using this method?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|You must investigate this for us, <name>. Your talents should allow you the means to sense magical influences upon the world, if you have studied your scrolls.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|I bid you venture out to the very end of the river, furthest from the Whispering Pools, to the crest of the mighty waterfall that spills out into the Twilight Sea.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Use your spell to sense magical flows and determine whether the naiads' enchantments have extended so far out from their domain. Should you discover enchanments at the falls, take a sample of the water using this flask and return it to me.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive an [[Empty Water Flask]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{QuestNote| From the Noob Lift take a right. At the fork in the road take the right side. Run south west until you get to where the river falls off the edge of the map. That's the crest of the water fall (the wolf cave is on the cliffs across the river for reference). Stand on the bank just to the right of the rocks (north of them) with your feet in the water.}}
{{QuestNote|You must have either the [[Ancestor's Eye]] or [[Ancestral Wisdom]] buff.}}
{{Chat|mud|/inspect water}}
{{Emote|The enchantment's effects are faint this far from the Whispering Pools, but they remain present within the flowing waters and long the banks.}}
{{Chat|mud|/take water}}
{{Emote|You carefully scoop your flask through the water, collecting a sample of it and much of the foam. The miniscule bubbles produce a soft, haunting melody that attempts to invade your mind, but whispers from your headdress block out the instrusive sounds, allowing you to regain your composure.}}

=== Part 5 - ===
{{QuestNote|Return to [[Varilis Thornvine]] and hand him [[Filled Water Flask]]}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|A curious thing, this sample you have brought me. Even while contained, I can hear the intrusive melodies that are bound within.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|This is a disturbing revelation. If the naiads have somehow found a way to carry their voices down the span of the entire river, it threatens the very balance of the Weald.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|We must take action to purge this enchantment before more minds are drawn into madness.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|Take this sigil. young Listener. You will need it to fashion a totem that can be used to cleanse the waters of the naiad's influence. It is but one component of this specific recipe.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Sigil of Purging]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{Chat|say|What recipe?}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|To fashion the totem, you will need to acquire some fine wood for the base. Four timber should be enough. If you have a talent for logging, you may find some in Keeper's Blight.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|While in the Blight, you will also need the skins of four serpents that roam the fields. The serpent's flesh is well suited for warding away moisture.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|Lastly, you will need something from the river water that is both born from it, but also immune to a siren's song. I believe Selstie Kelp will serve the purpose well.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|Scour the river's floor here in Evershade for at least two strands of kelp, then fashion everything together along with the sigil of purging at one of the carpentry tables on Traders Terrace.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|Worry not if you are unskilled with such labors, the totem need not be a masterpiece. Return to me with your crafted totem, and I shall guide you further.}}
{{QuestNote|Go collect 2 [[Selstie Kelp]], 4 [[Fine Wood]], and 4 [[Bight Serpent Skin]]. The wood is from Lumberjacking in [[Keepers Blight]]. This is also where you will find [[Bight Asp]], which is soloable with your new level 8 spells. Alternatively you can buy it from the tanner in the town there, [[Tessa Kentwell]], if other players have sold some to her for 6cp a piece at the time of this writing.}}
{{QuestNote|Combine the 10 items above along with your [[Sigil of Purging]] at a carpentry table to create [[Fashioned Totem of Purging]]. Then return to Varilis Thornvine and hand [[Fashioned Totem of Purging]] to him.}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine looks over your work with a pleased, serene smile. He raises the totem into the air and beseeches the spirits of the forest to empower your creation. This time, you begin to hear the murmurings of a response through the boughs of the trees, and your totem takes on weathered appearance.}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine offers the empowered totem to you.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|Take this totem to the top of the falls, which cascade over the Whispering Pools the water nymphs call their home.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|Invoke the totem's powers to purge the waters of the enchantment. But be warned, the naiads will not appreciate us denying them their amusement.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|If you are challenged, then do what you must to restore balance to the Weald. Should your totem lose its potency, return it to me and I will do my best to empower it once more.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thronvine|Spirits watch over you, young Listener.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Empowered Totem of Purging]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}

=== Part 6 - ===

{{QuestInfo|(The enemies for this part of the quest con red and yellow at level 8)}}
{{QuestNote|Head over to the Kennel Lift and ride it down. Walk east through the ruins and across two bridges, then make an immediate left to the waterfall. Stand at the edge of it and right-click your [[Empowered Totem of Purging]] to start the event.}}
{{Emote|Delugia Coldsong emerges from the waterfall as if stepping through a doorway.}}
{{Chat|Delugia Coldsong|You will not defile our waters with your horrid magics, mortal! Our voices shall spread across all rivers, in the name of Mistress Naelira!!}}
{{QuestNote|[[Delugia Coldsong]] (click for fight details) will spawn and immediately start attacking you. She was stuck in the wall when I fought her and I had to move away to get her to out.}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Circle of Spores|+}}
{{Faction|Fossergrim|-}}
{{Faction|Naelira's Court|-}}
{{Chat|Delugia Coldsong|H-how could you... a mere mortal...}}
{{Emote|[[Delugia Coldsong]] falls to the ground, her body slowly dissipating back into the waters.}}
{{QuestNote|Once you defeat her, loot the [[Coldstone Shard]] and return it to [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine shivers visibly as you offer him the coldstone, though he refuses to accept it alone.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|It seems that you have had to confront a particularly vile spirit, young Listener. Your efforts are already being felt throughout the Weald.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Return to me the expended totem, the coldstone, and your apprentice hoop. I would hear all three of their tales of your triumph this day.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive you items back from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{QuestNote|Hand Varilis all 3 items.}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Faction|Naelira's Court|-}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine carefully clutches the coldstone with one hand, while your hoop remains in the other. He brings both items up to either elongated ear and soon begins nodding along with their supposed tales, which you feel you may begin to perceive.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|It appears that this Delugia Coldsong was driven by a desire to appease her Mistress Naelira. So much so, that she would risk breaking the pact they made with the fae courts.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|It did not matter which minds she was forced to break, so long as her voice could reach out to someone capable of freeing them from their bond. A tragic tale, if also misguided and malevolent.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Already the spirits of the river and those surrounding it sigh out in relief at her passing. You have restored balance to the Weals, and for that I recognize you as an accomplished Listener, Chamois.}}
{{Emote|Varilis Thornvine offers you a simple leaf pulled from his silvered hair.}}
{{Chat|Varilis Thornvine|Bring this to the Elder Whisperer, Eraeldor Lowmist. He shall already know its meaning.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Weathered Leaf Token]] from [[Varilis Thornvine]].}}
{{QuestNote|Turn around and go in the building. Give your [[Weathered Leaf Token]] to [[Eraeldor Lowmist]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Preservers|+}}
{{Chat|Eraeldor Lowmist|The promising apprentice makes their appearance at last. It was heard, and it is now known.}}
{{Chat|Eraeldor Lowmist|We have you to thank for calming the spirits of the waters and all those who are fed by its life.}}
{{Chat|Eraeldor Lowmist|Only one who truly listens could have heard the cries and comforted the daunted.}}
{{Chat|Eraeldor Lowmist|You are a true preserver of the balance, deserving to bear the symbol of such.}}
{{Chat|Eraeldor Lowmist|My gift to you, Listener Chamois.}}
{{Emote|Eraeldor Lowmist produces a folded bundle of fine cloth and leaf, offering it to you with a serene smile.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Robes of the Listener]] from [[Eraeldor Lowmist]].}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Hoop of the Listener]] from [[Eraeldor Lowmist]].}}

