Shaman Starter Quest (Underdocks).content:
{{Quest
| imagefilename     = Picci Manifold.png
| width             = 
| caption           = Picci Manifold
|Start Zone         = [[Underdocks]]
|Quest Giver        = [[Picci Manifold]]
|Minimum Level      = 1
|Classes            = [[Shaman]]
|Related NPCs       = 
}}
== Reward ==
<ul class="hover-list">
<li>[[Shredded Cloak]]</li>
<li>[[Petrified Undercap Stem]]</li>
<li>[[Mycelial Staff]]</li>
<li>[[Mycelial Spear]]</li>
<li>Experience</li>
</ul>

== Walkthrough ==
{{QuestNote|The weapon progresses from [[Petrified Undercap Stem]] to [[Mycelial Staff]], then [[Mycelial Spear]]. For the Mycelial Staff, complete Part 3, Step 1. The preserved-brain task in Step 2 upgrades it to the spear.}}
<span id="Part_1_-_First_steps_as_a_Rot_of_Gorm_Shaman"></span>
== Part 1 - Starting Note and Shredded Cloak ==

Read [[Moldy Note]] you start with as a new Shaman Character:
<pre>
It is time for you to accept the gifts of the 
Rotfather.

Come to the Rotten Hollow to learn the ways of 
plague and pestilence. Seek the Rot of Gorm in the 
cavern west of the palace.

                                       Picci M.
</pre>

{{QuestNote|Give [[Moldy Note]] to [[Picci Manifold]].}}
{{exp}}
{{Faction|Rot of Gorm|+}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|The Rotfather beckons and here you are. His blessing, your gift, is a kindness. What life is worth living without decay and death? You and I are bound to this fate. Bear this drape in his honor.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Shredded Cloak]] from Picci Manifold.}}


<span id="Part_2_-_Uncovering_the_blight"></span>
=== Part 2 - Four Blightspores and Petrified Undercap Stem ===

{{Chat|say|Hail, Picci Manifold}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|There are a great many problems to solve before the Rotfather takes us. Will you aid me with my research?}}

{{Chat|say|research}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|The flora and fauna of the Deep are connected in ways that cannot be easily perceived. The myconids are of great interest to me, you see. They may hold the key to spreading the Rotfather's joy to the farthest reaches of Eth-ur, even into lowest abyss.}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|I need you to conduct an experiment.}}

{{Chat|say|experiment}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Take this balm and look for the little myconids within this cavern. The sporelings. Use it on the sickly ones. It is a kind of medicine.}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Return to me with four spore samples from these myconids. If you run out, return the empty jar to me and I will replenish it.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Putrid Fungal Balm]] from Picci Manifold.}}

{{QuestNote|If you run out of balm, return the empty jar to [[Picci Manifold]] for replenishment.}}

{{QuestNote|Use the Putrid Fungal Balm (4/4) on [[a sickly undercap]]. <br>They will attack you. <br>Loot [[Blightspores]]. <br>Return 4 Blightspores to Picci Manifold}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|How curious. The spores are more resilient than I expected. A blight is spreading among the myconids, but it is not our doing. We will need to study this further if we are to shape the undercaps to our purpose. False plagues are not to be tolerated.}}

Picci Manifold frowns.

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|It troubles me, Shaman. But you have taken the first step on the path to becoming a prophet of Bulibyre. You must endure many trials. Take this spear haft, carved from the petrified stalk of a giant toadstool.}}

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Petrified Undercap Stem]] from Picci Manifold.}}

=== Part 3 - Gather the Specimens ===
'''Requires Level 5'''


==== Step 1 - Six Mycelium Roots and Mycelial Staff ====


{{Chat|say|Hail, Picci Manifold}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Your spear is unfinished, fledgling. Will you help me continue my research?}}

{{Chat|say|yes}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|The myconids have a unique connection with the natural flora of the Deep. Like their fungal cousins, they are tethered together. They feel, think, act in unison.}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|The blightspores we have collected only tell us that something is changing, but we need to look deeper. Fill this sack with six mycelium roots from mature undercap specimens. Do this, and I will grant you the mycelial bonding threads you need to fashion your plaguespear.}}

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Mycelium Sack]] from Picci Manifold.}}

{{QuestNote|Gather six [[Undercap Mycelium Root]] and combine them in the Mycelium Sack. Known sources in [[Underdocks]] include level 5+ [[an undercap gatherer]], [[an undercap scavenger]], [[an undercap hunter]], and [[an undercap truffian]].}}

Return to Picci Manifold.

{{Chat|say|Hail, Picci Manifold}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Have you found the mycelium roots I asked for, shaman?}}

{{QuestNote|Give the [[Full Mycelium Sack]] to Picci Manifold.}}

You gain experience!

Your faction with Rot of Gorm got better


{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Magnificent. I can learn much from these. Undercap mycelia have special bonding properties. Take this refined mycelial thread. You will need it to assemble your spear.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive Mycelial Bonding Thread from Picci Manifold}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Wrap the mycelial threads around your shaman's staff. They should form a strong, living bond.}}
{{QuestNote|Right-click the thread, it will transform your [[Petrified Undercap Stem]] into a [[Mycelial Staff]].}}

==== Step 2 - Preserved Specimen and Mycelial Spear ====


{{Chat|say|Hail, Picci Manifold.}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Your spear remains unfinished, (your name). Help me with one more task and I will provide the spearhead you need.}}
{{Chat|say|What task?}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|For all the myconids have in common with ordinary fungi, they are unique. They are individual. I need the preserved brain of an infected myconid. No lesser specimens will suffice. You must find a myconid whose entire being has been consumed by this blight.}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Place the brain in this jar. It must be submerged in embalming fluid.}}
{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Specimen Jar]] from Picci Manifold.}}

{{QuestNote|Take a hunting party out of the North Gate and travel East and find the tunnel that leads to a blight consumed mushroom patch.}}

{{QuestNote|Collect the [[Blightspore Brain]] from a [[mindless blightspore]], semi-rare spawn. This item is NO RENT.}}

{{QuestNote|Purchase [[Embalming Fluid]] from [[Telar Nur'gta]] in the [[Underdocks]].}}

{{QuestNote|Combine the Blightspore Brain and the Embalming Fluid in the Specimen Jar to create the [[Preserved Specimen]].}}

{{QuestNote|Return the Preserved Specimen to Picci Manifold.}}


You gain experience!

Your faction standing with Rot of Gorm got better.


{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Splendid, most splendid. What a peculiar sample it is! I will begin my experiments right away.}}

{{Chat|Picci Manifold|Oh, yes. I almost forgot. You'll be needing this to assemble your spear. This spearhead was carved from the remains of a massive beetle. Go now, (your name). Spread his gifts!}}

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Jagged Chitin Spearhead]] from Picci Manifold.}}

{{QuestNote|Right-click the Jagged Chitin Spearhead to attach the spearhead.}}

{{ReceiveItem|You receive [[Mycelial Spear]].}}

